  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q03', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'Which is recorded as one of the wettest places on Earth?', 'Mawsynram', 'Pune', 'Jaisalmer', 'Leh', 'A', 'Mawsynram in Meghalaya receives the highest average annual rainfall in the world.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q04', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', '''Mango showers'' are pre-monsoon rains associated mainly with which region?', 'Punjab and Haryana', 'Assam', 'Rajasthan', 'Kerala and Karnataka', 'D', 'Pre-monsoon showers in Kerala and coastal Karnataka help ripen mangoes, hence the name.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q05', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'Winter rainfall in north-west India is caused mainly by:', 'Western disturbances', 'Norwesters', 'Retreating monsoon', 'Trade winds', 'A', 'Western disturbances originating in the Mediterranean bring vital winter rain for the rabi crop.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q06', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'The two branches into which the South-West Monsoon splits are the:', 'Coromandel and Malabar branches', 'Arabian Sea and Bay of Bengal branches', 'Himalayan and Peninsular branches', 'Polar and Tropical branches', 'B', 'The monsoon divides into the Arabian Sea branch and the Bay of Bengal branch.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q07', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'The seasonal reversal of winds that defines the monsoon is linked to the migration of the:', 'Inter-Tropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ)', 'Jet stream only', 'Tropic of Cancer', 'Equatorial low alone', 'A', 'The northward shift of the ITCZ in summer pulls moisture-laden winds onto the subcontinent.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q08', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', '''Kal Baisakhi'' or Norwesters are violent thunderstorms that mainly affect:', 'Gujarat', 'Tamil Nadu', 'West Bengal and Assam', 'Kashmir', 'C', 'These pre-monsoon evening storms strike Bengal and Assam, aiding tea and jute cultivation.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q01', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'Which body sets the policy repo rate in India?', 'The Finance Ministry', 'The Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs', 'The NITI Aayog', 'The Monetary Policy Committee', 'D', 'The six-member Monetary Policy Committee fixes the repo rate under the amended RBI Act.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q02', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'India''s flexible inflation target is set at:', '4% ± 2%', '2% ± 2%', '5% ± 1%', '6% ± 2%', 'A', 'The CPI inflation target is 4% with a tolerance band of plus or minus two percentage points.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q03', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Core inflation excludes food and fuel prices.
2. WPI includes the prices of services.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Core inflation strips out volatile food and fuel, while the WPI covers only goods, not services.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q04', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'The repo rate is the rate at which:', 'Banks lend to the public', 'RBI lends to commercial banks', 'RBI borrows from banks', 'Banks lend to one another', 'B', 'Repo is the rate at which the RBI lends short-term funds to commercial banks against securities.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q05', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'A situation of high inflation combined with stagnant growth and high unemployment is called:', 'Deflation', 'Disinflation', 'Reflation', 'Stagflation', 'D', 'Stagflation pairs rising prices with economic stagnation and high joblessness.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q06', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'To control high inflation, the RBI would typically:', 'Reduce the repo rate', 'Conduct OMO purchases', 'Raise the repo rate', 'Lower the CRR', 'C', 'Raising the repo rate makes credit costlier, curbing demand and cooling inflation.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q07', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'The headline Consumer Price Index in India is released by:', 'The NSO under MoSPI', 'The SEBI', 'The Office of the Economic Adviser', 'The Reserve Bank of India', 'A', 'The National Statistical Office under MoSPI compiles and releases the CPI.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q08', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', '''Too much money chasing too few goods'' best describes which type of inflation?', 'Imported inflation', 'Cost-push inflation', 'Structural inflation', 'Demand-pull inflation', 'D', 'Demand-pull inflation arises when aggregate demand outstrips the available supply of goods.', 7),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q01', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'Ayushman Bharat (PM-JAY) provides annual health cover of what amount per family?', '₹2 lakh', '₹3 lakh', '₹5 lakh', '₹10 lakh', 'C', 'PM-JAY gives a health cover of ₹5 lakh per family per year for secondary and tertiary care.', 0),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q02', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The ''JAM'' trinity used for Direct Benefit Transfer stands for:', 'Jan Dhan, Awas, MGNREGA', 'Jobs, Agriculture, Manufacturing', 'Justice, Aadhaar, Money', 'Jan Dhan, Aadhaar, Mobile', 'D', 'JAM links Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar identity and Mobile numbers to deliver subsidies directly.', 1),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q03', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'PM-KISAN provides income support of how much per year to eligible farmer families?', '₹12,000', '₹6,000', '₹8,000', '₹4,000', 'B', 'PM-KISAN transfers ₹6,000 a year in three equal instalments of ₹2,000.', 2),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q04', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The Ujjwala Yojana is associated with the distribution of:', 'Free LPG connections', 'Bank accounts', 'Solar panels', 'Free housing', 'A', 'PM Ujjwala Yojana provides free LPG connections to women from below-poverty-line households.', 3),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q05', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'MGNREGA guarantees how many days of wage employment per rural household per year?', '50 days', '150 days', '100 days', '200 days', 'C', 'The Act guarantees 100 days of unskilled manual wage employment to each rural household.', 4),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q06', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'Consider the following statements:
1. PM Jan Dhan Yojana provides RuPay debit cards.
2. The Saubhagya scheme aims at universal household electrification.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Jan Dhan accounts come with RuPay cards, while Saubhagya targets electricity for all households.', 5),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q07', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The Production-Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme is designed primarily to boost:', 'Agricultural exports', 'Tourism', 'Rural employment', 'Domestic manufacturing', 'D', 'PLI offers incentives on incremental sales to expand domestic manufacturing under Make in India.', 6),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q08', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission is chiefly aimed at achieving:', 'An open-defecation-free India', 'Free education', 'Universal banking', 'Affordable housing', 'A', 'The mission focuses on sanitation and making India open-defecation-free through toilet construction.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q01', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'In which Part of the Constitution are the Directive Principles of State Policy contained?', 'Part IV (Articles 36-51)', 'Part III (Articles 12-35)', 'Part IVA (Article 51A)', 'Part II (Articles 5-11)', 'A', 'DPSP are contained in Part IV, Articles 36-51, and are borrowed from the Irish Constitution.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q02', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution by which amendment?', '86th Amendment, 2002', '42nd Amendment, 1976', '44th Amendment, 1978', '73rd Amendment, 1992', 'B', 'The 42nd Amendment (1976) added Fundamental Duties on the recommendation of the Swaran Singh Committee.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q03', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Consider the following statements about DPSP:
1. They are justiciable and enforceable in courts.
2. They were borrowed from the Irish Constitution.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'DPSP are non-justiciable but fundamental in governance; they were borrowed from the Irish Constitution.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q04', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Which Article of the Constitution provides for a Uniform Civil Code?', 'Article 40', 'Article 44', 'Article 39A', 'Article 50', 'B', 'Article 44 directs the State to secure a Uniform Civil Code; it is a liberal-intellectual directive.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q05', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'The Eleventh Fundamental Duty, added by the 86th Amendment (2002), relates to:', 'Protecting the environment', 'A parent''s duty to provide education to a child aged 6-14', 'Safeguarding public property', 'Promoting scientific temper', 'B', 'The 86th Amendment added the duty of a parent to provide education opportunities to a child aged 6-14.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q06', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Article 50 calls for separation of the judiciary from the executive.
2. Fundamental Duties are enshrined in Part IVA under Article 51A.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'B', 'Article 50 mandates judiciary-executive separation; Fundamental Duties sit in Part IVA, Article 51A.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q07', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Which case held that balance between Fundamental Rights and DPSP is part of the basic structure?', 'Minerva Mills case (1980)', 'Maneka Gandhi case (1978)', 'Golaknath case (1967)', 'Gopalan case (1950)', 'A', 'In Minerva Mills (1980), the Supreme Court held the balance between FRs and DPSP is part of the basic structure.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q08', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Article 39A, providing for free legal aid and equal justice, was added by which amendment?', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '86th Amendment', '1st Amendment', 'A', 'Article 39A on equal justice and free legal aid was inserted by the 42nd Amendment of 1976.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q01', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Under which Article is the Supreme Court of India established?', 'Article 124', 'Article 32', 'Article 137', 'Article 143', 'A', 'Article 124 establishes the Supreme Court of India and provides for its composition.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q02', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'What is the present sanctioned strength of judges in the Supreme Court (including the CJI)?', '34', '26', '30', '31', 'A', 'The sanctioned strength is 34: the Chief Justice of India plus up to 33 other judges.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q03', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Consider the following statements:
1. A Supreme Court judge holds office until 65 years of age.
2. Article 137 empowers the court to review its own judgments.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'A', 'SC judges retire at 65; Article 137 grants the power to review the court''s own judgments.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q04', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'The advisory jurisdiction of the Supreme Court is provided under which Article?', 'Article 131', 'Article 143', 'Article 136', 'Article 132', 'B', 'Article 143 allows the President to seek the advisory opinion of the Supreme Court.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q05', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'The 99th Amendment that created the NJAC was struck down by the Supreme Court in which year?', '2010', '2013', '2018', '2015', 'D', 'The Supreme Court struck down the NJAC (99th Amendment) in 2015, restoring the collegium system.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q06', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Consider the following statements about writ jurisdiction:
1. A High Court issues writs under Article 226.
2. Article 226 is wider than Article 32 as it covers legal rights too.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'High Courts issue writs under Article 226, which is wider than Article 32 since it covers legal rights too.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q07', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Public Interest Litigation (PIL) in India was pioneered chiefly by which judges?', 'H.J. Kania and M. Patanjali Sastri', 'M. Hidayatullah and S.M. Sikri', 'P.N. Bhagwati and V.R. Krishna Iyer', 'A.N. Ray and Y.V. Chandrachud', 'C', 'Justices P.N. Bhagwati and V.R. Krishna Iyer pioneered PIL by relaxing the rule of locus standi.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q08', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'The collegium system for the appointment of judges evolved from which cases?', 'The Second and Third Judges Cases', 'The First and Second Judges Cases', 'The Kesavananda and Minerva cases', 'The Golaknath and Maneka Gandhi cases', 'A', 'The collegium system evolved primarily from the Second (1993) and Third (1998) Judges Cases.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q01', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'Which one of the following is a constitutional body?', 'Election Commission of India', 'National Human Rights Commission', 'NITI Aayog', 'Central Information Commission', 'A', 'The Election Commission is a constitutional body under Article 324; the others are non-constitutional or statutory.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q02', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Comptroller and Auditor General of India is provided for under which Article?', 'Article 280', 'Article 324', 'Article 315', 'Article 148', 'D', 'Article 148 provides for the CAG, the guardian of the public purse who audits government accounts.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q03', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Finance Commission is constituted under Article 280.
2. It is set up every five years to recommend tax devolution.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The Finance Commission, under Article 280, is constituted every five years for Centre-State tax devolution.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q04', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The National Human Rights Commission (NHRC) was established under which law?', 'Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993', 'Lokpal and Lokayuktas Act, 2013', 'RTI Act, 2005', 'Right to Education Act, 2009', 'A', 'The NHRC is a statutory body set up under the Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q05', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The National Commission for Backward Classes became a constitutional body under which Article?', 'Article 280', 'Article 338', 'Article 324', 'Article 338B', 'D', 'The NCBC gained constitutional status under Article 338B via the 102nd Amendment (2018).', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q06', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The UPSC is a constitutional body under Article 315.
2. The Lokpal is a statutory body created in 2013.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'A', 'The UPSC is constitutional under Article 315; the Lokpal is statutory under the 2013 Act.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q07', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Central Information Commission functions under which Act?', 'Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993', 'Right to Information Act, 2005', 'Companies Act, 2013', 'Lokpal and Lokayuktas Act, 2013', 'B', 'The CIC is a statutory body that functions under the Right to Information Act, 2005.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q08', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Attorney General of India is provided for under which Article?', 'Article 315', 'Article 148', 'Article 280', 'Article 76', 'D', 'Article 76 provides for the Attorney General, the highest law officer of the Union.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'Who was the first president of the Indian National Congress?', 'W.C. Bonnerjee', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'A.O. Hume', 'Surendranath Banerjee', 'A', 'W.C. Bonnerjee presided over the first Congress session in 1885; A.O. Hume founded the party.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The ''Drain Theory'' explaining the economic exploitation of India was propounded by:', 'Gopal Krishna Gokhale', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak', 'Bipin Chandra Pal', 'B', 'Dadabhai Naoroji propounded the Drain Theory in his work Poverty and Un-British Rule in India.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Congress split into Moderates and Extremists at the Surat session of 1907.
2. They reunited at the Lucknow session of 1916.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'The Surat Split occurred in 1907 and the two factions reunited at Lucknow in 1916.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'Which trio is collectively known as ''Lal-Bal-Pal''?', 'Lala Hardayal, Tilak, B.G. Pal', 'Lajpat Rai, Bonnerjee, Pherozeshah Mehta', 'Lajpat Rai, Tilak, Bipin Chandra Pal', 'Lajpat Rai, Gokhale, Naoroji', 'C', 'Lal-Bal-Pal were the extremist leaders Lala Lajpat Rai, Bal Gangadhar Tilak and Bipin Chandra Pal.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The slogan ''Swaraj is my birthright and I shall have it'' was given by:', 'Lala Lajpat Rai', 'Bipin Chandra Pal', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak', 'Aurobindo Ghosh', 'C', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak gave the famous slogan asserting Swaraj as a birthright.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Moderates relied on petitions, prayers and protests.
2. The Swadeshi Movement was triggered by the Partition of Bengal in 1905.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Moderates used the 3 Ps; the 1905 Partition of Bengal triggered the Swadeshi Movement.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in which year?', '1857', '1905', '1885', '1916', 'C', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in 1885 by A.O. Hume.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The Lucknow session of 1916 is notable because:', 'It marked the founding of the Congress', 'It launched the Quit India Movement', 'It saw the Lucknow Pact with the Muslim League', 'It abolished the Drain Theory', 'C', 'The 1916 Lucknow session reunited Congress factions and produced the Lucknow Pact with the Muslim League.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'Gandhi''s first Satyagraha in India, in 1917, was launched at:', 'Kheda', 'Ahmedabad', 'Champaran', 'Dandi', 'C', 'The Champaran Satyagraha of 1917 opposed the tinkathia system imposed on indigo cultivators in Bihar.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The Non-Cooperation Movement was withdrawn following which incident?', 'Jallianwala Bagh massacre', 'Chauri Chaura incident', 'Failure of the Cripps Mission', 'Partition of Bengal', 'B', 'Gandhi withdrew the Non-Cooperation Movement in 1922 after the violent Chauri Chaura incident.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Dandi March began on 12 March 1930.
2. The Civil Disobedience Movement broke the salt law.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The Dandi March started on 12 March 1930 and launched Civil Disobedience by breaking the salt law.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The slogan ''Do or Die'' is associated with which movement?', 'Non-Cooperation Movement', 'Quit India Movement', 'Swadeshi Movement', 'Civil Disobedience Movement', 'B', 'Gandhi gave the ''Do or Die'' call during the Quit India Movement of 1942.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The Kheda Satyagraha of 1918 was launched for:', 'Remission of land revenue during crop failure', 'Abolition of the tinkathia system', 'Higher wages for mill workers', 'Repeal of the salt tax', 'A', 'The Kheda Satyagraha in Gujarat demanded remission of land revenue after crop failure.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Quit India Movement was triggered by the failure of the Cripps Mission.
2. The Gandhi-Irwin Pact led to Congress joining the Second Round Table Conference.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Quit India followed the Cripps Mission failure; the 1931 Gandhi-Irwin Pact preceded the Second Round Table Conference.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'In which year did Mahatma Gandhi return to India from South Africa?', '1915', '1909', '1920', '1919', 'A', 'Gandhi returned to India in 1915 and transformed the freedom struggle into a mass movement.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'Gandhi''s first hunger strike in India was undertaken during which event?', 'Champaran Satyagraha', 'Kheda Satyagraha', 'Ahmedabad Mill Strike', 'Dandi March', 'C', 'Gandhi undertook his first hunger strike during the 1918 Ahmedabad Mill Strike.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Brahmo Samaj was founded in 1828 by:', 'Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar', 'Dayananda Saraswati', 'Swami Vivekananda', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy', 'D', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy founded the Brahmo Samaj in 1828 and is called the Father of Indian Renaissance.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The slogan ''Back to the Vedas'' was given by:', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy', 'Jyotiba Phule', 'Dayananda Saraswati', 'Sir Syed Ahmed Khan', 'C', 'Dayananda Saraswati, founder of the Arya Samaj (1875), gave the slogan ''Back to the Vedas''.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Sati was abolished by Lord William Bentinck in 1829.
2. Raja Ram Mohan Roy campaigned against Sati.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Lord William Bentinck abolished Sati in 1829, supported by Raja Ram Mohan Roy''s campaign.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Satyashodhak Samaj (1873) was founded by:', 'Swami Vivekananda', 'Colonel Olcott', 'Dayananda Saraswati', 'Jyotiba Phule', 'D', 'Jyotiba Phule founded the Satyashodhak Samaj in 1873 to fight caste oppression.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'Who championed the cause of widow remarriage, leading to the Act of 1856?', 'Sir Syed Ahmed Khan', 'Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar', 'Swami Vivekananda', 'Madame Blavatsky', 'B', 'Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar championed widow remarriage, which led to the Widow Remarriage Act of 1856.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Ramakrishna Mission was founded by Swami Vivekananda in 1897.
2. The Aligarh Movement was led by Sir Syed Ahmed Khan.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Vivekananda founded the Ramakrishna Mission in 1897; Sir Syed Ahmed Khan led the Aligarh Movement.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Shuddhi movement, aimed at reconversion, was started by which organisation?', 'Theosophical Society', 'Brahmo Samaj', 'Ramakrishna Mission', 'Arya Samaj', 'D', 'The Arya Samaj, founded by Dayananda Saraswati, started the Shuddhi reconversion movement.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Theosophical Society was founded in 1875 by:', 'Annie Besant alone', 'Sir Syed Ahmed Khan', 'Madame Blavatsky and Colonel Olcott', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy', 'C', 'The Theosophical Society was founded in 1875 by Madame Blavatsky and Colonel Olcott.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'Mohenjo-daro is situated on the banks of which river?', 'Indus', 'Ravi', 'Ghaggar', 'Sutlej', 'A', 'Mohenjo-daro, meaning Mound of the Dead, is located on the Indus river and housed the Great Bath.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The site of Lothal is best known for its:', 'Artificial dockyard', 'Citadel', 'Great Bath', 'Pillared hall', 'A', 'Lothal in Gujarat had an artificial dockyard, evidence of Harappan maritime trade.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Harappa was discovered in 1921 by Daya Ram Sahni.
2. Mohenjo-daro was discovered in 1922 by R.D. Banerji.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Harappa was found in 1921 by Daya Ram Sahni and Mohenjo-daro in 1922 by R.D. Banerji.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Harappans traded with Mesopotamia, where their land was referred to as:', 'Meluhha', 'Magan', 'Dilmun', 'Punt', 'A', 'Mesopotamian records refer to the Indus region as Meluhha.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Indus Valley Civilisation belonged to which technological age?', 'Iron Age', 'Bronze Age', 'Stone Age', 'Copper Age only', 'B', 'The IVC was a Bronze Age civilisation flourishing roughly 2600-1900 BCE.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Harappan script is pictographic and remains undeciphered.
2. The Pashupati seal is regarded as a proto-Shiva representation.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The pictographic Harappan script is undeciphered, and the Pashupati seal is seen as proto-Shiva.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'Harappan towns were typically laid out on which pattern?', 'Grid pattern', 'Radial pattern', 'Concentric circles', 'Random clusters', 'A', 'Harappan towns followed a grid pattern with a citadel and a lower town, plus advanced drainage.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'Which deity was widely worshipped in the Indus Valley Civilisation?', 'The Mother Goddess', 'Indra', 'Vishnu', 'Surya', 'A', 'The Harappans worshipped the Mother Goddess and a proto-Shiva Pashupati figure.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Who was the founder of the Mauryan Empire?', 'Chandragupta Maurya', 'Bindusara', 'Ashoka', 'Pushyamitra Shunga', 'A', 'Chandragupta Maurya founded the empire in 322 BCE with the guidance of Chanakya (Kautilya).', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'The Greek envoy who wrote ''Indica'' at the Mauryan court was:', 'Seleucus', 'Fa-Hien', 'Megasthenes', 'Hiuen Tsang', 'C', 'Megasthenes, the Greek envoy of Seleucus, wrote Indica at Chandragupta Maurya''s court.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Kalinga War was fought in 261 BCE.
2. After the war Ashoka propagated his policy of Dhamma.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The Kalinga War of 261 BCE transformed Ashoka, who then propagated Dhamma.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'The Arthashastra, a treatise on statecraft, was authored by:', 'Megasthenes', 'Kautilya (Chanakya)', 'Harisena', 'Varahamihira', 'B', 'Kautilya, also known as Chanakya, authored the Arthashastra on statecraft, economy and espionage.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'The Lion Capital of Sarnath, India''s national emblem, was erected by:', 'Chandragupta Maurya', 'Bindusara', 'Ashoka', 'Samudragupta', 'C', 'Ashoka''s Lion Capital of Sarnath was adopted as India''s national emblem.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Ashoka''s edicts were inscribed in scripts including Brahmi and Kharosthi.
2. The Mauryan dynasty ended with the assassination of Brihadratha by Pushyamitra Shunga.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'A', 'Ashoka''s edicts used Brahmi, Kharosthi, Greek and Aramaic; Pushyamitra Shunga killed Brihadratha in 185 BCE.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Which Mauryan ruler was known by the title ''Amitraghata''?', 'Bindusara', 'Chandragupta Maurya', 'Ashoka', 'Dasharatha', 'A', 'Bindusara, son of Chandragupta, was known as Amitraghata, the slayer of foes.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Mauryan provinces were administered by princes who held which title?', 'Mahamatras', 'Kumaras', 'Amatyas', 'Rajukas', 'B', 'Mauryan provinces were governed by princes known as Kumaras.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Which Gupta ruler is described as the ''Napoleon of India'' by historian V.A. Smith?', 'Chandragupta I', 'Samudragupta', 'Chandragupta II', 'Skandagupta', 'B', 'Samudragupta''s extensive conquests earned him the title ''Napoleon of India'' from V.A. Smith.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The Allahabad Pillar inscription (Prayag Prashasti) was composed by:', 'Kalidasa', 'Harisena', 'Aryabhata', 'Varahamihira', 'B', 'Harisena composed the Allahabad Pillar inscription recording Samudragupta''s conquests.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Aryabhata wrote the Aryabhatiya and proposed Earth''s rotation.
2. Fa-Hien visited India during Chandragupta II''s reign.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Aryabhata wrote the Aryabhatiya; the Chinese pilgrim Fa-Hien visited during Chandragupta II''s reign.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Chandragupta II earned fame by defeating which foreign rulers?', 'The Hunas', 'The Shakas', 'The Kushanas', 'The Greeks', 'B', 'Chandragupta II Vikramaditya defeated the Shakas, extending Gupta power to western India.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Kalidasa, the celebrated Gupta-era poet, authored which work?', 'Aryabhatiya', 'Abhijnanashakuntalam', 'Brihat Samhita', 'Indica', 'B', 'Kalidasa wrote Abhijnanashakuntalam; the Brihat Samhita was by Varahamihira.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Gupta age is called the Golden Age of India.
2. The decline of the Guptas was hastened by Huna invasions under Toramana and Mihirakula.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The Gupta age is the Golden Age; Huna invasions led by Toramana and Mihirakula hastened its decline.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'Who founded the Gupta dynasty and married Kumaradevi of the Licchavis?', 'Samudragupta', 'Sri Gupta', 'Chandragupta II', 'Chandragupta I', 'D', 'Chandragupta I founded the imperial Gupta line and strengthened it by marrying Licchavi princess Kumaradevi.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The Mehrauli Iron Pillar is a notable example of Gupta-era advances in:', 'Metallurgy', 'Painting', 'Astronomy', 'Town planning', 'A', 'The rust-resistant Mehrauli Iron Pillar demonstrates the high metallurgical skill of the Gupta period.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'Gautama Buddha attained enlightenment at which place?', 'Lumbini', 'Bodh Gaya', 'Kushinagar', 'Sarnath', 'B', 'Buddha attained enlightenment at Bodh Gaya; he was born at Lumbini and gave his first sermon at Sarnath.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'Who was the 24th and last Tirthankara of Jainism?', 'Rishabhanatha', 'Parshvanatha', 'Neminatha', 'Mahavira', 'D', 'Mahavira was the 24th Tirthankara; Rishabhanatha was the first and Parshvanatha the 23rd.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Buddha''s first sermon at Sarnath is called Dharmachakra Pravartana.
2. Buddhism follows the Middle Path.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The first sermon at Sarnath is the Dharmachakra Pravartana; Buddhism advocates the Middle Path.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The Fourth Buddhist Council, which split Buddhism into Hinayana and Mahayana, was held under:', 'Kanishka', 'Bindusara', 'Ajatashatru', 'Ashoka', 'A', 'The Fourth Buddhist Council was held under Kanishka and led to the Hinayana-Mahayana split.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The Three Jewels (Triratna) of Jainism are right faith, right knowledge and:', 'Right conduct', 'Right livelihood', 'Right speech', 'Right mindfulness', 'A', 'The Jain Triratna comprises right faith, right knowledge and right conduct.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Third Buddhist Council was held under Ashoka at Pataliputra.
2. Early Buddhist texts (Tripitaka) were written in Pali.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'A', 'The Third Council met under Ashoka at Pataliputra; the Tripitaka was composed in Pali.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The two principal sects of Jainism are:', 'Hinayana and Mahayana', 'Saguna and Nirguna', 'Theravada and Vajrayana', 'Digambara and Svetambara', 'D', 'Jainism''s two principal sects are the Digambara (sky-clad) and Svetambara (white-clad).', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The core ethical principle emphasised by Jainism is:', 'Ahimsa (non-violence)', 'Moksha through ritual', 'Animal sacrifice', 'Idol worship', 'A', 'Ahimsa, or non-violence, is the central ethical principle of Jainism.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Who founded the Slave (Mamluk) dynasty of the Delhi Sultanate in 1206?', 'Iltutmish', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak', 'Balban', 'Jalal-ud-din Khalji', 'B', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak founded the Slave dynasty in 1206 and began the Qutub Minar.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'The only woman to rule the Delhi Sultanate was:', 'Chand Bibi', 'Razia Sultana', 'Nur Jahan', 'Rani Durgavati', 'B', 'Razia Sultana, daughter of Iltutmish, was the only woman to rule the Delhi Sultanate.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Alauddin Khalji introduced market price control reforms.
2. He repelled repeated Mongol invasions.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Alauddin Khalji introduced market control reforms and successfully repelled Mongol invasions.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'The transfer of capital to Daulatabad and the issue of token currency are associated with:', 'Firoz Shah Tughlaq', 'Muhammad bin Tughlaq', 'Ghiyasuddin Tughlaq', 'Bahlol Lodi', 'B', 'Muhammad bin Tughlaq shifted the capital to Daulatabad and introduced token currency.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Under the iqta system of the Delhi Sultanate, an iqta referred to:', 'A unit of currency', 'A military rank', 'An assignment of land revenue in lieu of salary', 'A religious tax', 'C', 'The iqta system assigned land revenue to officials in place of a cash salary.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Qutub Minar was begun by Qutb-ud-din Aibak and completed by Iltutmish.
2. The Delhi Sultanate ended with the First Battle of Panipat in 1526.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Aibak began and Iltutmish completed the Qutub Minar; Babur ended the Sultanate at Panipat in 1526.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Which ruler founded the Lodi dynasty, the last of the Delhi Sultanate?', 'Khizr Khan', 'Ibrahim Lodi', 'Sikandar Lodi', 'Bahlol Lodi', 'D', 'Bahlol Lodi founded the Lodi dynasty in 1451; Ibrahim Lodi was the last Sultan.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Firoz Shah Tughlaq is particularly remembered for:', 'Introducing token currency', 'Levying jizya and building canals', 'Transferring the capital to Daulatabad', 'Defeating Babur at Panipat', 'B', 'Firoz Shah Tughlaq levied the jizya tax and built irrigation canals.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Mughal Empire was founded after the First Battle of Panipat (1526) by:', 'Babur', 'Akbar', 'Sher Shah Suri', 'Humayun', 'A', 'Babur founded the Mughal Empire after defeating Ibrahim Lodi at the First Battle of Panipat in 1526.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'Who introduced the silver coin ''rupiya'' and built the Grand Trunk Road?', 'Aurangzeb', 'Akbar', 'Babur', 'Sher Shah Suri', 'D', 'Sher Shah Suri introduced the rupiya and developed the Grand Trunk Road.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Akbar abolished the jizya tax.
2. Akbar started the Din-i-Ilahi in 1582.
Which is/are correct?', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'B', 'Akbar abolished the jizya and founded the syncretic Din-i-Ilahi in 1582.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Zabti or Dahsala revenue system was developed under Akbar by:', 'Raja Todar Mal', 'Abul Fazl', 'Birbal', 'Man Singh', 'A', 'Raja Todar Mal developed the Zabti (Dahsala) land revenue system under Akbar.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'In the Mansabdari system, the ranks ''zat'' and ''sawar'' indicated respectively:', 'Tax rate and revenue share', 'Personal status and cavalry obligation', 'Religious rank and military rank', 'Land grant and salary', 'B', 'Zat denoted personal status and pay, while sawar indicated the number of cavalry to be maintained.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal.
2. Mughal painting peaked under Jahangir.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'C', 'Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal and Mughal painting reached its zenith under Jahangir.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'Which Mughal emperor re-imposed the jizya and expanded the empire to its greatest extent?', 'Akbar', 'Jahangir', 'Shah Jahan', 'Aurangzeb', 'D', 'Aurangzeb re-imposed the jizya and took the empire to its greatest territorial extent.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'Mughal emperor Humayun is best known for:', 'Building Fatehpur Sikri', 'Starting the Din-i-Ilahi', 'Building the Taj Mahal', 'Losing his throne to Sher Shah Suri', 'D', 'Humayun temporarily lost the throne to Sher Shah Suri before regaining it in 1555.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'Which saint founded Sikhism?', 'Chaitanya', 'Ramananda', 'Kabir', 'Guru Nanak', 'D', 'Guru Nanak founded Sikhism; he was a Nirguna saint who rejected ritualism and caste.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The Bhakti saint Mirabai was devoted to:', 'Vishnu as Vithoba', 'Shiva', 'Rama', 'Krishna', 'D', 'Mirabai of Rajasthan was a devotee of Krishna and a celebrated Bhakti poet.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Kabir and Guru Nanak were Nirguna saints.
2. Saguna saints worshipped a god with form.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Kabir and Guru Nanak belonged to the Nirguna (formless) school; Saguna saints worshipped a god with form.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The Chishti Sufi order in India is most closely associated with which saint of Ajmer?', 'Nizamuddin Auliya', 'Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti', 'Baba Farid', 'Sheikh Bahauddin Zakariya', 'B', 'Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti of Ajmer founded the influential Chishti order in India.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'In Sufi tradition, a ''khanqah'' refers to:', 'A mystical order', 'A devotional song', 'A Sufi hospice', 'A holy relic', 'C', 'A khanqah was a Sufi hospice where the saint lived and disciples gathered.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Sufi orders were organised into silsilas.
2. Sama, or devotional music, was central to the Chishti order.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Sufism was organised into silsilas (orders), and Sama (devotional music) was central to the Chishtis.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The Bhakti saint Chaitanya is chiefly associated with which region?', 'Bengal', 'Awadh', 'Rajasthan', 'Maharashtra', 'A', 'Chaitanya Mahaprabhu spread Krishna devotion in Bengal and Odisha.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The poet and musician closely associated with Nizamuddin Auliya was:', 'Tulsidas', 'Kabir', 'Surdas', 'Amir Khusro', 'D', 'Amir Khusro, a disciple of Nizamuddin Auliya, contributed greatly to a composite Indo-Islamic culture.', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The curvilinear shikhara is the defining feature of which temple style?', 'Nagara', 'Dravida', 'Vesara', 'Kalinga only', 'A', 'The Nagara style of north India is marked by a curvilinear shikhara and lacks boundary walls.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The gopuram, a towering gateway, is a characteristic feature of which style?', 'Nagara', 'Dravida', 'Vesara', 'Bengal terracotta', 'B', 'The Dravida temple of south India is enclosed by walls with a gopuram gateway tower.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Brihadeshwara Temple at Thanjavur was built by the Cholas.
2. The Kandariya Mahadeva at Khajuraho is a Nagara temple.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'The Chola Brihadeshwara Temple is Dravida; Khajuraho''s Kandariya Mahadeva is a Nagara temple.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'In temple architecture, the ''garbhagriha'' is the:', 'Assembly hall', 'Circumambulatory path', 'Sanctum housing the deity', 'Gateway tower', 'C', 'The garbhagriha is the sanctum sanctorum that houses the main deity; the mandapa is the assembly hall.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The monolithic Kailasa Temple at Ellora was carved by which dynasty?', 'Cholas', 'Rashtrakutas', 'Pallavas', 'Hoysalas', 'B', 'The Rashtrakutas carved the monolithic Kailasa Temple at Ellora from top to bottom.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Vesara style is a hybrid associated with the Chalukyas and Hoysalas.
2. The shore temple and rathas at Mahabalipuram were built by the Pallavas.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Vesara is a hybrid style of the Chalukyas and Hoysalas; Mahabalipuram''s monuments are Pallava works.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The Sun Temple at Konark is an example of which architectural style?', 'Nagara', 'Vesara', 'Dravida', 'Indo-Saracenic', 'A', 'The Sun Temple at Konark is a famous Nagara-style temple in Odisha.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The amalaka and kalasha typically crown the tower of which temple style?', 'Cave temples', 'Dravida', 'Vesara', 'Nagara', 'D', 'The amalaka and kalasha crown the shikhara of a Nagara-style temple.', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'How many dance forms are officially recognised as classical in India?', 'Six', 'Seven', 'Nine', 'Eight', 'D', 'India recognises eight classical dance forms, each rooted in Bharata''s Natya Shastra.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Which classical dance form originates from Kerala and uses elaborate make-up and masks?', 'Kuchipudi', 'Kathakali', 'Odissi', 'Manipuri', 'B', 'Kathakali of Kerala uses elaborate make-up and masks to depict episodes from the epics.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Bharatanatyam is the oldest classical dance and originated in temples.
2. Kathak shows strong Persian and Mughal influence.
Which is/are correct?', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'C', 'Bharatanatyam is the oldest temple dance, and Kathak carries strong Persian and Mughal influence.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Sattriya, a classical dance form, originated in which state?', 'Odisha', 'Manipur', 'Assam', 'Tamil Nadu', 'C', 'Sattriya originated in Assam and was founded by the Vaishnavite saint Sankaradeva.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Mohiniyattam, a solo female dance embodying Lasya grace, belongs to:', 'Odisha', 'Andhra Pradesh', 'Kerala', 'Karnataka', 'C', 'Mohiniyattam is a graceful solo female dance form from Kerala embodying the Lasya aspect.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Tandava is the vigorous, masculine aspect of dance.
2. Lasya is the graceful, feminine aspect of dance.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'A', 'Tandava is the vigorous masculine aspect and Lasya the graceful feminine aspect of dance.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'The foundational treatise on Indian performing arts is the:', 'Abhinaya Darpana only', 'Arthashastra', 'Sangeet Ratnakara', 'Natya Shastra', 'D', 'Bharata''s Natya Shastra is the foundational treatise underpinning India''s classical dance forms.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Manipuri dance is best known for its gentle devotional movements linked to:', 'Mughal courts', 'Tandava', 'The devadasi tradition', 'Raslila', 'D', 'Manipuri dance is known for its gentle, devotional movements linked to the Raslila of Krishna.', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The Ajanta cave murals were executed primarily in which technique?', 'Tempera', 'Watercolour wash', 'Oil painting', 'Fresco buono', 'A', 'The Buddhist murals of Ajanta were painted in the tempera technique.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The famous ''Bani Thani'' portrait belongs to which school of painting?', 'Pahari (Kangra)', 'Mughal', 'Deccan', 'Kishangarh', 'D', 'The Bani Thani portrait is the signature work of the Kishangarh school of Rajasthani painting.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Madhubani painting originates from Bihar.
2. Warli painting uses white figures on a mud background.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Madhubani (Mithila) painting is from Bihar; Warli painting uses white figures on a mud background.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Mughal painting reached its zenith under which emperor?', 'Jahangir', 'Akbar', 'Shah Jahan', 'Humayun', 'A', 'Mughal painting, blending Persian technique with Indian themes, peaked under Jahangir.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Pattachitra, a cloth-based scroll painting, is traditionally associated with:', 'Maharashtra', 'Bihar', 'Odisha and Bengal', 'Rajasthan', 'C', 'Pattachitra is a cloth-based scroll painting tradition of Odisha and Bengal.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Bengal School was led by Abanindranath Tagore.
2. It revived Indian themes against Western academic art.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'B', 'Abanindranath Tagore led the Bengal School, which revived Indian themes against Western academic art.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Which of the following is a Pahari school of miniature painting?', 'Kangra', 'Bijapur', 'Bundi', 'Mewar', 'A', 'Kangra and Basohli are Pahari schools; Bundi and Mewar are Rajasthani and Bijapur is Deccan.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The Deccan school of miniature painting flourished at which centres?', 'Kangra and Basohli', 'Mewar and Bundi', 'Mithila and Tanjore', 'Bijapur and Golconda', 'D', 'The Deccan school flourished at Bijapur and Golconda.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q01', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The largest peninsular river of India, called the ''Dakshin Ganga'', is the:', 'Mahanadi', 'Kaveri', 'Krishna', 'Godavari', 'D', 'The Godavari is the largest peninsular river and is known as the Dakshin Ganga.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q02', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'Which two rivers flow westward through rift valleys into the Arabian Sea?', 'Godavari and Krishna', 'Ganga and Yamuna', 'Narmada and Tapi', 'Mahanadi and Kaveri', 'C', 'The Narmada and Tapi flow westward through rift valleys into the Arabian Sea.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q03', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Indus and Brahmaputra are antecedent rivers.
2. They are older than the Himalayas.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The Indus and Brahmaputra are antecedent rivers older than the Himalayas through which they cut.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q04', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The highest peak of peninsular India is:', 'K2 (Godwin Austen)', 'Anamudi', 'Doda Betta', 'Mahendragiri', 'B', 'Anamudi, in the Western Ghats, is the highest peak of peninsular India.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q05', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The three parallel ranges of the Himalayas from north to south are:', 'Himadri, Himachal, Shiwaliks', 'Shiwaliks, Himachal, Himadri', 'Himachal, Himadri, Shiwaliks', 'Himadri, Shiwaliks, Himachal', 'A', 'From north to south the ranges are the Himadri (Greater), Himachal (Lesser) and Shiwaliks (Outer).', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q06', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Peninsular Plateau is the oldest landmass made of Gondwana rocks.
2. The Western Ghats are continuous and higher than the Eastern Ghats.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The Peninsular Plateau is the oldest Gondwana landmass, and the Western Ghats are continuous and higher.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q07', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The highest peak located within India is:', 'Mount Everest', 'Kanchenjunga', 'K2 (Godwin Austen)', 'Nanda Devi', 'C', 'K2, also called Godwin Austen, is the highest peak in India (in the Karakoram range).', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q08', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'Himalayan rivers are generally described as perennial because they are fed by:', 'Only the monsoon', 'Both glaciers and rainfall', 'Only groundwater', 'Only lakes', 'B', 'Himalayan rivers are perennial because they receive water from both melting glaciers and rainfall.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q01', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Black soil (regur) is especially suited to the cultivation of:', 'Tea', 'Coffee', 'Rice', 'Cotton', 'D', 'Black soil, or regur, retains moisture well and is ideal for cotton, hence ''black cotton soil''.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q02', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'In the alluvial soils of India, the older alluvium is known as:', 'Khadar', 'Bhangar', 'Regur', 'Laterite', 'B', 'Bhangar is old alluvium while khadar is the newer, more fertile alluvium.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q03', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Kharif crops are sown in June-July.
2. Rabi crops include wheat and gram.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Kharif crops are sown in June-July; rabi crops such as wheat and gram are sown in winter.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q04', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'The White Revolution in India is associated with:', 'Foodgrains', 'Oilseeds', 'Milk production', 'Fisheries', 'C', 'The White Revolution (Operation Flood) under Verghese Kurien boosted milk production.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q05', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Laterite soil, formed by leaching, is best suited to which crops?', 'Wheat and sugarcane', 'Tea, coffee and cashew', 'Mustard and pulses', 'Cotton and gram', 'B', 'Leached, acidic laterite soil suits plantation crops like tea, coffee and cashew.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q06', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Green Revolution was associated with M.S. Swaminathan and Norman Borlaug.
2. Alluvial soil covers about 40% of India''s land.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Swaminathan and Borlaug led the Green Revolution; alluvial soil covers roughly 40% of India''s land.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q07', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Which cropping season corresponds to the short summer period?', 'Kharif', 'Zaid', 'Rabi', 'Bhangar', 'B', 'The Zaid season is the short summer cropping period for crops like watermelon and cucumber.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q08', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'The Blue Revolution in India refers to development in:', 'Oilseeds', 'Milk', 'Fisheries', 'Foodgrains', 'C', 'The Blue Revolution refers to the development of fisheries and aquaculture.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q01', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The theory of Continental Drift was proposed by:', 'Alfred Wegener', 'Charles Lyell', 'James Hutton', 'Harry Hess', 'A', 'Alfred Wegener proposed the Continental Drift theory, a precursor to plate tectonics.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q02', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'Mid-ocean ridges and rift valleys are typically formed at which plate boundary?', 'Convergent', 'Subduction', 'Transform', 'Divergent', 'D', 'Divergent boundaries, where plates move apart, create mid-ocean ridges and rift valleys.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q03', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Himalayas formed by the convergence of the Indian and Eurasian plates.
2. The Pacific Ring of Fire hosts about two-thirds of the world''s active volcanoes.
Which is/are correct?', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The Himalayas arose from Indian-Eurasian convergence; the Ring of Fire holds about two-thirds of active volcanoes.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q04', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The San Andreas Fault is a classic example of which type of plate boundary?', 'Transform', 'Divergent', 'Convergent', 'Continental', 'A', 'The San Andreas Fault is a transform boundary where plates slide past one another, causing earthquakes.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q05', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The highest plateau in the world is the:', 'Colorado Plateau', 'Deccan Plateau', 'Tibetan Plateau', 'Ethiopian Plateau', 'C', 'The Tibetan Plateau is the highest plateau in the world.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q06', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Block mountains are formed by horst and graben structures.
2. The Himalayas and Andes are examples of fold mountains.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Block mountains arise from horst-and-graben faulting; the Himalayas and Andes are fold mountains.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q07', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'Forces originating from within the Earth that shape landforms are called:', 'Exogenic forces', 'Aeolian forces', 'Gradational forces', 'Endogenic forces', 'D', 'Endogenic (internal) forces such as tectonics build landforms; exogenic forces wear them down.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q08', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The outermost layer of the Earth, broken into tectonic plates, is the:', 'Lithosphere', 'Mantle', 'Outer core', 'Asthenosphere', 'A', 'The lithosphere is the rigid outer layer of the Earth that is broken into tectonic plates.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q01', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Gross Domestic Product (GDP) measures the value of final goods and services produced:', 'Within a country''s borders', 'Only in the manufacturing sector', 'By a country''s nationals worldwide', 'After deducting depreciation', 'A', 'GDP is the value of all final goods and services produced within a country''s borders in a year.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q02', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Gross National Product (GNP) is equal to:', 'GDP plus depreciation', 'GDP minus depreciation', 'GDP plus net factor income from abroad', 'NNP plus taxes', 'C', 'GNP equals GDP plus net factor income from abroad (NFIA).', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q03', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Nominal GDP is calculated at current prices.
2. Real GDP is calculated at constant base-year prices.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Nominal GDP uses current prices, while real GDP uses constant base-year prices.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q04', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'The current base year for India''s GDP estimates is:', '2004-05', '2015-16', '2011-12', '2020-21', 'C', 'India''s GDP series uses 2011-12 as the base year, with figures released by the NSO under MoSPI.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q05', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'The GDP deflator is calculated as:', '(Nominal GDP / Real GDP) x 100', 'Nominal GDP minus Real GDP', '(Real GDP / Nominal GDP) x 100', 'GDP minus depreciation', 'A', 'The GDP deflator equals Nominal GDP divided by Real GDP, multiplied by 100.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q06', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Consider the following statements:
1. NNP at factor cost is termed the National Income.
2. Per capita income equals National Income divided by population.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'NNP at factor cost is the National Income, and per capita income is National Income divided by population.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q07', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Net Domestic Product (NDP) is obtained by:', 'Adding NFIA to GDP', 'Subtracting taxes from GNP', 'Adding depreciation to GDP', 'Subtracting depreciation from GDP', 'D', 'NDP equals GDP minus depreciation.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q08', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'Which of the following is NOT one of the three methods of measuring national income?', 'Production (value-added) method', 'Income method', 'Expenditure method', 'Depreciation method', 'D', 'National income is measured by the production, income and expenditure methods, not a ''depreciation method''.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q01', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'In which year was the Reserve Bank of India nationalised?', '1935', '1947', '1949', '1969', 'C', 'The RBI was established in 1935 and nationalised in 1949.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q02', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The ''repo rate'' is the rate at which:', 'Banks lend to the RBI', 'The RBI lends to commercial banks', 'Banks lend to each other', 'The government borrows from the public', 'B', 'The repo rate is the rate at which the RBI lends short-term funds to commercial banks.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q03', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The RBI is the sole issuer of currency except the one-rupee note and coins.
2. The RBI is the lender of last resort to banks.
Which is/are correct?', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The RBI issues currency except the one-rupee note and coins, and acts as lender of last resort.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q04', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'An asset is classified as a Non-Performing Asset (NPA) if interest or principal is overdue for:', '30 days', '60 days', '180 days', '90 days', 'D', 'A loan becomes an NPA when interest or principal remains overdue for 90 days.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q05', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The one-rupee note and coins in India are issued by:', 'The Ministry of Finance', 'The Reserve Bank of India', 'The State Bank of India', 'NABARD', 'A', 'The one-rupee note and coins are issued by the Ministry of Finance, not the RBI.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q06', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The SLR is capped at 40%.
2. Scheduled commercial banks are listed in the Second Schedule of the RBI Act.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '1 only', 'B', 'SLR is capped at 40% and scheduled commercial banks are listed in the Second Schedule of the RBI Act.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q07', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'Which of the following is true of Payments Banks in India?', 'They cannot lend or issue credit cards', 'They can give long-term loans', 'They can issue credit cards', 'They function only in rural areas', 'A', 'Payments Banks accept small deposits but cannot lend or issue credit cards.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q08', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) was enacted in which year?', '2016', '2013', '2014', '2018', 'A', 'The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code was enacted in 2016 to speed up resolution of bad loans.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q01', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The Union Budget is presented as the ''Annual Financial Statement'' under which Article?', 'Article 280', 'Article 110', 'Article 266', 'Article 112', 'D', 'Article 112 provides for the Annual Financial Statement, that is, the Union Budget.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q02', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The Fiscal Deficit is best defined as:', 'Total Expenditure minus Total Receipts excluding borrowings', 'Revenue Expenditure minus Revenue Receipts', 'Fiscal Deficit minus Interest Payments', 'Capital Receipts minus Capital Expenditure', 'A', 'The Fiscal Deficit equals total expenditure minus total receipts excluding borrowings, indicating borrowing needs.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q03', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Primary Deficit equals the Fiscal Deficit minus interest payments.
2. The FRBM Act was enacted in 2003.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The Primary Deficit is the Fiscal Deficit minus interest payments; the FRBM Act was passed in 2003.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q04', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The Goods and Services Tax (GST) was launched in India on:', '1 July 2017', '26 January 2017', '1 January 2018', '1 April 2016', 'A', 'GST, a destination-based tax, was launched on 1 July 2017 and is governed by the GST Council.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q05', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The GST Council is a constitutional body created under which Article?', 'Article 112', 'Article 279A', 'Article 110', 'Article 266', 'B', 'The GST Council is established under Article 279A of the Constitution.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q06', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Direct taxes are progressive.
2. Indirect taxes such as GST are regressive.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Direct taxes like income tax are progressive, while indirect taxes such as GST are regressive.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q07', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'All revenues received by the Government of India are credited to the:', 'Contingency Fund', 'Public Account', 'Consolidated Fund of India', 'Capital Account', 'C', 'The Consolidated Fund of India (Article 266) holds all government revenues; withdrawals need parliamentary approval.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q08', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'Which of the following is a revenue receipt of the government?', 'Disinvestment proceeds', 'Tax revenue', 'Borrowings', 'Recovery of loans', 'B', 'Tax revenue is a non-debt-creating revenue receipt; borrowings and disinvestment are capital receipts.', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q01', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'How many biodiversity hotspots are located in India?', 'Two', 'Three', 'Four', 'Six', 'C', 'India has four biodiversity hotspots: the Himalayas, Western Ghats, Indo-Burma and Sundaland.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q02', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Conservation of species within their natural habitat is known as:', 'Ex-situ conservation', 'In-situ conservation', 'Cryopreservation', 'Captive breeding', 'B', 'In-situ conservation protects species in their natural habitat, such as national parks and sanctuaries.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q03', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Consider the following statements:
1. National Parks allow no human activity.
2. Wildlife Sanctuaries permit some regulated activity.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'National Parks prohibit human activity while Sanctuaries permit certain regulated activities.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q04', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Project Tiger was launched in which year?', '1972', '1992', '1985', '1973', 'D', 'Project Tiger was launched in 1973; Project Elephant followed in 1992.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q05', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'The Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD) was adopted at which summit?', 'Stockholm Conference 1972', 'Johannesburg Summit 2002', 'Rio Earth Summit 1992', 'Paris Summit 2015', 'C', 'The CBD was adopted at the Rio Earth Summit in 1992.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q06', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Consider the following statements:
1. India is one of 17 megadiverse countries.
2. Biosphere Reserves have core, buffer and transition zones.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'India is among 17 megadiverse nations, and Biosphere Reserves comprise core, buffer and transition zones.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q07', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Protected species in India are listed in the schedules of which Act?', 'Biological Diversity Act, 2002', 'Environment Protection Act, 1986', 'Forest Conservation Act, 1980', 'Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972', 'D', 'The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 lists protected species in its schedules.', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q08', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Which international convention regulates trade in endangered species?', 'CBD', 'CITES', 'Ramsar Convention', 'UNFCCC', 'B', 'CITES regulates international trade in endangered species of wild fauna and flora.', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q01', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Paris Agreement (2015) aims to limit the rise in global average temperature to:', 'Below 3 degrees C', 'Below 4 degrees C', 'Exactly 2.5 degrees C', 'Well below 2 degrees C, pursuing 1.5 degrees C', 'D', 'The Paris Agreement seeks to keep warming well below 2 degrees C while pursuing 1.5 degrees C.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q02', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Montreal Protocol (1987) was aimed at phasing out:', 'Greenhouse gases', 'Ozone-depleting substances', 'Fossil fuel subsidies', 'Plastic waste', 'B', 'The Montreal Protocol phased out ozone-depleting substances; its Kigali Amendment targets HFCs.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q03', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The IPCC was set up in 1988 by WMO and UNEP.
2. The UNFCCC of 1992 is the parent climate treaty.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The IPCC was set up in 1988 by WMO and UNEP, and the 1992 UNFCCC is the parent climate treaty.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q04', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'India has set a target of achieving net zero emissions by:', '2050', '2060', '2047', '2070', 'D', 'India targets net zero emissions by 2070, following the principle of CBDR.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q05', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Kyoto Protocol of 1997 set binding emission targets primarily for:', 'Developing nations', 'Only island nations', 'All UN members equally', 'Developed nations', 'D', 'The Kyoto Protocol set binding greenhouse gas targets for developed nations.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q06', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Methane is mainly emitted by livestock, paddy and landfills.
2. The Paris Agreement operates through Nationally Determined Contributions.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Methane comes from livestock, paddy and landfills; the Paris Agreement works through NDCs.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q07', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'Parties to the UNFCCC meet annually at the:', 'G20 Summit', 'General Assembly', 'Security Council', 'Conference of the Parties (COP)', 'D', 'Parties to the UNFCCC meet annually at the Conference of the Parties (COP).', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q08', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'India''s climate missions are coordinated under which national framework?', 'NAPCC', 'NITI Aayog', 'FRBM', 'NDB', 'A', 'India''s climate missions operate under the National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC).', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q01', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'In an ecosystem, green plants are classified as:', 'Primary consumers', 'Decomposers', 'Producers', 'Secondary consumers', 'C', 'Green plants are autotrophic producers that fix energy at the base of the food chain.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q02', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'According to Lindeman''s 10% law, the energy transferred to the next trophic level is about:', '10%', '1%', '50%', '90%', 'A', 'Lindeman''s 10% law states that only about 10% of energy is transferred to the next trophic level.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q03', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Energy flow in an ecosystem is unidirectional.
2. The pyramid of energy is always upright.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Energy flow is unidirectional and the energy pyramid is always upright.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q04', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Which of the following are decomposers in an ecosystem?', 'Bacteria and fungi', 'Carnivores', 'Herbivores', 'Green plants', 'A', 'Bacteria and fungi act as decomposers, breaking down dead organic matter.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q05', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'An interconnected network of food chains is called a:', 'Ecological niche', 'Trophic level', 'Biome', 'Food web', 'D', 'A food web is an interconnected network of multiple food chains.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q06', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Net Primary Productivity equals GPP minus respiration.
2. NPP is the energy available to consumers.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'NPP equals GPP minus respiration and represents the energy available to consumers.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q07', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Which of the following is an abiotic component of an ecosystem?', 'Herbivores', 'Decomposers', 'Producers', 'Sunlight', 'D', 'Sunlight, water, soil and temperature are abiotic (non-living) components of an ecosystem.', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q08', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Herbivores in a food chain occupy the trophic level of:', 'Producers', 'Primary consumers', 'Secondary consumers', 'Decomposers', 'B', 'Herbivores feed on producers and so occupy the primary consumer trophic level.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Who is regarded as the father of the Indian space programme?', 'A.P.J. Abdul Kalam', 'Vikram Sarabhai', 'Satish Dhawan', 'Homi Bhabha', 'B', 'Vikram Sarabhai, under whom ISRO was founded in 1969, is the father of the Indian space programme.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'India''s first satellite, launched in 1975, was named:', 'Bhaskara', 'Rohini', 'Aryabhata', 'INSAT-1A', 'C', 'Aryabhata, launched in 1975, was India''s first satellite.', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The PSLV is known as the workhorse of ISRO.
2. The GSLV uses an indigenous cryogenic upper stage.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'The PSLV is ISRO''s workhorse, and the GSLV uses an indigenous cryogenic upper stage.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Which Indian mission made India the first nation to reach Mars orbit on its first attempt?', 'Chandrayaan-1', 'Mangalyaan (Mars Orbiter Mission)', 'Aditya-L1', 'Gaganyaan', 'B', 'Mangalyaan (2013) made India the first nation to reach Mars orbit on its first attempt.', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Chandrayaan-3 (2023) is notable for soft-landing near the Moon''s:', 'North pole', 'South pole', 'Equator', 'Far side centre', 'B', 'Chandrayaan-3 soft-landed near the lunar south pole in 2023.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Chandrayaan-1 discovered water molecules on the Moon.
2. NavIC is India''s regional satellite navigation system.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'A', 'Chandrayaan-1 found water molecules on the Moon, and NavIC (IRNSS) is India''s regional navigation system.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'The Aditya-L1 mission is designed to study the:', 'Sun', 'Mars', 'Moon', 'Venus', 'A', 'Aditya-L1 studies the Sun from the L1 Lagrange point.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Gaganyaan is India''s planned mission for:', 'A Mars rover', 'Its first crewed spaceflight', 'A lunar sample return', 'An asteroid mission', 'B', 'Gaganyaan aims to achieve India''s first crewed spaceflight.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Which enzymes are used to cut DNA at specific recognition sites?', 'Polymerases', 'DNA ligases', 'Restriction enzymes', 'Helicases', 'C', 'Restriction enzymes cut DNA at specific sequences, a key tool in genetic engineering.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'The technique used to amplify copies of a DNA segment is:', 'Electrophoresis', 'Chromatography', 'Centrifugation', 'PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction)', 'D', 'PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) amplifies copies of a specific DNA segment.', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Bt cotton is India''s only approved GM crop for commercial cultivation.
2. Golden Rice is engineered to be rich in Vitamin A.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Bt cotton is India''s only approved commercial GM crop, and Golden Rice is engineered for Vitamin A.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Which body in India approves the release of genetically modified organisms?', 'ICMR', 'GEAC', 'DBT', 'CSIR', 'B', 'The Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee (GEAC) under the MoEFCC approves GM organisms.', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'The revolutionary precise gene-editing tool widely used in biotechnology is:', 'PCR', 'Gel electrophoresis', 'CRISPR-Cas9', 'Plasmid cloning', 'C', 'CRISPR-Cas9 is a revolutionary tool for precise gene editing.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Plasmids are used as vectors to carry genes into cells.
2. Bt cotton resists bollworm pests.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'B', 'Plasmids serve as vectors carrying genes into cells, and Bt cotton resists bollworm pests.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'The insertion, deletion or modification of genes using recombinant DNA is called:', 'Tissue culture', 'Hybridisation', 'Fermentation', 'Genetic engineering', 'D', 'Genetic engineering modifies genes using recombinant DNA technology.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Which of the following is commonly produced using biotechnology?', 'Steel', 'Cement', 'Petroleum', 'Insulin', 'D', 'Insulin, vaccines and monoclonal antibodies are produced using biotechnology.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) was established in:', '1947', '1974', '1969', '1958', 'D', 'DRDO was established in 1958 to make India''s armed forces self-reliant in technology.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The Integrated Guided Missile Development Programme (IGMDP) was led by:', 'Homi Bhabha', 'A.P.J. Abdul Kalam', 'Vikram Sarabhai', 'Satish Dhawan', 'B', 'Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam led the IGMDP, earning the title ''Missile Man of India''.', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'Consider the following statements:
1. BrahMos is an India-Russia joint venture cruise missile.
2. Akash is a surface-to-air missile.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'BrahMos is an India-Russia supersonic cruise missile and Akash is a surface-to-air missile.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'Tejas is India''s indigenous:', 'Light Combat Aircraft', 'Main battle tank', 'Nuclear submarine', 'Aircraft carrier', 'A', 'Tejas is India''s indigenous Light Combat Aircraft (LCA).', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'INS Arihant is significant as India''s:', 'First aircraft carrier', 'Largest destroyer', 'First frigate', 'First nuclear-powered submarine', 'D', 'INS Arihant is India''s first indigenous nuclear-powered ballistic missile submarine, completing the nuclear triad.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'Consider the following statements:
1. India follows a No First Use nuclear doctrine.
2. INS Vikrant is India''s first indigenous aircraft carrier.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'C', 'India follows a No First Use doctrine, and INS Vikrant is its first indigenous aircraft carrier.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The Agni series of missiles are classified as:', 'Surface-to-air missiles', 'Anti-tank missiles', 'Cruise missiles', 'Surface-to-surface ballistic missiles', 'D', 'Agni missiles are surface-to-surface ballistic missiles.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The Nag missile developed by DRDO is a:', 'Surface-to-air missile', 'Anti-tank guided missile', 'Intercontinental ballistic missile', 'Cruise missile', 'B', 'The Nag is an anti-tank guided missile developed under the IGMDP.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'With which country does India share its longest land border?', 'Bangladesh', 'Pakistan', 'Nepal', 'China', 'A', 'India shares its longest land border with Bangladesh.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The boundary line between India and China in the eastern sector is the:', 'Radcliffe Line', 'Line of Control', 'Durand Line', 'McMahon Line', 'D', 'The McMahon Line demarcates the India-China boundary in the eastern sector.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Chabahar Port is located in Iran.
2. It helps India reach Afghanistan and Central Asia bypassing Pakistan.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The Chabahar Port in Iran lets India reach Afghanistan and Central Asia while bypassing Pakistan.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The ''SAGAR'' doctrine relates to India''s policy in which domain?', 'Cyber security', 'Space cooperation', 'Maritime security and growth', 'Trade tariffs', 'C', 'SAGAR (Security and Growth for All in the Region) guides India''s maritime policy in the Indian Ocean.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The Kalapani territorial dispute is between India and:', 'China', 'Bhutan', 'Myanmar', 'Nepal', 'D', 'The Kalapani dispute is a boundary issue between India and Nepal.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Land Boundary Agreement with Bangladesh was implemented in 2015.
2. India and China are separated by the Line of Actual Control.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The India-Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement took effect in 2015; India and China are divided by the LAC.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The Gujral Doctrine emphasised:', 'Non-reciprocal accommodation of smaller neighbours', 'Strict reciprocity with all neighbours', 'Military alliances in South Asia', 'Economic sanctions on rivals', 'A', 'The Gujral Doctrine emphasised non-reciprocal accommodation of India''s smaller neighbours.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'India''s broad approach toward its immediate neighbours is captured by which policy?', 'Look East Policy', 'Indo-Pacific Strategy', 'Neighbourhood First Policy', 'Connect Central Asia Policy', 'C', 'India''s approach to its immediate neighbours is guided by the ''Neighbourhood First'' policy.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'Which countries make up the QUAD grouping?', 'India, US, UK, France', 'India, China, Russia, Brazil', 'India, Japan, Israel, UAE', 'India, US, Japan, Australia', 'D', 'The QUAD comprises India, the United States, Japan and Australia.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'The New Development Bank (NDB) of BRICS is headquartered in:', 'Moscow', 'New Delhi', 'Shanghai', 'Johannesburg', 'C', 'The BRICS New Development Bank is headquartered in Shanghai.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'Consider the following statements:
1. SAARC was established in 1985 with its secretariat at Kathmandu.
2. ASEAN is central to India''s Act East policy.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'SAARC was set up in 1985 with its secretariat in Kathmandu; ASEAN anchors India''s Act East policy.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'The I2U2 grouping comprises India, Israel, the USA and:', 'Saudi Arabia', 'Qatar', 'The United Arab Emirates', 'Egypt', 'C', 'I2U2 groups India, Israel, the United Arab Emirates and the United States.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'India hosted the G20 summit in which year?', '2021', '2024', '2022', '2023', 'D', 'India hosted the G20 summit in 2023.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'Consider the following statements:
1. India is a member of the MTCR.
2. India is a member of the Nuclear Suppliers Group (NSG).
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'India is a member of the MTCR but is not yet a member of the Nuclear Suppliers Group.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'The grouping linking the countries around the Bay of Bengal is:', 'SAARC', 'BIMSTEC', 'ASEAN', 'SCO', 'B', 'BIMSTEC links South Asian and Southeast Asian nations around the Bay of Bengal.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'Consider the following statements about India''s global standing:
1. India is a founding member of the United Nations (1945).
2. India is a permanent member of the UN Security Council.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'India is a founding UN member of 1945 but is not a permanent member of the Security Council.', 7),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q01', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The Human Development Index (HDI) is published by which organisation?', 'UNDP', 'IMF', 'WEF', 'World Bank', 'A', 'The HDI is published annually by the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP).', 0),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q02', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The Global Innovation Index is released by:', 'UNESCO', 'WTO', 'WIPO', 'WHO', 'C', 'The Global Innovation Index is released by the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO).', 1),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q03', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'Consider the following statements:
1. NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015.
2. The HDI combines life expectancy, education and per capita income.
Which is/are correct?', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015; the HDI combines longevity, education and income.', 2),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q04', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The ''World Economic Outlook'' is published by which institution?', 'IMF', 'OECD', 'WEF', 'World Bank', 'A', 'The International Monetary Fund (IMF) publishes the World Economic Outlook.', 3),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q05', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The Global Gender Gap Report is released by the:', 'World Bank', 'World Economic Forum', 'UNDP', 'WHO', 'B', 'The World Economic Forum (WEF) releases the Global Gender Gap Report.', 4),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q06', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Multidimensional Poverty Index is published jointly by UNDP and OPHI.
2. The Environmental Performance Index is released by Yale and Columbia universities.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The MPI is published by UNDP and OPHI; the EPI is released by Yale and Columbia universities.', 5),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q07', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The World Development Report is published by:', 'The IMF', 'The UNDP', 'The World Bank', 'The WTO', 'C', 'The World Bank publishes the World Development Report.', 6),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q08', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The World Happiness Report is published under the auspices of the:', 'WHO', 'Sustainable Development Solutions Network (SDSN)', 'World Bank', 'OECD', 'B', 'The World Happiness Report is released by the UN''s Sustainable Development Solutions Network (SDSN).', 7),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q01', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Anti-defection disqualifications are decided by whom under the Tenth Schedule?', 'The President', 'The Supreme Court', 'The Presiding Officer of the House', 'The Election Commission', 'C', 'Under the Tenth Schedule, the Presiding Officer of the House decides anti-defection disqualifications.', 0),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q02', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) was established in:', '1988', '1991', '1992', '2000', 'C', 'SEBI was given statutory status in 1992 to regulate securities markets and protect investors.', 1),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q03', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The classification of a Money Bill is certified by the Speaker.
2. The Speaker''s decision on a Money Bill is final.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The Speaker certifies a bill as a Money Bill under Article 110, and that decision is final.', 2),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q04', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'A Governor''s options on a bill under Article 200 include assent, withholding assent and:', 'Dissolving the assembly', 'Reserving it for the President', 'Amending it directly', 'Issuing an ordinance', 'B', 'Under Article 200 a Governor may assent, withhold assent, or reserve a bill for the President''s consideration.', 3),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q05', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Disinvestment of public sector undertakings is managed by which body?', 'RBI', 'DIPAM', 'SEBI', 'NITI Aayog', 'B', 'Disinvestment is managed by DIPAM (Department of Investment and Public Asset Management).', 4),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q06', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Election Commission conducts elections under Article 324.
2. The CAG audits and reports to Parliament under Article 148.
Which is/are correct?', 'Neither 1 nor 2', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '1 only', 'C', 'The Election Commission acts under Article 324 and the CAG audits and reports under Article 148.', 5),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q07', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Inflation targeting in India is carried out by which body?', 'The Finance Commission', 'The GST Council', 'The Monetary Policy Committee of the RBI', 'SEBI', 'C', 'Inflation targeting is handled by the RBI''s Monetary Policy Committee (MPC).', 6),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q08', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'Fiscal transfers between the Centre and the States are recommended by the:', 'Finance Commission', 'GST Council', 'NITI Aayog', 'RBI', 'A', 'The Finance Commission recommends fiscal transfers and tax devolution between the Centre and the States.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q01', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'Under which Article is the President of India the head of the Union executive?', 'Article 74', 'Article 53', 'Article 52', 'Article 75', 'C', 'Article 52 provides that there shall be a President of India, the head of the Union executive.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q02', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The President is elected by an electoral college through proportional representation.
2. The election uses the single transferable vote system.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Article 55 prescribes proportional representation by single transferable vote for the presidential election.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q03', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The total number of ministers in the Council cannot exceed what percentage of the Lok Sabha strength?', 'Ten per cent', 'Twelve per cent', 'Twenty per cent', 'Fifteen per cent', 'D', 'The 91st Amendment (2003) caps the Council of Ministers at 15 per cent of the Lok Sabha''s total strength.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q04', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The power of the President to grant pardons is contained in which Article?', 'Article 76', 'Article 72', 'Article 123', 'Article 61', 'B', 'Article 72 empowers the President to grant pardons, reprieves, respites and remissions of punishment.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q05', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to which House?', 'The Rajya Sabha', 'The President', 'Both Houses jointly', 'The Lok Sabha', 'D', 'Article 75(3) makes the Council of Ministers collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q06', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'A person who is not a member of either House can remain a minister for a maximum of how long?', 'Three months', 'One year', 'Six months', 'Twelve months', 'C', 'Such a minister must become a member of either House within six months, failing which the post is vacated.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q07', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'Under which Article does the President promulgate ordinances?', 'Article 123', 'Article 74', 'Article 72', 'Article 356', 'A', 'Article 123 empowers the President to promulgate ordinances when Parliament is not in session.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q08', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The President normally acts on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers.
2. The President may return such advice once for reconsideration.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Article 74, as amended by the 44th Amendment, lets the President return advice once but then must accept it.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q01', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'The division of legislative powers between the Centre and States is contained in which Schedule?', 'Seventh Schedule', 'Sixth Schedule', 'Fifth Schedule', 'Tenth Schedule', 'A', 'The Seventh Schedule contains the Union, State and Concurrent Lists distributing legislative powers.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q02', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'In whom do the residuary powers of legislation vest?', 'The State Legislatures', 'The Union Parliament', 'The President', 'The Inter-State Council', 'B', 'Article 248 vests residuary powers of legislation in the Union Parliament.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q03', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Police and public order are subjects in the State List.
2. Education is a subject in the Concurrent List.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Police and public order fall in the State List, while education is on the Concurrent List after the 42nd Amendment.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q04', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'Which commission was set up in 1983 to examine Centre-State relations?', 'The Punchhi Commission', 'The Rajamannar Committee', 'The Sarkaria Commission', 'The Mandal Commission', 'C', 'The Sarkaria Commission (1983) was appointed to review Centre-State relations; the Punchhi Commission came in 2007.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q05', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'Parliament can legislate on a State subject in the national interest if the Rajya Sabha passes a resolution under which Article?', 'Article 280', 'Article 256', 'Article 262', 'Article 249', 'D', 'Article 249 lets Parliament legislate on a State subject if the Rajya Sabha resolves so in the national interest.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q06', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'Which body is described by some scholars as an example of cooperative federalism in India?', 'The Supreme Court', 'The Election Commission', 'The GST Council', 'The Comptroller and Auditor General', 'C', 'The GST Council, with Centre and States deciding tax rates jointly, exemplifies cooperative federalism.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q07', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'The Inter-State Council can be established by the President under which Article?', 'Article 131', 'Article 324', 'Article 280', 'Article 263', 'D', 'Article 263 empowers the President to establish an Inter-State Council to coordinate between states and the Centre.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q08', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'When a Union law and a State law on a Concurrent subject conflict, which prevails?', 'The State law', 'Neither, both are void', 'The earlier law', 'The Union law', 'D', 'Under Article 254, the Union law generally prevails over a conflicting State law on a Concurrent List subject.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q01', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Which Constitutional Amendment gave panchayats constitutional status?', '74th Amendment', '73rd Amendment', '65th Amendment', '44th Amendment', 'B', 'The 73rd Amendment (1992) added Part IX, giving panchayati raj institutions constitutional status.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q02', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'The three-tier system of panchayati raj is mandatory for states with a population above:', 'Ten lakh', 'Twenty lakh', 'Fifteen lakh', 'Fifty lakh', 'B', 'States with a population above twenty lakh must constitute the three-tier panchayati raj system.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q03', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Eleventh Schedule lists subjects for panchayats.
2. The Twelfth Schedule lists subjects for municipalities.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The Eleventh Schedule has 29 subjects for panchayats; the Twelfth Schedule has 18 for municipalities.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q04', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Which committee first recommended the three-tier panchayati raj system?', 'The Balwant Rai Mehta Committee', 'The Ashok Mehta Committee', 'The L.M. Singhvi Committee', 'The G.V.K. Rao Committee', 'A', 'The Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957) recommended the three-tier structure of panchayati raj.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q05', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'The conduct of elections to panchayats is vested in the:', 'Election Commission of India', 'District Collector', 'State Finance Commission', 'State Election Commission', 'D', 'Article 243K vests superintendence of panchayat elections in the State Election Commission.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q06', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'What is the fixed term of a panchayat under Article 243E?', 'Four years', 'Six years', 'Five years', 'Three years', 'C', 'Article 243E fixes a five-year term for every panchayat from the date of its first meeting.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q07', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'The PESA Act, 1996 extends panchayat provisions to which areas?', 'Urban municipal areas', 'Sixth Schedule areas', 'Union Territories', 'Fifth Schedule (tribal) areas', 'D', 'The PESA Act, 1996 extends Part IX provisions to the Scheduled (Fifth Schedule) tribal areas.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q08', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'The financial position of panchayats is reviewed every five years by the:', 'Union Finance Commission', 'NITI Aayog', 'Comptroller and Auditor General', 'State Finance Commission', 'D', 'Article 243I provides for a State Finance Commission to review panchayat finances every five years.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q01', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'A National Emergency is proclaimed under which Article?', 'Article 368', 'Article 356', 'Article 360', 'Article 352', 'D', 'Article 352 allows a National Emergency on grounds of war, external aggression or armed rebellion.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q02', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'President''s Rule in a State is imposed under which Article?', 'Article 352', 'Article 360', 'Article 356', 'Article 365', 'C', 'Article 356 provides for President''s Rule when the constitutional machinery in a State fails.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q03', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The 44th Amendment replaced ''internal disturbance'' with ''armed rebellion''.
2. A National Emergency must be approved by Parliament within one month.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The 44th Amendment substituted ''armed rebellion'' and required parliamentary approval within one month.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q04', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'Which case made the imposition of President''s Rule subject to judicial review?', 'S.R. Bommai case', 'Minerva Mills case', 'Kesavananda Bharati case', 'Maneka Gandhi case', 'A', 'The S.R. Bommai (1994) case held that President''s Rule under Article 356 is subject to judicial review.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q05', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'The procedure for amending the Constitution is laid down in which Article?', 'Article 360', 'Article 352', 'Article 370', 'Article 368', 'D', 'Article 368 lays down the procedure for amending the Constitution.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q06', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'Which amendment is popularly called the ''Mini-Constitution''?', '73rd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '1st Amendment', '42nd Amendment', 'D', 'The 42nd Amendment (1976) made sweeping changes and is known as the ''Mini-Constitution''.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q07', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'The doctrine that Parliament cannot alter the ''basic structure'' was laid down in which case?', 'Kesavananda Bharati case', 'Golaknath case', 'Shankari Prasad case', 'Indira Sawhney case', 'A', 'The Kesavananda Bharati (1973) case established the basic structure doctrine limiting Article 368.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q08', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'A Financial Emergency can be proclaimed under which Article?', 'Article 352', 'Article 356', 'Article 360', 'Article 365', 'C', 'Article 360 provides for a Financial Emergency on a threat to the financial stability or credit of India.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q01', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'GST in India was introduced by which Constitutional Amendment?', '103rd Amendment', '100th Amendment', '102nd Amendment', '101st Amendment', 'D', 'The 101st Amendment Act, 2016 introduced the Goods and Services Tax, effective from 1 July 2017.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q02', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'The GST Council is established under which Article?', 'Article 246A', 'Article 280', 'Article 279A', 'Article 110', 'C', 'Article 279A provides for the constitution of the GST Council, chaired by the Union Finance Minister.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q03', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Income tax is a direct tax.
2. GST is an indirect tax.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Income tax is a direct tax borne by the payer, while GST is an indirect tax that can be passed on.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q04', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'GST levied on inter-state supply of goods is known as:', 'IGST', 'SGST', 'CGST', 'UTGST', 'A', 'Integrated GST (IGST) is levied by the Centre on inter-state supplies of goods and services.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q05', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'Which of the following is currently outside the ambit of GST?', 'Restaurant services', 'Electronics', 'Textiles', 'Petroleum products', 'D', 'Petroleum products, alcohol for human consumption and electricity remain outside GST at present.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q06', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'GST is best described as which kind of tax?', 'Origin-based tax', 'A wealth tax', 'A direct tax', 'Destination-based tax', 'D', 'GST is a destination-based, value-added tax collected at the point of consumption.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q07', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'The Laffer Curve illustrates the relationship between:', 'Inflation and unemployment', 'Tax rates and tax revenue', 'Savings and investment', 'Demand and supply', 'B', 'The Laffer Curve shows that beyond a point, higher tax rates can reduce total tax revenue.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q08', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'Tax buoyancy refers to the responsiveness of tax revenue to changes in:', 'GDP / national income', 'The repo rate', 'The exchange rate', 'The fiscal deficit', 'A', 'Tax buoyancy measures how tax revenue responds to growth in GDP or national income.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q01', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Which type of unemployment is most associated with Indian agriculture?', 'Frictional unemployment', 'Cyclical unemployment', 'Voluntary unemployment', 'Disguised unemployment', 'D', 'Disguised unemployment, where surplus workers add little output, is common in Indian agriculture.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q02', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Tendulkar Committee estimated poverty based on consumption expenditure.
2. The Rangarajan Committee later reviewed poverty estimation.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Both the Tendulkar (2009) and Rangarajan (2014) committees estimated poverty using consumption expenditure.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q03', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'The Gini coefficient is a measure of:', 'Inflation', 'Economic growth', 'Income inequality', 'Tax efficiency', 'C', 'The Gini coefficient measures income inequality, ranging from 0 (perfect equality) to 1 (perfect inequality).', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q04', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Which survey is the primary official source of employment data in India?', 'National Family Health Survey', 'National Sample Survey on Consumption', 'Census of India', 'Periodic Labour Force Survey', 'D', 'The Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) by the NSO is the main source of employment and unemployment data.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q05', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Unemployment arising from a mismatch between workers'' skills and job requirements is called:', 'Structural unemployment', 'Cyclical unemployment', 'Frictional unemployment', 'Seasonal unemployment', 'A', 'Structural unemployment results from a mismatch between available skills and the demands of the economy.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q06', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'The Multidimensional Poverty Index in India is released by:', 'The RBI', 'NITI Aayog', 'SEBI', 'The Finance Commission', 'B', 'NITI Aayog releases the national Multidimensional Poverty Index covering health, education and living standards.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q07', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'The Lorenz Curve is used to depict:', 'The business cycle', 'Marginal utility', 'The distribution of income', 'Price elasticity', 'C', 'The Lorenz Curve graphically represents the distribution of income or wealth in an economy.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q08', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Which programme guarantees 100 days of wage employment to rural households?', 'PM-KISAN', 'PM Awas Yojana', 'PMKVY', 'MGNREGA', 'D', 'MGNREGA guarantees 100 days of wage employment per year to every rural household demanding work.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q01', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'The current account of the Balance of Payments includes:', 'Trade in goods, services and remittances', 'Foreign direct investment', 'External commercial borrowings', 'Portfolio investment', 'A', 'The current account records trade in goods and services, income and current transfers like remittances.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q02', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'Consider the following statements:
1. FDI is generally long-term and involves management control.
2. FPI is short-term portfolio investment often called ''hot money''.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'FDI is durable and management-linked, while FPI is volatile portfolio flow termed ''hot money''.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q03', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'Depreciation of the rupee generally makes:', 'Exports costlier and imports cheaper', 'No change in trade flows', 'Both exports and imports cheaper', 'Exports cheaper and imports costlier', 'D', 'A weaker rupee makes Indian exports cheaper abroad and imports more expensive at home.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q04', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'India''s exchange rate system is best described as:', 'Fixed peg', 'Free float', 'Managed float', 'Currency board', 'C', 'India follows a managed floating exchange rate, with the RBI intervening to limit volatility.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q05', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'A Current Account Deficit arises when:', 'Exports exceed imports of goods and services', 'Forex reserves rise', 'Capital inflows exceed outflows', 'Imports of goods and services exceed exports plus net transfers', 'D', 'A CAD occurs when a country''s imports of goods and services exceed exports and net current transfers.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q06', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'Which body administers India''s Foreign Trade Policy?', 'The RBI', 'The Directorate General of Foreign Trade', 'SEBI', 'The Finance Commission', 'B', 'The Directorate General of Foreign Trade (DGFT) administers India''s Foreign Trade Policy.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q07', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'Which of the following is classified as an ''invisible'' in the Balance of Payments?', 'Software services and remittances', 'Import of crude oil', 'Export of machinery', 'Import of gold', 'A', 'Services and remittances are ''invisibles'', as against visible merchandise trade in goods.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q08', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'The global body that frames the rules of international trade is the:', 'IMF', 'WTO', 'World Bank', 'UNCTAD', 'B', 'The World Trade Organization (WTO), established in 1995, frames and enforces global trade rules.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q01', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The Minimum Support Price (MSP) is recommended by which body?', 'The Food Corporation of India', 'The Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices', 'NABARD', 'The NITI Aayog', 'B', 'The Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices (CACP) recommends the MSP to the government.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q02', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The National Food Security Act was enacted in 2013.
2. It gives a legal right to subsidised foodgrains.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'The National Food Security Act, 2013 gives a legal entitlement to subsidised foodgrains via the PDS.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q03', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'Procurement of foodgrains for the central pool is handled mainly by the:', 'Food Corporation of India', 'NABARD', 'RBI', 'CACP', 'A', 'The Food Corporation of India (FCI) is the principal agency for procurement and buffer stocking.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q04', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The apex institution for agricultural and rural credit in India is:', 'NABARD', 'SIDBI', 'The RBI', 'EXIM Bank', 'A', 'NABARD is the apex development bank for agriculture and rural credit in India.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q05', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The ''One Nation One Ration Card'' scheme primarily enables:', 'Crop insurance', 'Portability of PDS benefits across states', 'Free electricity to farmers', 'Direct cash transfer of MSP', 'B', 'One Nation One Ration Card allows beneficiaries to access PDS rations anywhere in the country.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q06', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'MSP has been declared as a benchmark of how many times the A2+FL cost?', '1.2 times', '1 time', '2 times', '1.5 times', 'D', 'The government announced MSP at a level of at least 1.5 times the A2+FL cost of production.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q07', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'e-NAM is best described as:', 'A unified national online agricultural market', 'A crop insurance scheme', 'A fertiliser subsidy portal', 'A soil health card scheme', 'A', 'e-NAM is the electronic National Agriculture Market, a unified online trading platform for farm produce.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q08', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The Green Revolution in India is most associated with which crops?', 'Pulses and oilseeds', 'Cotton and jute', 'Wheat and rice', 'Tea and coffee', 'C', 'The Green Revolution sharply raised the output of wheat and rice through high-yielding varieties.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'How many permanent members does the UN Security Council have?', 'Seven', 'Ten', 'Fifteen', 'Five', 'D', 'The UNSC has five permanent members (USA, UK, France, Russia, China) with veto power.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'Where is the International Court of Justice located?', 'New York', 'The Hague', 'Geneva', 'Vienna', 'B', 'The International Court of Justice, the principal judicial organ of the UN, sits at The Hague.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The IMF and the World Bank are Bretton Woods institutions.
2. Both are headquartered in Washington DC.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'The IMF and World Bank emerged from the 1944 Bretton Woods Conference and are based in Washington DC.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'Special Drawing Rights (SDRs) are issued by which institution?', 'The World Bank', 'The WTO', 'The IMF', 'The Asian Development Bank', 'C', 'Special Drawing Rights are an international reserve asset created and allocated by the IMF.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) is headquartered in:', 'Geneva', 'Vienna', 'Paris', 'New York', 'B', 'The IAEA, which promotes peaceful use of nuclear energy, is headquartered in Vienna.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'Which is the only tripartite agency of the United Nations?', 'The WHO', 'The ILO', 'UNESCO', 'UNICEF', 'B', 'The International Labour Organization (ILO) is unique in bringing together governments, employers and workers.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The WTO, governing global trade rules, came into existence in which year?', '1945', '1995', '1948', '2001', 'B', 'The World Trade Organization was established in 1995, succeeding the GATT.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The G4 group, which seeks permanent UNSC seats, consists of India, Germany, Japan and:', 'Australia', 'South Africa', 'Italy', 'Brazil', 'D', 'The G4 nations seeking permanent UN Security Council seats are India, Germany, Japan and Brazil.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'The Panchsheel principles were enunciated in which year?', '1947', '1950', '1962', '1954', 'D', 'The Panchsheel, the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence, were articulated in 1954.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'SAGAR, a maritime vision, stands for:', 'Security and Growth for All in the Region', 'Strategic Action for Global Asian Regions', 'South Asian Group for African Relations', 'Safe Anchorage and Gulf Access Route', 'A', 'SAGAR stands for ''Security and Growth for All in the Region'', India''s maritime cooperation vision.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'Consider the following statements:
1. India has the largest overseas diaspora in the world.
2. India is among the top recipients of remittances.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'India has the world''s largest diaspora and is the leading recipient of remittances globally.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'Pravasi Bharatiya Divas is observed on which date?', '9 January', '26 January', '15 August', '2 October', 'A', 'Pravasi Bharatiya Divas is observed on 9 January, marking Gandhi''s return from South Africa in 1915.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'India''s ''Act East'' policy is chiefly directed toward:', 'ASEAN and East Asia', 'Africa', 'The Gulf countries', 'Latin America', 'A', 'The Act East policy strengthens India''s economic and strategic ties with ASEAN and East Asia.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'Which leader is most closely associated with shaping the Non-Aligned Movement for India?', 'Sardar Patel', 'Lal Bahadur Shastri', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'B.R. Ambedkar', 'C', 'Jawaharlal Nehru was a principal architect of India''s non-alignment and the Non-Aligned Movement.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'An Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) cardholder is generally:', 'A foreign citizen of Indian origin with visa-free entry', 'An Indian citizen by birth', 'Allowed to vote in Indian elections', 'Eligible to hold constitutional office', 'A', 'An OCI is a foreign citizen of Indian origin given lifelong visa-free entry but no voting rights.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'Indian diplomacy and foreign relations are primarily conducted by which ministry?', 'Ministry of Home Affairs', 'Ministry of External Affairs', 'Ministry of Defence', 'Ministry of Commerce', 'B', 'The Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) conducts India''s diplomacy and foreign relations.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q01', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Ethics is best defined as:', 'A set of legal rules', 'The systematic study of morality', 'Individual personal preferences', 'Religious commandments only', 'B', 'Ethics is the systematic, reflective study of morality and standards of right and wrong conduct.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q02', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Deontology judges an act by its consequences.
2. Consequentialism judges an act by its outcomes.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Deontology judges acts by adherence to duty, while consequentialism judges them by their outcomes.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q03', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'The branch of ethics that analyses the meaning of moral terms is called:', 'Meta-ethics', 'Normative ethics', 'Descriptive ethics', 'Applied ethics', 'A', 'Meta-ethics examines the nature and meaning of moral concepts such as ''good'' and ''right''.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q04', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Which is often described as the inner moral guide or ''court of last appeal''?', 'Law', 'Conscience', 'Custom', 'Public opinion', 'B', 'Conscience is regarded as the inner moral compass, the final internal arbiter of right and wrong.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q05', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Morals differ from ethics in that morals are:', 'The systematic study of conduct', 'Identical to legal rules', 'Always codified in law', 'Personal beliefs of right and wrong', 'D', 'Morals are an individual''s personal convictions, whereas ethics is the reasoned study of those convictions.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q06', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Normative ethics is primarily concerned with:', 'What people ought to do', 'What people actually do', 'The meaning of moral language', 'Statistical study of behaviour', 'A', 'Normative ethics prescribes the standards of how people ought to act.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q07', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Public conduct demands higher accountability than private conduct.
2. Conscience is regarded as a source of ethics.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Public actions affect many and demand higher accountability, and conscience is a recognised source of ethics.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q08', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Which of the following is NOT generally considered a source of ethics?', 'Religion', 'Random chance', 'The Constitution', 'Society and family', 'B', 'Family, religion, society and the constitution shape ethics; random chance is not a source of moral values.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q01', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'The three components of attitude in the ABC model are affective, behavioural and:', 'Contextual', 'Compulsive', 'Cognitive', 'Cultural', 'C', 'The ABC model of attitude comprises affective (feelings), behavioural and cognitive (beliefs) components.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q02', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'The concept of Emotional Intelligence was popularised by:', 'Abraham Maslow', 'Sigmund Freud', 'Daniel Goleman', 'Leon Festinger', 'C', 'Daniel Goleman popularised Emotional Intelligence through his widely read work on the subject.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q03', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Prejudice is a negative attitude toward a group.
2. Discrimination is the behavioural expression of prejudice.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Prejudice is a negative attitude, and discrimination is its behavioural manifestation.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q04', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Which is NOT one of Goleman''s five elements of Emotional Intelligence?', 'Intelligence quotient', 'Empathy', 'Self-awareness', 'Self-regulation', 'A', 'Goleman''s elements are self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation, empathy and social skills; IQ is separate.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q05', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'The mental discomfort from holding conflicting beliefs is termed:', 'Cognitive bias', 'Cognitive dissonance', 'Cognitive load', 'Cognitive map', 'B', 'Leon Festinger''s cognitive dissonance describes discomfort from holding inconsistent beliefs or attitudes.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q06', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'A stereotype is best described as the ___ component of an attitude toward a group.', 'Affective', 'Behavioural', 'Cognitive', 'Physiological', 'C', 'A stereotype is the cognitive component, a generalised belief about members of a group.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q07', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Which feature best characterises attitudes?', 'They are innate and fixed at birth', 'They change every moment', 'They cannot influence behaviour', 'They are learned and relatively enduring', 'D', 'Attitudes are learned, relatively enduring evaluations that influence behaviour.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q08', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Empathy is a component of emotional intelligence.
2. High emotional intelligence helps an administrator manage stress.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Empathy is central to EI, and high EI aids stress management and balanced decision-making.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q01', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'The ''categorical imperative'' is a core idea of which philosopher?', 'Aristotle', 'Jeremy Bentham', 'Immanuel Kant', 'John Rawls', 'C', 'Immanuel Kant''s categorical imperative requires acting only on maxims that could be universal laws.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q02', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'The principle of the ''greatest happiness of the greatest number'' is associated with:', 'Deontology', 'Virtue ethics', 'Existentialism', 'Utilitarianism', 'D', 'Utilitarianism, advanced by Bentham and Mill, seeks the greatest happiness of the greatest number.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q03', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Aristotle is associated with virtue ethics and the golden mean.
2. John Rawls proposed the ''veil of ignorance''.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'Aristotle gave virtue ethics and the golden mean; Rawls proposed the veil of ignorance for justice.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q04', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Gandhi''s idea that the wealthy hold their riches in trust for society is called:', 'Satyagraha', 'Sarvodaya', 'Trusteeship', 'Swadeshi', 'C', 'Gandhi''s trusteeship doctrine holds that the rich should manage wealth for the welfare of society.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q05', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'According to Aristotle, virtue lies in:', 'The greatest pleasure', 'Maximising utility', 'Strict obedience to law', 'The golden mean between extremes', 'D', 'Aristotle held that moral virtue is the golden mean between two vices of excess and deficiency.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q06', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'The concept of ''Nishkama Karma'', action without attachment to results, is taught in the:', 'Bhagavad Gita', 'Arthashastra', 'Republic', 'Leviathan', 'A', 'The Bhagavad Gita teaches Nishkama Karma, performing one''s duty without attachment to its fruits.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q07', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Which thinker linked ethics with statecraft in the Arthashastra?', 'Confucius', 'Plato', 'Kautilya', 'Socrates', 'C', 'Kautilya (Chanakya) integrated ethics with practical statecraft and economy in the Arthashastra.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q08', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Swami Vivekananda chiefly emphasised:', 'Renunciation of all action', 'Pursuit of personal wealth', 'Service to humanity as worship', 'Absolute obedience to authority', 'C', 'Vivekananda taught that selfless service to humanity is a form of worship of the divine.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q01', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'The ''Seven Principles of Public Life'' were articulated by which committee?', 'The Nolan Committee', 'The Santhanam Committee', 'The Hota Committee', 'The Sarkaria Commission', 'A', 'The UK''s Nolan Committee laid down the Seven Principles of Public Life.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q02', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Which value requires a civil servant to treat all citizens without favour or bias?', 'Anonymity', 'Impartiality', 'Secrecy', 'Hierarchy', 'B', 'Impartiality requires treating all citizens equally, without favour, bias or discrimination.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q03', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Integrity means honesty and wholeness in conduct.
2. Objectivity means deciding on merit and evidence.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'Integrity is honesty and consistency, while objectivity means basing decisions on merit and evidence.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q04', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Conduct of All India Service officers is governed by which rules?', 'Representation of the People Act, 1951', 'All India Services (Conduct) Rules, 1968', 'Right to Information Act, 2005', 'Indian Penal Code, 1860', 'B', 'The All India Services (Conduct) Rules, 1968 govern the conduct of All India Service officers.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q05', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'The traditional value requiring a civil servant to serve the elected government of the day neutrally is:', 'Partisanship', 'Political neutrality', 'Populism', 'Activism', 'B', 'Political neutrality requires the permanent civil service to serve any elected government impartially.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q06', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Which body in India recommended reforms in its report ''Ethics in Governance''?', 'The First ARC', 'The Law Commission', 'The Second ARC', 'The Finance Commission', 'C', 'The Second Administrative Reforms Commission devoted a report to ''Ethics in Governance''.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q07', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Ultimately, in a democracy, a civil servant is accountable to the:', 'Public', 'Media alone', 'Their own family', 'Foreign agencies', 'A', 'A civil servant is accountable to the law, the political executive and ultimately the public.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q08', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Which value increasingly emphasised in modern administration relates to compassion for the weak?', 'Aloofness', 'Empathy', 'Indifference', 'Rigidity', 'B', 'Empathy and compassion toward weaker sections are increasingly stressed civil service values.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q01', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Probity in governance essentially means:', 'Integrity and uprightness in public life', 'Speed of decision-making', 'Maximising government revenue', 'Strict secrecy of files', 'A', 'Probity means complete integrity, uprightness and honesty in the conduct of public affairs.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q02', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'The Right to Information Act was enacted in which year?', '2002', '2009', '2005', '2013', 'C', 'The Right to Information Act was enacted in 2005 to promote transparency and accountability.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q03', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Prevention of Corruption Act was enacted in 1988.
2. The Central Vigilance Commission is the apex integrity watchdog.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The Prevention of Corruption Act dates to 1988, and the CVC is the apex anti-corruption watchdog.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q04', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'A Citizen''s Charter primarily aims to:', 'Declare service standards and grievance redress', 'Increase tax collection', 'Conduct elections', 'Appoint judges', 'A', 'A Citizen''s Charter declares an organisation''s service standards and mechanisms for redress.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q05', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'The institution created to act as an ombudsman against corruption at the central level is the:', 'Election Commission', 'NITI Aayog', 'Finance Commission', 'Lokpal', 'D', 'The Lokpal, set up under the Lokpal and Lokayuktas Act, 2013, is the central anti-corruption ombudsman.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q06', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Which Act protects those who expose corruption or wrongdoing?', 'The Official Secrets Act, 1923', 'The Whistle Blowers Protection Act, 2014', 'The Companies Act, 2013', 'The Contempt of Courts Act, 1971', 'B', 'The Whistle Blowers Protection Act, 2014 provides protection to those disclosing corruption.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q07', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Which mechanism, used in MGNREGA, lets the community verify public spending?', 'Social audit', 'Internal audit', 'Statutory audit', 'Forensic audit', 'A', 'Social audit empowers the community to scrutinise public spending, notably under MGNREGA.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q08', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Probity in governance rests primarily on transparency, accountability and the:', 'Discretion of officials', 'Rule of the majority', 'Rule of law', 'Secrecy of decisions', 'C', 'Probity rests on transparency, accountability and the rule of law in public administration.', 7),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q01', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'An ethical dilemma is best described as a conflict between:', 'A right and a clearly wrong option', 'Law and personal profit', 'Two equally valid right values', 'Two illegal options', 'C', 'An ethical dilemma is a genuine conflict between two competing right values, not right versus wrong.', 0),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q02', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'In ethics, the principle that good ends do not justify wrong means stresses the importance of:', 'Only the final outcome', 'Means as well as ends', 'Personal gain', 'Speed over correctness', 'B', 'Ethical administration insists that the means must be as legitimate as the ends sought.', 1),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q03', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Identifying stakeholders is a key step in a case study.
2. The decision should be justified with reasons.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'Both 1 and 2', 'D', 'A sound case-study answer identifies stakeholders and gives a reasoned justification for the chosen action.', 2),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q04', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'The ''publicity test'' for an ethical decision asks whether you would:', 'Keep it strictly secret', 'Be willing to defend it publicly', 'Maximise personal benefit', 'Obey superiors blindly', 'B', 'The publicity test asks whether you could openly justify and defend the decision before the public.', 3),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q05', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'Which of the following is typically the FIRST step in analysing a case study?', 'State the facts and identify the dilemma', 'Announce the final decision', 'Punish the wrongdoer', 'Ignore the stakeholders', 'A', 'The first step is to understand the facts clearly and identify the central ethical dilemma.', 4),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q06', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'A frequent dilemma in case studies is the conflict between:', 'Two unrelated hobbies', 'Personal ethics and professional duty', 'Two foreign policies', 'Weather and climate', 'B', 'Conflicts between personal ethics and professional or official duty are common case-study dilemmas.', 5),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q07', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'Evaluating each option against ethics and law before deciding is important because it ensures the choice is:', 'Arbitrary', 'Based on personal bias', 'Defensible and reasoned', 'Hidden from scrutiny', 'C', 'Weighing options against ethics and law makes the final decision defensible and well reasoned.', 6),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q08', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Pressure from political superiors is a recurring case-study theme.
2. The legality and conscience checks help resolve dilemmas.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Pressure from superiors is common, and legality plus conscience checks guide a reasoned resolution.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q01', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'The Digital India programme was launched in which year?', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', 'B', 'The Digital India programme was launched in 2015 to transform India into a digitally empowered society.', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q02', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'In e-governance, ''G2C'' interaction refers to:', 'Government to Citizen', 'Government to Business', 'Government to Government', 'Government to Employee', 'A', 'G2C denotes Government to Citizen service delivery in the e-governance framework.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q03', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Accountability and transparency are pillars of good governance.
2. e-Governance can reduce discretion and corruption.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'Good governance rests on accountability and transparency, and e-governance curbs discretion and graft.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q04', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'Which platform allows citizens to store official documents digitally?', 'DigiLocker', 'MyGov', 'GeM', 'PRAGATI', 'A', 'DigiLocker provides citizens secure cloud-based storage and access to official documents.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q05', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'Common Service Centres (CSCs) are mainly intended to:', 'Replace courts', 'Conduct elections', 'Deliver digital services at the last mile', 'Print currency', 'C', 'CSCs deliver government and digital services to citizens at the last mile, especially in rural areas.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q06', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'The ''JAM trinity'' enabling Direct Benefit Transfer comprises Jan Dhan, Aadhaar and:', 'Microfinance', 'Mobile', 'Markets', 'Mandis', 'B', 'The JAM trinity is Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar and Mobile numbers, enabling Direct Benefit Transfer.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q07', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'The motto ''Minimum Government, Maximum Governance'' emphasises:', 'Expanding bureaucracy', 'Reducing citizen services', 'Centralising all power', 'Simplification and process re-engineering', 'D', 'The motto stresses simplifying processes and reducing red tape while improving service delivery.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q08', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'The Sevottam model is associated with:', 'Service delivery standards and grievance redress', 'Defence procurement', 'Foreign trade', 'Monetary policy', 'A', 'The Sevottam model sets standards for public service delivery and grievance redress.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q01', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'The Right to Information flows mainly from which Fundamental Right?', 'Article 21', 'Article 32', 'Article 14', 'Article 19(1)(a) freedom of speech and expression', 'D', 'The RTI is read into Article 19(1)(a), the freedom of speech and expression.', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q02', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'Under the RTI Act, information is normally to be provided within:', '15 days', '45 days', '30 days', '60 days', 'C', 'The RTI Act requires information to be furnished within 30 days of the request in normal cases.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q03', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The CAG audits government accounts under Article 148.
2. The Public Accounts Committee scrutinises government spending.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The CAG audits accounts under Article 148, and the PAC examines audited government expenditure.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q04', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'The apex appellate body under the RTI Act at the central level is the:', 'Central Information Commission', 'Central Vigilance Commission', 'Central Administrative Tribunal', 'National Human Rights Commission', 'A', 'The Central Information Commission is the apex appellate authority under the RTI Act at the Centre.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q05', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'When information concerns the life or liberty of a person, the RTI reply must be given within:', '15 days', '7 days', '48 hours', '30 days', 'C', 'Where life or liberty is involved, the RTI Act mandates a response within 48 hours.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q06', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'Which tool lets a local community directly verify the use of public funds?', 'Statutory audit', 'Performance budgeting', 'Social audit', 'Zero-based budgeting', 'C', 'Social audit allows the community to verify how public funds are spent, as in MGNREGA.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q07', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'The CAG is described as the:', 'Chief electoral officer', 'Head of the executive', 'Guardian of the public purse', 'Custodian of foreign reserves', 'C', 'The Comptroller and Auditor General is called the guardian of the public purse.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q08', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'RTI exemptions for certain intelligence and security organisations are listed in the:', 'First Schedule', 'Second Schedule', 'Third Schedule', 'Fourth Schedule', 'B', 'The Second Schedule of the RTI Act lists exempt intelligence and security organisations.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q01', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Untouchability is abolished by which Article of the Constitution?', 'Article 14', 'Article 15', 'Article 17', 'Article 21', 'C', 'Article 17 abolishes untouchability and forbids its practice in any form.', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q02', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The National Commission for Scheduled Castes is provided for under which Article?', 'Article 340', 'Article 338A', 'Article 338B', 'Article 338', 'D', 'Article 338 provides for the National Commission for Scheduled Castes.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q03', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Forest Rights Act was enacted in 2006.
2. It recognises rights of forest-dwelling communities.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The Forest Rights Act, 2006 recognises the rights of forest-dwelling Scheduled Tribes and other dwellers.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q04', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The National Commission for Backward Classes became a constitutional body under which Article?', 'Article 338', 'Article 338B', 'Article 338A', 'Article 340', 'B', 'The 102nd Amendment inserted Article 338B, giving the NCBC constitutional status.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q05', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act was enacted in which year?', '1995', '2006', '2013', '2016', 'D', 'The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act was enacted in 2016, expanding recognised disabilities to 21.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q06', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Which scheme targets the welfare of women and children through nutrition support?', 'Make in India', 'Poshan Abhiyaan', 'Stand-Up India', 'Smart Cities Mission', 'B', 'Poshan Abhiyaan aims to improve nutritional outcomes for children, pregnant women and mothers.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q07', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Special provisions enabling the State to make laws for women and children are found in:', 'Article 32', 'Article 19(1)(a)', 'Article 25', 'Article 15(3)', 'D', 'Article 15(3) allows the State to make special provisions for women and children.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q08', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Administration of tribal areas in states like Assam, Meghalaya and Mizoram is governed by the:', 'Fifth Schedule', 'Sixth Schedule', 'Seventh Schedule', 'Eighth Schedule', 'B', 'The Sixth Schedule governs the administration of tribal areas in Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura and Mizoram.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q01', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY provides health cover of how much per family per year?', '5 lakh', '3 lakh', '1 lakh', '10 lakh', 'A', 'PM-JAY provides health cover of 5 lakh rupees per family per year for secondary and tertiary care.', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q02', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education Act was enacted in:', '2002', '2005', '2009', '2016', 'C', 'The RTE Act, 2009 operationalises Article 21A, guaranteeing free education to children aged 6 to 14.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q03', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The National Medical Commission replaced the Medical Council of India.
2. The NEP 2020 introduced a 5+3+3+4 school structure.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'C', 'The NMC replaced the MCI in 2020, and the NEP 2020 introduced the 5+3+3+4 schooling structure.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q04', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'Which body regulates higher education and universities in India?', 'SEBI', 'The RBI', 'The UGC', 'The NITI Aayog', 'C', 'The University Grants Commission (UGC) regulates standards in higher education and universities.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q05', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The Human Development Index combines income with which two dimensions?', 'Inflation and employment', 'Savings and consumption', 'Trade and investment', 'Health and education', 'D', 'The HDI combines health (life expectancy), education and per capita income.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q06', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The NEP 2020 targets a Gross Enrolment Ratio in higher education of about what level by 2035?', '50 per cent', '40 per cent', '30 per cent', '60 per cent', 'A', 'The NEP 2020 aims to raise the higher-education Gross Enrolment Ratio to 50 per cent by 2035.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q07', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'Health and education in India largely fall under which legislative list?', 'Union List', 'Concurrent List', 'State List', 'Residuary powers', 'B', 'Both health-related matters and education are largely on the Concurrent List shared by Centre and States.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q08', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'India''s potential ''demographic dividend'' depends most critically on:', 'Rising death rates', 'Reducing literacy', 'Skilling its young workforce', 'Cutting health spending', 'C', 'The demographic dividend is realised only if the large young population is educated and skilled.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Which is India''s principal anti-terror law?', 'The NIA Act, 2008', 'The PMLA, 2002', 'The Arms Act, 1959', 'The UAPA, 1967', 'D', 'The Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act, 1967 is India''s principal anti-terror legislation.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Which agency investigates terror-related offences at the national level?', 'The CBI', 'The Intelligence Bureau', 'The Enforcement Directorate', 'The National Investigation Agency', 'D', 'The National Investigation Agency (NIA) investigates terror offences under the NIA Act, 2008.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Left-Wing Extremism has been called India''s single biggest internal security threat.
2. The CRPF is the lead force for anti-Naxal operations.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'LWE was termed the biggest internal security threat, and the CRPF leads anti-Naxal operations.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'The 2019 amendment to the UAPA notably allowed the government to designate as terrorists:', 'Only organisations', 'Only foreign nationals', 'Only convicted persons', 'Individuals as well', 'D', 'The 2019 UAPA amendment empowered the government to designate individuals, not just organisations, as terrorists.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Insurgency in India has been most persistently associated with which region?', 'Kerala', 'The North-East', 'Gujarat', 'Goa', 'B', 'Several North-Eastern states have witnessed long-running insurgencies over identity and autonomy.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Which of the following is a Central Armed Police Force?', 'The Indian Navy', 'The Territorial Army', 'The Indian Air Force', 'The CISF', 'D', 'The CISF is one of the Central Armed Police Forces, alongside the CRPF, BSF, ITBP and SSB.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'The corridor of districts affected by Left-Wing Extremism is popularly called the:', 'Golden Corridor', 'Red Corridor', 'Green Corridor', 'Blue Corridor', 'B', 'The belt of LWE-affected districts in central and eastern India is known as the Red Corridor.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Which force is mainly deployed for internal security and law-and-order duties across states?', 'The CRPF', 'The BSF', 'The ITBP', 'The Coast Guard', 'A', 'The Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF) is the lead force for internal security and law and order.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Which is the national nodal agency for responding to cyber security incidents in India?', 'NCIIPC', 'CERT-In', 'NTRO', 'NIA', 'B', 'CERT-In is the national nodal agency for handling cyber security incidents in India.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'The primary law dealing with cyber offences in India is the:', 'Indian Penal Code, 1860', 'Telegraph Act, 1885', 'Information Technology Act, 2000', 'Evidence Act, 1872', 'C', 'The Information Technology Act, 2000 is the primary law governing cyber offences in India.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Consider the following statements:
1. Money laundering has three stages: placement, layering and integration.
2. The Enforcement Directorate enforces the PMLA.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'Laundering involves placement, layering and integration, and the ED enforces the PMLA, 2002.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Which global body sets standards against money laundering and terror financing?', 'The IMF', 'The WTO', 'The FATF', 'The OECD', 'C', 'The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) sets global anti-money-laundering and counter-terror-finance standards.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Ransomware is a cyber threat that typically:', 'Speeds up a computer', 'Backs up files automatically', 'Encrypts data and demands payment', 'Improves network security', 'C', 'Ransomware encrypts a victim''s data and demands a ransom for its release.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'The agency that receives and analyses suspicious transaction reports in India is the:', 'FIU-IND', 'SEBI', 'CERT-In', 'RBI', 'A', 'The Financial Intelligence Unit-India (FIU-IND) collects and analyses suspicious transaction reports.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'An informal value-transfer system often misused for laundering is known as:', 'Hundi insurance', 'Hawala', 'Crowdfunding', 'Factoring', 'B', 'Hawala is an informal, trust-based money-transfer network frequently misused for laundering.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Which body is tasked with protecting India''s critical information infrastructure?', 'NCIIPC', 'CERT-In', 'FIU-IND', 'The Coast Guard', 'A', 'The National Critical Information Infrastructure Protection Centre (NCIIPC) guards critical information assets.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'Which force primarily guards the India-Pakistan and India-Bangladesh borders?', 'The ITBP', 'The Border Security Force', 'The SSB', 'The Assam Rifles', 'B', 'The Border Security Force (BSF) guards the India-Pakistan and India-Bangladesh borders.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The Indo-Tibetan Border Police primarily guards the border with:', 'Pakistan', 'Bangladesh', 'China', 'Myanmar', 'C', 'The ITBP guards the India-China border along the Line of Actual Control.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The Sashastra Seema Bal guards the Nepal and Bhutan borders.
2. The Assam Rifles guards the Myanmar border.
Which is/are correct?', '1 only', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'B', 'The SSB guards the Nepal and Bhutan borders, while the Assam Rifles guards the Myanmar frontier.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The boundary between India and Pakistan demarcated at Partition is the:', 'McMahon Line', 'Radcliffe Line', 'Durand Line', 'Line of Actual Control', 'B', 'The Radcliffe Line, drawn in 1947, demarcates the India-Pakistan boundary.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'After the 2008 Mumbai attacks, the lead agency for coastal security in territorial waters became the:', 'Indian Navy', 'Indian Coast Guard', 'The BSF', 'The CISF', 'B', 'The Indian Coast Guard was made the lead agency for coastal security in territorial waters after 2008.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The India-China boundary in the eastern sector is broadly defined by the:', 'Radcliffe Line', 'McMahon Line', 'Durand Line', 'Line of Control', 'B', 'The McMahon Line broadly defines the India-China boundary in the eastern sector.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The programme that funds development of villages along the border is the:', 'Smart Cities Mission', 'Border Area Development Programme', 'AMRUT', 'PM Gram Sadak Yojana', 'B', 'The Border Area Development Programme (BADP) funds development of border-area villages.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The technology-based system to seal vulnerable border stretches is the:', 'CIBMS', 'NATGRID', 'CCTNS', 'UMANG', 'A', 'The Comprehensive Integrated Border Management System (CIBMS) uses technology to monitor borders.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The Disaster Management Act in India was enacted in which year?', '2000', '2009', '2005', '2013', 'C', 'The Disaster Management Act was enacted in 2005, creating a three-tier institutional structure.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA) is chaired by the:', 'Home Minister', 'Cabinet Secretary', 'President', 'Prime Minister', 'D', 'The NDMA is chaired by the Prime Minister of India.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'Consider the following statements:
1. The State Disaster Management Authority is headed by the Chief Minister.
2. The District Disaster Management Authority is headed by the District Collector.
Which is/are correct?', 'Both 1 and 2', '2 only', '1 only', 'Neither 1 nor 2', 'A', 'The SDMA is headed by the Chief Minister and the DDMA by the District Collector or Magistrate.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The global framework guiding disaster risk reduction for 2015-2030 is the:', 'Hyogo Framework', 'Paris Agreement', 'Kyoto Protocol', 'Sendai Framework', 'D', 'The Sendai Framework (2015-2030) guides global disaster risk reduction with four priorities.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The specialised force for disaster response in India is the:', 'BSF', 'CRPF', 'NDRF', 'Territorial Army', 'C', 'The National Disaster Response Force (NDRF) is the specialised force for disaster response.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The Coalition for Disaster Resilient Infrastructure (CDRI) was launched by India in:', '2015', '2019', '2017', '2021', 'B', 'India launched the Coalition for Disaster Resilient Infrastructure (CDRI) in 2019.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The 1984 Bhopal Gas Tragedy is an example of which type of disaster?', 'Natural disaster', 'Biological disaster', 'Man-made (industrial) disaster', 'Astronomical disaster', 'C', 'The Bhopal Gas Tragedy was a man-made industrial chemical disaster.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'Activities such as prevention, mitigation and preparedness belong to which phase of disaster management?', 'Response phase', 'Pre-disaster phase', 'Recovery phase', 'Rehabilitation phase', 'B', 'Prevention, mitigation and preparedness are activities of the pre-disaster phase.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-fundamental-rights-q09', 'upsc-polity-fundamental-rights', 'The Right to Constitutional Remedies (Article 32) was described by Dr B. R. Ambedkar as:', 'The soul of the Constitution', 'A dead letter', 'A minor provision', 'The heart and soul of the Constitution', 'D', 'Ambedkar called Article 32 ''the heart and soul of the Constitution'' for enabling enforcement of Fundamental Rights.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-fundamental-rights-q10', 'upsc-polity-fundamental-rights', 'The writ issued to release a person unlawfully detained is:', 'Mandamus', 'Habeas Corpus', 'Certiorari', 'Quo Warranto', 'B', 'Habeas Corpus (''to have the body'') orders the production of a detained person to test the legality of detention.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-fundamental-rights-q11', 'upsc-polity-fundamental-rights', 'Right to Property was removed as a Fundamental Right by which amendment?', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '1st Amendment', '73rd Amendment', 'B', 'The 44th Amendment (1978) made the Right to Property a legal right under Article 300A, not a Fundamental Right.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-fundamental-rights-q12', 'upsc-polity-fundamental-rights', 'Article 21 guarantees the:', 'Right to equality', 'Right to protection of life and personal liberty', 'Right against exploitation', 'Right to freedom of religion', 'B', 'Article 21 protects life and personal liberty, expansively interpreted (dignity, privacy, clean environment).', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures-q09', 'upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures', 'A Money Bill can be introduced only in the:', 'Rajya Sabha', 'Lok Sabha', 'Either House', 'Joint sitting', 'B', 'Under Article 110, a Money Bill originates only in the Lok Sabha, on the President''s recommendation.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures-q10', 'upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures', 'The maximum gap allowed between two sessions of Parliament is:', 'Three months', 'Six months', 'One year', 'Four months', 'B', 'Article 85 requires that six months not elapse between the last sitting of one session and the first of the next.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures-q11', 'upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures', 'A joint sitting of both Houses is presided over by the:', 'President', 'Vice-President', 'Speaker of the Lok Sabha', 'Prime Minister', 'C', 'The Speaker of the Lok Sabha presides over a joint sitting summoned under Article 108.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures-q12', 'upsc-polity-parliament-state-legislatures', 'The Rajya Sabha''s special power under Article 249 allows Parliament to legislate on a State List subject if it passes a resolution by:', 'Simple majority', 'Two-thirds of members present and voting', 'Absolute majority', 'Unanimous vote', 'B', 'Article 249 needs a Rajya Sabha resolution by two-thirds of members present and voting in the national interest.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q09', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'The Directive Principles of State Policy are borrowed from the constitution of:', 'USA', 'Ireland', 'Britain', 'Canada', 'B', 'The DPSP were inspired by the Irish Constitution (which took them from the Spanish).', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q10', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution by which amendment?', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '1st Amendment', '73rd Amendment', 'A', 'The 42nd Amendment (1976), on the Swaran Singh Committee''s recommendation, added Fundamental Duties (Article 51A).', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q11', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Directive Principles are:', 'Justiciable (enforceable in court)', 'Non-justiciable but fundamental in governance', 'Superior to Fundamental Rights', 'Applicable only to states', 'B', 'DPSP are non-justiciable but Article 37 makes them fundamental in the country''s governance.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties-q12', 'upsc-polity-dpsp-and-fundamental-duties', 'Which article directs the State to secure a uniform civil code?', 'Article 44', 'Article 40', 'Article 48', 'Article 50', 'A', 'Article 44 directs the State to endeavour to secure a Uniform Civil Code for all citizens.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q09', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'The ''basic structure'' doctrine was propounded in which case?', 'Golaknath case', 'Kesavananda Bharati case', 'Minerva Mills case', 'Maneka Gandhi case', 'B', 'The Kesavananda Bharati case (1973) held that Parliament cannot alter the Constitution''s basic structure.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q10', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Judges of the Supreme Court are appointed by the:', 'President', 'Prime Minister', 'Parliament', 'Chief Justice alone', 'A', 'The President appoints Supreme Court judges, in practice through the collegium system.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q11', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'A Supreme Court judge holds office until the age of:', '62 years', '65 years', '70 years', '60 years', 'B', 'Supreme Court judges retire at 65; High Court judges at 62.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review-q12', 'upsc-polity-judiciary-and-judicial-review', 'Public Interest Litigation (PIL) in India was pioneered largely by:', 'Justices P. N. Bhagwati and V. R. Krishna Iyer', 'The executive', 'The Election Commission', 'Parliament', 'A', 'PIL was developed by Justices Bhagwati and Krishna Iyer, relaxing locus standi for public causes.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q09', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) is provided for under which article?', 'Article 148', 'Article 324', 'Article 315', 'Article 280', 'A', 'Article 148 establishes the CAG, the guardian of the public purse who audits government accounts.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q10', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Election Commission of India is a:', 'Statutory body', 'Constitutional body', 'Executive body', 'Non-governmental body', 'B', 'The ECI is a constitutional body under Article 324, superintending elections.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q11', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The National Human Rights Commission (NHRC) is a:', 'Constitutional body', 'Statutory body', 'Constitutional and statutory body', 'Private body', 'B', 'The NHRC is a statutory body established under the Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies-q12', 'upsc-polity-constitutional-and-statutory-bodies', 'The Finance Commission is constituted every:', 'Year', 'Five years (or earlier)', 'Ten years', 'Three years', 'B', 'Under Article 280, the President constitutes a Finance Commission every fifth year or earlier.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q09', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The President is elected by an electoral college through:', 'Direct election', 'Proportional representation by single transferable vote', 'First-past-the-post', 'Nomination', 'B', 'The President is elected indirectly by proportional representation using the single transferable vote.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q10', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the:', 'President', 'Lok Sabha', 'Rajya Sabha', 'Supreme Court', 'B', 'Article 75 makes the Council of Ministers collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q11', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The ordinance-making power of the President is under which article?', 'Article 123', 'Article 72', 'Article 356', 'Article 143', 'A', 'Article 123 lets the President promulgate ordinances when Parliament is not in session.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers-q12', 'upsc-polity-president-pm-and-council-of-ministers', 'The maximum size of the Council of Ministers is capped at ___ of the strength of the Lok Sabha (91st Amendment).', '10%', '15%', '20%', '25%', 'B', 'The 91st Amendment (2003) caps the Council of Ministers at 15% of the Lok Sabha''s strength.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q09', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'The division of legislative powers is set out in the:', 'Seventh Schedule', 'Ninth Schedule', 'Tenth Schedule', 'Fifth Schedule', 'A', 'The Seventh Schedule contains the Union, State, and Concurrent Lists dividing legislative subjects.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q10', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'In case of conflict on a Concurrent List subject, which law prevails?', 'State law', 'Central law (with exceptions)', 'Neither', 'The older law', 'B', 'Under Article 254, central law generally prevails over conflicting state law on the Concurrent List.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q11', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'The Indian federation is often described as:', 'Purely federal', 'Quasi-federal / federal with a unitary bias', 'Purely unitary', 'Confederal', 'B', 'K. C. Wheare called India ''quasi-federal'' — federal in form but with a strong unitary tilt.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations-q12', 'upsc-polity-federalism-and-centre-state-relations', 'The Inter-State Council is provided for under which article?', 'Article 263', 'Article 280', 'Article 324', 'Article 356', 'A', 'Article 263 empowers the President to establish an Inter-State Council to coordinate between states.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q09', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Panchayati Raj was given constitutional status by which amendment?', '73rd Amendment', '74th Amendment', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', 'A', 'The 73rd Amendment (1992) added Part IX and the Eleventh Schedule, giving Panchayats constitutional status.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q10', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Urban local bodies (municipalities) were constitutionalised by the:', '73rd Amendment', '74th Amendment', '72nd Amendment', '65th Amendment', 'B', 'The 74th Amendment (1992) added Part IXA and the Twelfth Schedule for urban local governance.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q11', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'Reservation for women in Panchayats under the 73rd Amendment is at least:', 'One-third', 'One-half', 'One-fourth', 'One-tenth', 'A', 'At least one-third of seats (and chairperson posts) are reserved for women in Panchayats.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government-q12', 'upsc-polity-panchayati-raj-and-local-government', 'The three-tier Panchayati Raj system was recommended by the:', 'Balwant Rai Mehta Committee', 'Sarkaria Commission', 'Punchhi Commission', 'Ashok Mehta Committee', 'A', 'The Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957) recommended the three-tier structure (village, block, district).', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q09', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'A National Emergency is proclaimed under which article?', 'Article 352', 'Article 356', 'Article 360', 'Article 370', 'A', 'Article 352 provides for a National Emergency on grounds of war, external aggression, or armed rebellion.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q10', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'President''s Rule in a state is imposed under which article?', 'Article 352', 'Article 356', 'Article 360', 'Article 365', 'B', 'Article 356 allows President''s Rule on the failure of constitutional machinery in a state.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q11', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'A Financial Emergency is declared under which article?', 'Article 352', 'Article 356', 'Article 360', 'Article 361', 'C', 'Article 360 provides for a Financial Emergency; it has never been invoked.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments-q12', 'upsc-polity-emergency-provisions-and-amendments', 'The word ''secular'' was added to the Preamble by which amendment?', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '1st Amendment', '24th Amendment', 'A', 'The 42nd Amendment (1976) added ''socialist'', ''secular'', and ''integrity'' to the Preamble.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857', 'The immediate trigger of the Revolt of 1857 was the:', 'Doctrine of Lapse', 'Greased Enfield rifle cartridges', 'Partition of Bengal', 'Vernacular Press Act', 'B', 'The rumour that cartridges were greased with cow and pig fat outraged Hindu and Muslim sepoys.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857', 'The 1857 revolt began at which cantonment?', 'Meerut', 'Barrackpore', 'Kanpur', 'Jhansi', 'A', 'The revolt broke out at Meerut on 10 May 1857 before spreading to Delhi.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857', 'After 1857, the governance of India was transferred from the East India Company to the:', 'British Crown', 'Mughal Emperor', 'Indian National Congress', 'Board of Control', 'A', 'The Government of India Act 1858 transferred power to the British Crown, ending Company rule.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-revolt-of-1857', 'Who led the revolt at Jhansi?', 'Rani Lakshmibai', 'Nana Sahib', 'Tantia Tope', 'Begum Hazrat Mahal', 'A', 'Rani Lakshmibai led the resistance at Jhansi against the British.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in 1885 by:', 'A. O. Hume', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak', 'Mahatma Gandhi', 'A', 'Retired ICS officer A. O. Hume founded the INC in 1885; W. C. Bonnerjee was its first president.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The slogan ''Swaraj is my birthright and I shall have it'' is associated with:', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak', 'Gopal Krishna Gokhale', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'Lala Lajpat Rai', 'A', 'Tilak, an Extremist leader, popularised this Swaraj slogan.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'The Congress split into Moderates and Extremists at the ___ session (1907).', 'Surat', 'Lucknow', 'Calcutta', 'Lahore', 'A', 'The famous Surat Split of 1907 divided the Congress into Moderates and Extremists.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-moderates-and-extremists', 'Dadabhai Naoroji is best known for his:', 'Drain of Wealth theory', 'Non-Cooperation Movement', 'Doctrine of Passive Resistance', 'Home Rule League', 'A', 'Naoroji''s ''Drain of Wealth'' theory exposed the economic exploitation of India by Britain.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The Non-Cooperation Movement was launched in:', '1920', '1930', '1942', '1919', 'A', 'Gandhi launched the Non-Cooperation Movement in 1920 after Jallianwala Bagh and the Khilafat issue.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The Dandi March (1930) launched the:', 'Civil Disobedience Movement', 'Quit India Movement', 'Non-Cooperation Movement', 'Home Rule Movement', 'A', 'Gandhi''s Salt March to Dandi began the Civil Disobedience Movement by breaking the salt law.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The slogan ''Do or Die'' is associated with the:', 'Quit India Movement (1942)', 'Non-Cooperation Movement', 'Swadeshi Movement', 'Khilafat Movement', 'A', 'Gandhi gave the ''Do or Die'' call during the Quit India Movement of 1942.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-gandhian-mass-movements', 'The Non-Cooperation Movement was withdrawn after the ___ incident.', 'Chauri Chaura', 'Jallianwala Bagh', 'Kakori', 'Champaran', 'A', 'Gandhi called off Non-Cooperation in 1922 after the violent Chauri Chaura incident.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Brahmo Samaj was founded by:', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy', 'Dayananda Saraswati', 'Swami Vivekananda', 'Jyotiba Phule', 'A', 'Raja Ram Mohan Roy founded the Brahmo Samaj (1828) and campaigned against sati.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'The Arya Samaj, with the slogan ''Back to the Vedas'', was founded by:', 'Dayananda Saraswati', 'Ram Mohan Roy', 'Keshab Chandra Sen', 'Annie Besant', 'A', 'Swami Dayananda Saraswati founded the Arya Samaj (1875), advocating a return to the Vedas.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'Sati was abolished in 1829 during the governor-generalship of:', 'Lord William Bentinck', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'Lord Curzon', 'Warren Hastings', 'A', 'Lord William Bentinck abolished sati in 1829 with Ram Mohan Roy''s support.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-socio-religious-reform-movements', 'Jyotiba Phule is associated with the:', 'Satyashodhak Samaj', 'Ramakrishna Mission', 'Aligarh Movement', 'Theosophical Society', 'A', 'Jyotiba Phule founded the Satyashodhak Samaj (1873) for the upliftment of lower castes and women.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q09', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'The Indian monsoon is a type of ___ wind.', 'Seasonal (reversing)', 'Permanent', 'Local', 'Trade', 'A', 'Monsoons are seasonal winds that reverse direction between summer and winter.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q10', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'The southwest monsoon typically arrives in India through:', 'Kerala coast', 'West Bengal', 'Gujarat', 'Tamil Nadu', 'A', 'The southwest monsoon usually breaks over the Kerala coast around 1 June.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q11', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'El Niño generally results in ___ rainfall over India.', 'Below-normal', 'Above-normal', 'No effect on', 'Excessive', 'A', 'El Niño (warming of the equatorial Pacific) is usually associated with weaker Indian monsoon rainfall.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate-q12', 'upsc-geography-monsoon-and-climate', 'The retreating monsoon brings rainfall mainly to:', 'Coromandel coast (Tamil Nadu)', 'Punjab', 'Rajasthan', 'Assam', 'A', 'The northeast (retreating) monsoon brings winter rain to the Tamil Nadu/Coromandel coast.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q09', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The highest peak in India (within its territory) is:', 'K2 (Godwin-Austen)', 'Kanchenjunga', 'Nanda Devi', 'Everest', 'A', 'K2, in the Karakoram, is the highest peak in Indian-administered territory (Kanchenjunga is highest wholly within India).', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q10', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'Which river is known as the ''Sorrow of Bihar''?', 'Kosi', 'Damodar', 'Yamuna', 'Godavari', 'A', 'The Kosi river, prone to shifting course and flooding, is called the ''Sorrow of Bihar''.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q11', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The Western Ghats and Eastern Ghats meet at the:', 'Nilgiri Hills', 'Aravalli Range', 'Vindhya Range', 'Satpura Range', 'A', 'The Western and Eastern Ghats converge at the Nilgiri Hills in the south.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers-q12', 'upsc-geography-indian-physiography-and-rivers', 'The Narmada and Tapi rivers flow into the:', 'Arabian Sea', 'Bay of Bengal', 'Indian Ocean directly', 'Rann of Kutch', 'A', 'The Narmada and Tapi are west-flowing rivers draining into the Arabian Sea through rift valleys.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q09', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'The most widespread and fertile soil in India is:', 'Alluvial soil', 'Black soil', 'Laterite soil', 'Red soil', 'A', 'Alluvial soil covers the northern plains and is India''s most extensive and productive soil.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q10', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Black (regur) soil is most suitable for growing:', 'Cotton', 'Tea', 'Rice', 'Coffee', 'A', 'Black soil''s moisture retention makes it ideal for cotton, so it is called ''black cotton soil''.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q11', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'The Green Revolution in India was centred on:', 'Wheat and rice (high-yielding varieties)', 'Pulses and oilseeds', 'Cotton and jute', 'Tea and coffee', 'A', 'The Green Revolution introduced HYV seeds mainly for wheat and rice, boosting food-grain output.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture-q12', 'upsc-geography-soils-and-agriculture', 'Laterite soil is formed by intense:', 'Leaching in high rainfall areas', 'Wind deposition', 'Glacial action', 'Volcanic activity', 'A', 'Laterite soil forms by heavy leaching in high-rainfall tropical regions, leaving iron and aluminium oxides.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q09', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'Fold mountains such as the Himalayas are formed by:', 'Compression of the Earth''s crust (plate collision)', 'Volcanic eruption', 'Wind erosion', 'River deposition', 'A', 'Fold mountains arise when crustal compression at converging plate boundaries folds rock strata upward.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q10', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The ''Ring of Fire'' is associated with:', 'Volcanoes and earthquakes around the Pacific', 'Deserts', 'Coral reefs', 'Ocean currents', 'A', 'The Pacific ''Ring of Fire'' is a belt of intense volcanic and seismic activity along plate boundaries.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q11', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'A landform created by river deposition at its mouth is a:', 'Delta', 'Meander', 'Waterfall', 'Gorge', 'A', 'A delta forms where a river deposits sediment as it enters a sea or lake.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms-q12', 'upsc-geography-world-geography-landforms', 'The longest mountain range on Earth is the:', 'Andes', 'Himalayas', 'Rockies', 'Alps', 'A', 'The Andes of South America form the longest continental mountain range.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q09', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'The RBI''s primary tool to control inflation is adjusting the:', 'Repo rate', 'Income tax', 'Customs duty', 'Fiscal deficit', 'A', 'The RBI raises the repo rate to curb inflation by making borrowing costlier and reducing money supply.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q10', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'The Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) targets a CPI inflation of:', '4% (±2%)', '2% (±1%)', '6% fixed', '0%', 'A', 'India''s flexible inflation targeting aims at 4% CPI inflation with a tolerance band of ±2%.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q11', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'A sustained fall in the general price level is called:', 'Deflation', 'Disinflation', 'Stagflation', 'Reflation', 'A', 'Deflation is a persistent decline in the general price level (negative inflation).', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy-q12', 'upsc-economy-inflation-and-monetary-policy', 'High inflation combined with stagnant growth and high unemployment is:', 'Stagflation', 'Deflation', 'Hyperinflation', 'Disinflation', 'A', 'Stagflation is the coexistence of stagnation (low growth, high unemployment) and inflation.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q09', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'GDP measured at current prices is called:', 'Nominal GDP', 'Real GDP', 'Potential GDP', 'Green GDP', 'A', 'Nominal GDP is valued at current prices; real GDP is adjusted for inflation using constant prices.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q10', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'In India, national income estimates are prepared by:', 'NSO/CSO under MoSPI', 'RBI', 'SEBI', 'NITI Aayog', 'A', 'The National Statistical Office (formerly CSO) under MoSPI compiles national income accounts.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q11', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'GDP at market price minus depreciation gives:', 'NDP at market price', 'GNP', 'Nominal GDP', 'Per capita income', 'A', 'Net Domestic Product = GDP − depreciation (consumption of fixed capital).', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp-q12', 'upsc-economy-national-income-and-gdp', 'GNP differs from GDP by including:', 'Net factor income from abroad', 'Depreciation', 'Indirect taxes', 'Subsidies', 'A', 'GNP = GDP + net factor income from abroad (income of residents earned overseas, less foreigners'' income here).', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q09', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The RBI was established in:', '1935', '1947', '1949', '1969', 'A', 'The Reserve Bank of India was established in 1935 and nationalised in 1949.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q10', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The portion of deposits banks must keep as cash reserves with the RBI is the:', 'Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)', 'Statutory Liquidity Ratio', 'Repo rate', 'Bank rate', 'A', 'The CRR is the fraction of net demand and time liabilities banks must keep as reserves with the RBI.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q11', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'Major commercial banks were first nationalised in India in:', '1969', '1955', '1980', '1991', 'A', 'Fourteen major banks were nationalised in 1969, followed by six more in 1980.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi-q12', 'upsc-economy-banking-system-and-rbi', 'The rate at which the RBI lends to commercial banks against securities is the:', 'Repo rate', 'Reverse repo rate', 'CRR', 'SLR', 'A', 'The repo rate is the RBI''s lending rate to banks against government securities.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q09', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The fiscal deficit is the difference between total expenditure and total receipts excluding:', 'Borrowings', 'Tax revenue', 'Grants', 'Subsidies', 'A', 'Fiscal deficit = total expenditure − total receipts other than borrowings; it shows the government''s borrowing need.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q10', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The FRBM Act aims to:', 'Ensure fiscal discipline (limit deficits)', 'Control inflation', 'Regulate banks', 'Fix exchange rates', 'A', 'The Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management Act sets targets to reduce fiscal and revenue deficits.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q11', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'A revenue deficit arises when:', 'Revenue expenditure exceeds revenue receipts', 'Capital receipts exceed expenditure', 'There is no borrowing', 'Tax revenue is zero', 'A', 'Revenue deficit = revenue expenditure − revenue receipts; it signals borrowing to meet current spending.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy-q12', 'upsc-economy-union-budget-and-fiscal-policy', 'The Consolidated Fund of India requires ___ for withdrawals.', 'Parliamentary authorisation', 'RBI approval', 'Supreme Court approval', 'No approval', 'A', 'Money can be withdrawn from the Consolidated Fund only with Parliament''s authorisation (appropriation).', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q09', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'GST is a ___ tax.', 'Destination-based indirect', 'Direct', 'Origin-based direct', 'Wealth', 'A', 'GST is a destination-based, multi-stage indirect tax levied on value addition.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q10', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'The body that decides GST rates is the:', 'GST Council', 'RBI', 'Finance Commission', 'NITI Aayog', 'A', 'The GST Council, chaired by the Union Finance Minister, decides rates and rules (Article 279A).', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q11', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'Income tax is an example of a ___ tax.', 'Direct', 'Indirect', 'Ad valorem indirect', 'Value-added', 'A', 'Income tax is a direct tax — the burden falls on the person on whom it is levied.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst-q12', 'upsc-economy-taxation-and-gst', 'A tax where the rate rises with income is called:', 'Progressive', 'Regressive', 'Proportional', 'Degressive', 'A', 'A progressive tax takes a higher percentage from higher incomes (e.g., income tax slabs).', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q09', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'MGNREGA guarantees how many days of wage employment per rural household per year?', '100 days', '50 days', '365 days', '200 days', 'A', 'MGNREGA guarantees 100 days of unskilled manual wage employment to a rural household each year.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q10', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Unemployment caused by a mismatch of skills and jobs is:', 'Structural unemployment', 'Seasonal unemployment', 'Cyclical unemployment', 'Frictional unemployment', 'A', 'Structural unemployment results from a mismatch between workers'' skills and available jobs.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q11', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'Disguised unemployment is most common in:', 'Agriculture', 'IT sector', 'Banking', 'Manufacturing', 'A', 'Disguised unemployment (more workers than needed) is typical of Indian agriculture.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth-q12', 'upsc-economy-poverty-unemployment-and-inclusive-growth', 'The Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI) measures deprivation in health, education, and:', 'Standard of living', 'Income only', 'Employment', 'Political rights', 'A', 'The MPI captures overlapping deprivations across health, education, and living standards.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q09', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'The difference between a country''s exports and imports of goods is the:', 'Balance of trade', 'Current account', 'Fiscal deficit', 'Capital account', 'A', 'The balance of trade is exports minus imports of merchandise (visible) goods.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q10', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'India''s foreign exchange reserves are managed by the:', 'RBI', 'SEBI', 'Ministry of Commerce', 'NITI Aayog', 'A', 'The RBI manages India''s forex reserves and intervenes to stabilise the rupee.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q11', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'The current account of the balance of payments includes trade in goods, services, and:', 'Transfers (remittances)', 'Foreign investment', 'External borrowing', 'Reserve changes', 'A', 'The current account covers goods, services, primary income, and secondary income (transfers/remittances).', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade-q12', 'upsc-economy-external-sector-and-trade', 'A depreciation of the rupee makes Indian exports:', 'Cheaper and more competitive abroad', 'Costlier abroad', 'Unaffected', 'Banned', 'A', 'A weaker rupee lowers the foreign-currency price of exports, boosting their competitiveness.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q09', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The Minimum Support Price (MSP) is announced on the recommendation of the:', 'CACP (Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices)', 'RBI', 'SEBI', 'Finance Commission', 'A', 'The CACP recommends MSPs, which the government announces to assure farmers a floor price.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q10', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'Foodgrains are procured and distributed through the Public Distribution System by the:', 'Food Corporation of India (FCI)', 'RBI', 'NABARD', 'SEBI', 'A', 'The FCI procures, stores, and distributes foodgrains for the PDS and buffer stock.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q11', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The National Food Security Act aims to provide subsidised foodgrains to about ___ of the population.', 'Two-thirds', 'One-tenth', 'One-fourth', 'All', 'A', 'The NFSA, 2013 covers up to 67% (about two-thirds) of the population with subsidised grains.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security-q12', 'upsc-economy-agriculture-and-food-security', 'The apex bank for agricultural and rural credit in India is:', 'NABARD', 'SIDBI', 'EXIM Bank', 'SEBI', 'A', 'NABARD is the apex development bank for agriculture and rural credit.', 11),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q09', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The PM Jan Dhan Yojana primarily aims at:', 'Financial inclusion (bank accounts for all)', 'Rural roads', 'Crop insurance', 'Skill training', 'A', 'PMJDY promotes financial inclusion by providing bank accounts, insurance, and pension access.', 8),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q10', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'Ayushman Bharat (PM-JAY) provides:', 'Health insurance cover to poor families', 'Housing loans', 'Free education', 'Pension', 'A', 'PM-JAY offers health-insurance cover (up to a set annual limit) to poor and vulnerable families.', 9),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q11', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission focuses on:', 'Sanitation and cleanliness', 'Digital literacy', 'Renewable energy', 'Foreign trade', 'A', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission promotes sanitation, toilet construction, and an open-defecation-free India.', 10),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes-q12', 'upsc-current-affairs-government-schemes', 'PM-KISAN provides eligible farmers with:', 'Direct income support', 'Free electricity', 'Subsidised loans only', 'Crop insurance', 'A', 'PM-KISAN gives income support to eligible landholding farmers via direct benefit transfer.', 11),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q09', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The Human Development Index (HDI) is published by:', 'UNDP', 'World Bank', 'IMF', 'WTO', 'A', 'The UNDP publishes the HDI, combining life expectancy, education, and income.', 8),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q10', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'NITI Aayog replaced which body in 2015?', 'Planning Commission', 'Finance Commission', 'UGC', 'RBI', 'A', 'NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission as the government''s policy think tank in 2015.', 9),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q11', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The Global Hunger Index is used to measure:', 'Hunger and undernutrition', 'Corruption', 'Press freedom', 'Ease of doing business', 'A', 'The Global Hunger Index tracks hunger using undernourishment, child wasting, stunting, and mortality.', 10),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices-q12', 'upsc-current-affairs-key-institutions-and-indices', 'The World Economic Outlook is released by the:', 'IMF', 'World Bank', 'WTO', 'OECD', 'A', 'The IMF publishes the World Economic Outlook with global growth projections.', 11),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q09', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'A Finance Commission''s core task is to recommend:', 'Distribution of tax revenue between Centre and states', 'Monetary policy', 'Foreign policy', 'Judicial appointments', 'A', 'The Finance Commission recommends the vertical and horizontal devolution of taxes and grants-in-aid.', 8),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q10', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) primarily deals with:', 'Time-bound resolution of stressed assets', 'Income tax', 'Elections', 'Environmental clearances', 'A', 'The IBC, 2016 provides a time-bound framework for resolving insolvency of firms and individuals.', 9),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q11', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'The ''One Nation, One Election'' idea proposes simultaneous elections to:', 'Lok Sabha and State Assemblies', 'Only local bodies', 'Rajya Sabha only', 'Panchayats only', 'A', '''One Nation, One Election'' seeks to synchronise Lok Sabha and State Assembly elections.', 10),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news-q12', 'upsc-current-affairs-polity-and-economy-in-the-news', 'The Digital Personal Data Protection Act relates to:', 'Privacy and processing of personal data', 'Foreign trade', 'Agriculture', 'Defence procurement', 'A', 'The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 governs the processing of digital personal data and privacy.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Great Bath was found at which Indus site?', 'Mohenjo-daro', 'Harappa', 'Lothal', 'Kalibangan', 'A', 'The Great Bath, a large public water tank, was excavated at Mohenjo-daro.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Indus site with a dockyard, indicating maritime trade, is:', 'Lothal', 'Mohenjo-daro', 'Harappa', 'Dholavira', 'A', 'Lothal in Gujarat had a dockyard, evidence of the Harappans'' overseas trade.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Harappan civilisation belonged to the:', 'Bronze Age', 'Iron Age', 'Stone Age', 'Copper-Iron Age', 'A', 'The Indus Valley Civilisation was a Bronze Age urban culture.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-indus-valley-civilisation', 'The Harappan script is:', 'Undeciphered and pictographic', 'Based on Brahmi', 'Alphabetic like Greek', 'Deciphered as Sanskrit', 'A', 'The Indus script remains undeciphered; it appears pictographic and was written right to left.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'The Mauryan Empire was founded by:', 'Chandragupta Maurya', 'Ashoka', 'Bindusara', 'Bimbisara', 'A', 'Chandragupta Maurya founded the Mauryan Empire around 322 BCE with Chanakya''s guidance.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'The Arthashastra, a treatise on statecraft, was written by:', 'Kautilya (Chanakya)', 'Megasthenes', 'Kalidasa', 'Panini', 'A', 'Kautilya (Chanakya) authored the Arthashastra on economics, politics, and administration.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Ashoka embraced Buddhism after the:', 'Kalinga War', 'Battle of Hydaspes', 'Battle of Plassey', 'Kurukshetra War', 'A', 'The bloodshed of the Kalinga War led Ashoka to renounce war and adopt Buddhism (Dhamma).', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-mauryan-empire', 'Ashoka''s edicts were mostly written in which script?', 'Brahmi', 'Devanagari', 'Kharosthi only', 'Greek', 'A', 'Most Ashokan edicts are in the Brahmi script and Prakrit language (Kharosthi/Greek in the northwest).', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The Gupta period is often called the:', 'Golden Age of India', 'Dark Age', 'Iron Age', 'Age of Invasions', 'A', 'The Gupta era is called India''s Golden Age for its achievements in science, art, and literature.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The mathematician-astronomer who proposed that the Earth rotates on its axis was:', 'Aryabhata', 'Kalidasa', 'Varahamihira', 'Charaka', 'A', 'Aryabhata, of the Gupta age, proposed the Earth''s rotation and made key advances in mathematics and astronomy.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The great Sanskrit poet-dramatist of the Gupta court was:', 'Kalidasa', 'Banabhatta', 'Kabir', 'Tulsidas', 'A', 'Kalidasa, author of Abhijnanashakuntalam and Meghaduta, adorned the Gupta court.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-gupta-age', 'The Iron Pillar at Delhi, noted for rust resistance, dates to the ___ period.', 'Gupta', 'Mauryan', 'Mughal', 'Chola', 'A', 'The rust-resistant Iron Pillar (Mehrauli) reflects Gupta-era metallurgical skill.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The founder of Buddhism, Gautama Buddha, attained enlightenment at:', 'Bodh Gaya', 'Sarnath', 'Lumbini', 'Kushinagar', 'A', 'Gautama Buddha attained enlightenment under the Bodhi tree at Bodh Gaya.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The 24th and last Tirthankara of Jainism was:', 'Mahavira', 'Rishabhanatha', 'Parshvanatha', 'Gautama', 'A', 'Mahavira (Vardhamana) was the 24th Tirthankara who gave Jainism its final form.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The core principle of Jainism is:', 'Ahimsa (non-violence)', 'Idol worship', 'Animal sacrifice', 'Caste hierarchy', 'A', 'Jainism places supreme emphasis on ahimsa (non-violence) toward all living beings.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-buddhism-and-jainism', 'The ''Middle Path'' and the Four Noble Truths are teachings of:', 'Buddhism', 'Jainism', 'Sikhism', 'Zoroastrianism', 'A', 'The Buddha taught the Middle Path and the Four Noble Truths as the way to end suffering.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'The first ruler of the Delhi Sultanate (Slave/Mamluk dynasty) was:', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak', 'Iltutmish', 'Balban', 'Alauddin Khalji', 'A', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak founded the Slave (Mamluk) dynasty, beginning the Delhi Sultanate.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'Market (price) control regulations were introduced by:', 'Alauddin Khalji', 'Balban', 'Firoz Tughlaq', 'Iltutmish', 'A', 'Alauddin Khalji imposed famous market reforms to control prices and maintain a large army.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'The ruler who shifted the capital from Delhi to Daulatabad was:', 'Muhammad bin Tughlaq', 'Firoz Shah Tughlaq', 'Alauddin Khalji', 'Balban', 'A', 'Muhammad bin Tughlaq''s ill-fated transfer of capital to Daulatabad caused great hardship.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-delhi-sultanate', 'The Qutub Minar was begun by ___ and completed by Iltutmish.', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak', 'Balban', 'Alauddin Khalji', 'Firoz Tughlaq', 'A', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak began the Qutub Minar; Iltutmish completed it.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Mughal Empire was founded after the First Battle of Panipat (1526) by:', 'Babur', 'Akbar', 'Humayun', 'Aurangzeb', 'A', 'Babur defeated Ibrahim Lodi at Panipat in 1526, founding the Mughal Empire.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Din-i-Ilahi, a syncretic faith, was propounded by:', 'Akbar', 'Aurangzeb', 'Jahangir', 'Shah Jahan', 'A', 'Akbar founded Din-i-Ilahi, blending elements of various religions, as part of his liberal policy.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Taj Mahal was built by:', 'Shah Jahan', 'Akbar', 'Aurangzeb', 'Babur', 'A', 'Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal at Agra as a mausoleum for Mumtaz Mahal.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-mughal-empire', 'The Mughal emperor who reimposed the jizya tax was:', 'Aurangzeb', 'Akbar', 'Jahangir', 'Humayun', 'A', 'Aurangzeb reimposed the jizya (poll tax on non-Muslims) that Akbar had abolished.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The Bhakti and Sufi movements both emphasised:', 'Devotion and the unity of God', 'Ritual sacrifice', 'Caste hierarchy', 'Military conquest', 'A', 'Both movements stressed personal devotion, love of God, and social equality over ritualism.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'Kabir''s teachings emphasised:', 'Unity of Hindus and Muslims and one formless God', 'Idol worship', 'Caste divisions', 'Ritual pilgrimage', 'A', 'Kabir preached a formless God and the underlying unity of Hindu and Muslim paths.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The founder of Sikhism was:', 'Guru Nanak', 'Kabir', 'Ramanuja', 'Chaitanya', 'A', 'Guru Nanak founded Sikhism, preaching devotion to one God and equality.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-bhakti-and-sufi-movements', 'The Chishti Sufi order''s most famous saint in India was:', 'Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti', 'Shah Jahan', 'Tulsidas', 'Surdas', 'A', 'Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti of Ajmer was the leading saint of the Chishti Sufi order in India.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The Nagara style of temple architecture is associated with:', 'North India', 'South India', 'Deccan only', 'Bengal only', 'A', 'The Nagara (curvilinear shikhara) style developed in North India.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The Dravida style, marked by a gopuram and vimana, belongs to:', 'South India', 'North India', 'Central India', 'Kashmir', 'A', 'The Dravida style, with towering gopurams, is characteristic of South Indian temples.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The Sun Temple at Konark was built by the:', 'Eastern Ganga dynasty', 'Cholas', 'Pallavas', 'Mughals', 'A', 'The Konark Sun Temple (Odisha) was built by King Narasimhadeva I of the Eastern Ganga dynasty.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-temple-architecture', 'The Brihadeeswara Temple at Thanjavur was built by the:', 'Cholas', 'Pallavas', 'Chalukyas', 'Rashtrakutas', 'A', 'The Brihadeeswara (Rajarajeswara) Temple was built by Chola king Rajaraja I.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Bharatanatyam originated in which state?', 'Tamil Nadu', 'Kerala', 'Odisha', 'Manipur', 'A', 'Bharatanatyam, among the oldest classical dances, originated in Tamil Nadu.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Kathakali is a classical dance-drama from:', 'Kerala', 'Tamil Nadu', 'Andhra Pradesh', 'Assam', 'A', 'Kathakali, known for elaborate costumes and makeup, is from Kerala.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Kathak, with its Mughal-court influence, is associated with:', 'North India', 'Kerala', 'Odisha', 'Tamil Nadu', 'A', 'Kathak, a North Indian classical dance, flourished under Mughal and Rajput patronage.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-classical-dance-forms', 'Odissi dance originated in:', 'Odisha', 'Manipur', 'Kerala', 'Gujarat', 'A', 'Odissi, depicted in the sculptures of Odisha''s temples, originated in Odisha.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The Ajanta cave paintings mainly depict themes from:', 'Buddhism (Jataka tales)', 'Mughal court life', 'Rajput valour', 'Christianity', 'A', 'The Ajanta murals depict the life of the Buddha and Jataka tales.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The Mughal school of painting is noted for:', 'Court scenes, portraits, and fine miniatures', 'Abstract art', 'Cave frescoes', 'Folk motifs only', 'A', 'Mughal painting blended Persian and Indian styles in detailed court miniatures and portraits.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'Madhubani painting is a folk art from:', 'Bihar', 'Rajasthan', 'Bengal', 'Maharashtra', 'A', 'Madhubani (Mithila) painting is a traditional folk art of Bihar.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-painting-schools', 'The Pahari and Rajput (Rajasthani) schools often depicted:', 'Themes of Krishna, ragas, and romance', 'Industrial scenes', 'Sea voyages', 'Warfare only', 'A', 'Rajput and Pahari miniatures depicted Krishna legends, Ragamala, and romantic themes.', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q09', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'Project Tiger was launched in India in:', '1973', '1985', '2000', '1950', 'A', 'Project Tiger was launched in 1973 to conserve the Bengal tiger and its habitat.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q10', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'The IUCN Red List classifies species by their:', 'Conservation/extinction risk status', 'Economic value', 'Size', 'Colour', 'A', 'The IUCN Red List categorises species by extinction risk (e.g., Endangered, Vulnerable).', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q11', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'India has ___ biodiversity hotspots recognised globally.', 'Four', 'One', 'Ten', 'None', 'A', 'India has four biodiversity hotspots: the Himalayas, Western Ghats, Indo-Burma, and Sundaland (Nicobar).', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation-q12', 'upsc-environment-biodiversity-and-conservation', 'In-situ conservation includes:', 'National parks and wildlife sanctuaries', 'Zoos', 'Seed banks', 'Botanical gardens', 'A', 'In-situ conservation protects species in their natural habitat (parks, sanctuaries, biosphere reserves).', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q09', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Paris Agreement (2015) aims to limit global warming to well below:', '2°C above pre-industrial levels', '5°C', '10°C', '0°C', 'A', 'The Paris Agreement targets holding warming well below 2°C, pursuing efforts to limit it to 1.5°C.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q10', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Kyoto Protocol was aimed at reducing emissions of:', 'Greenhouse gases', 'CFCs only', 'Particulates', 'Noise', 'A', 'The Kyoto Protocol committed developed countries to reduce greenhouse-gas emissions.', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q11', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The Montreal Protocol protects the ozone layer by phasing out:', 'Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs)', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Methane', 'Nitrogen', 'A', 'The Montreal Protocol phases out ozone-depleting substances such as CFCs.', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements-q12', 'upsc-environment-climate-change-and-global-agreements', 'The UNFCCC''s annual climate summit is called the:', 'Conference of the Parties (COP)', 'General Assembly', 'G20 Summit', 'Security Council', 'A', 'The COP is the annual decision-making meeting of parties to the UNFCCC.', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q09', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'The flow of energy in an ecosystem is:', 'Unidirectional', 'Cyclic', 'Bidirectional', 'Absent', 'A', 'Energy flows one way through trophic levels, dissipating as heat, unlike cycling nutrients.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q10', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'According to the 10% law, energy transferred to the next trophic level is about:', '10%', '50%', '90%', '100%', 'A', 'Only about 10% of energy passes to the next trophic level (Lindeman''s ten-percent law).', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q11', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Organisms that break down dead matter and recycle nutrients are:', 'Decomposers', 'Producers', 'Primary consumers', 'Carnivores', 'A', 'Decomposers (bacteria, fungi) break down dead organic matter, recycling nutrients.', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains-q12', 'upsc-environment-ecosystems-and-food-chains', 'Biomagnification refers to the increasing concentration of a toxin:', 'At successive trophic levels', 'In water only', 'In soil only', 'In the atmosphere', 'A', 'Non-degradable toxins (e.g., DDT) accumulate and increase in concentration up the food chain.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'India''s first satellite, launched in 1975, was:', 'Aryabhata', 'Bhaskara', 'INSAT-1A', 'Chandrayaan-1', 'A', 'Aryabhata, India''s first satellite, was launched in 1975 (with Soviet help).', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'Chandrayaan missions are ISRO''s programme to explore the:', 'Moon', 'Mars', 'Sun', 'Venus', 'A', 'The Chandrayaan series are India''s lunar exploration missions.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'India''s Mars Orbiter Mission is popularly called:', 'Mangalyaan', 'Gaganyaan', 'Aditya', 'NavIC', 'A', 'Mangalyaan (Mars Orbiter Mission) made India the first nation to reach Mars orbit on its first attempt.', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-space-technology-isro', 'ISRO''s reliable workhorse launch vehicle for polar/sun-synchronous orbits is the:', 'PSLV', 'GSLV Mk III only', 'SLV-3', 'Ariane', 'A', 'The Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle (PSLV) is ISRO''s dependable workhorse for many launches.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'The molecule that carries genetic information is:', 'DNA', 'Protein', 'Lipid', 'Starch', 'A', 'DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) stores and transmits genetic information.', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'CRISPR-Cas9 is a technology used for:', 'Gene editing', 'Rocket propulsion', 'Water purification', 'Solar power', 'A', 'CRISPR-Cas9 is a precise gene-editing tool that can add, remove, or alter DNA sequences.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'Bt cotton is genetically engineered to be resistant to:', 'Insect pests', 'Drought', 'Herbicides only', 'Fungi', 'A', 'Bt cotton carries genes from Bacillus thuringiensis producing insecticidal proteins.', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-biotechnology-basics', 'The regulatory body approving genetically modified organisms in India is the:', 'GEAC', 'SEBI', 'RBI', 'TRAI', 'A', 'The Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee (GEAC) regulates GMOs in India.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The BrahMos is a ___ missile jointly developed by India and Russia.', 'Supersonic cruise', 'Ballistic', 'Surface-to-air only', 'Anti-tank', 'A', 'BrahMos is a supersonic cruise missile developed jointly by India and Russia.', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'The Agni series of missiles are:', 'Long-range ballistic missiles', 'Cruise missiles', 'Anti-tank guided missiles', 'Torpedoes', 'A', 'The Agni series are India''s medium-to-intercontinental range ballistic missiles.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'India''s premier defence R&D organisation is:', 'DRDO', 'ISRO', 'BARC', 'CSIR', 'A', 'The Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) develops India''s defence technology.', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-defence-technology-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-defence-technology', 'INS Vikrant is India''s first indigenously built:', 'Aircraft carrier', 'Submarine', 'Frigate', 'Destroyer', 'A', 'INS Vikrant is India''s first indigenously designed and built aircraft carrier.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'India''s ''Neighbourhood First'' policy prioritises relations with:', 'Immediate South Asian neighbours', 'European Union', 'Latin America', 'Africa only', 'A', '''Neighbourhood First'' prioritises close ties with India''s immediate South Asian neighbours.', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The Line of Actual Control (LAC) is the effective border between India and:', 'China', 'Pakistan', 'Nepal', 'Bangladesh', 'A', 'The LAC separates Indian-controlled territory from Chinese-controlled territory.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The Line of Control (LoC) separates India and Pakistan in:', 'Jammu & Kashmir', 'Punjab', 'Rajasthan', 'Gujarat', 'A', 'The LoC is the military control line between Indian- and Pakistani-administered Kashmir.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-its-neighbours', 'The 1960 treaty governing river-water sharing between India and Pakistan is the:', 'Indus Waters Treaty', 'Ganga Treaty', 'Farakka Accord', 'Tashkent Declaration', 'A', 'The Indus Waters Treaty (1960), brokered by the World Bank, allocates the Indus system rivers.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'BRICS comprises Brazil, Russia, India, China, and:', 'South Africa', 'Spain', 'Singapore', 'Saudi Arabia (original five)', 'A', 'The original BRICS grouping added South Africa to BRIC (later expanded with new members).', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'The Quad grouping includes India, the USA, Japan, and:', 'Australia', 'China', 'Russia', 'France', 'A', 'The Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (Quad) comprises India, the USA, Japan, and Australia.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'The G20 is a forum of major economies focused on:', 'Global economic cooperation', 'Military alliance', 'Space exploration', 'Cultural exchange', 'A', 'The G20 brings together major economies to coordinate on global economic and financial issues.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-major-global-groupings', 'SAARC is a regional grouping of countries in:', 'South Asia', 'Europe', 'Africa', 'the Americas', 'A', 'The South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC) unites eight South Asian nations.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The five permanent members of the UN Security Council are the USA, Russia, China, France, and:', 'United Kingdom', 'Germany', 'India', 'Japan', 'A', 'The P5 are the USA, Russia, China, France, and the United Kingdom, each with veto power.', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The World Trade Organization (WTO) deals with:', 'Rules of international trade', 'Global health', 'Refugees', 'Climate change', 'A', 'The WTO administers global trade rules and settles trade disputes.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The headquarters of the World Health Organization (WHO) is in:', 'Geneva', 'New York', 'Paris', 'Vienna', 'A', 'The WHO is headquartered in Geneva, Switzerland.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-important-international-organizations', 'The International Court of Justice (ICJ) is located at:', 'The Hague', 'Geneva', 'New York', 'London', 'A', 'The ICJ, the UN''s principal judicial organ, sits at The Hague in the Netherlands.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'India was a founding member of the ___ Movement during the Cold War.', 'Non-Aligned', 'Warsaw Pact', 'NATO', 'SEATO', 'A', 'India co-founded the Non-Aligned Movement, avoiding alignment with either Cold War bloc.', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'The ''Panchsheel'' agreement enunciated the five principles of:', 'Peaceful coexistence', 'Free trade', 'Nuclear disarmament', 'Collective defence', 'A', 'Panchsheel (1954) set out five principles of peaceful coexistence between India and China.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'Pravasi Bharatiya Divas is celebrated to honour the:', 'Indian diaspora', 'Freedom fighters', 'Scientists', 'Soldiers', 'A', 'Pravasi Bharatiya Divas (9 January) recognises the contribution of the overseas Indian community.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-indias-foreign-policy-and-diaspora', 'India''s ''Act East'' policy seeks closer ties with:', 'Southeast and East Asia', 'West Africa', 'Latin America', 'the Arctic', 'A', 'The Act East policy deepens strategic and economic engagement with Southeast and East Asia.', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q09', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Ethics is best described as the study of:', 'What is morally right and wrong', 'Legal statutes only', 'Economic efficiency', 'Physical laws', 'A', 'Ethics is the systematic study of moral rightness and wrongness of human conduct.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q10', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'Values that are considered universal, such as honesty and compassion, are called:', 'Core human values', 'Legal rules', 'Economic incentives', 'Local customs only', 'A', 'Core human values like honesty, compassion, and integrity are broadly shared across cultures.', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q11', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'The primary source of ethical values in early life is the:', 'Family and upbringing', 'Stock market', 'Legislature', 'Judiciary', 'A', 'Family and early socialisation are the foundational sources of a person''s values.', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface-q12', 'upsc-ethics-ethics-and-human-interface', 'The consistency between one''s beliefs, words, and actions reflects:', 'Integrity', 'Efficiency', 'Neutrality', 'Ambition', 'A', 'Integrity is the alignment of a person''s values, statements, and conduct.', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q09', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Emotional intelligence primarily involves the ability to:', 'Recognise and manage emotions (own and others'')', 'Solve equations', 'Memorise facts', 'Run fast', 'A', 'EI is the capacity to perceive, understand, and regulate emotions in oneself and others.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q10', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'An attitude is best defined as a:', 'Predisposition to respond in a certain way', 'Legal duty', 'Financial asset', 'Physical trait', 'A', 'An attitude is a learned tendency to respond favourably or unfavourably toward an object or idea.', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q11', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'The components of an attitude are commonly cognitive, behavioural, and:', 'Affective (emotional)', 'Financial', 'Physical', 'Legal', 'A', 'The ABC model: Affective (feelings), Behavioural (actions), and Cognitive (beliefs) components.', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence-q12', 'upsc-ethics-attitude-and-emotional-intelligence', 'Self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation, empathy, and social skills are the five components of EI according to:', 'Daniel Goleman', 'Abraham Maslow', 'Sigmund Freud', 'B. F. Skinner', 'A', 'Daniel Goleman popularised these five components of emotional intelligence.', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q09', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'The philosophy of ''the greatest good for the greatest number'' is:', 'Utilitarianism', 'Deontology', 'Virtue ethics', 'Nihilism', 'A', 'Utilitarianism (Bentham, Mill) judges actions by the aggregate happiness they produce.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q10', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Immanuel Kant''s ethics is based on:', 'Duty and the categorical imperative', 'Consequences alone', 'Pleasure maximisation', 'Self-interest', 'A', 'Kant''s deontology holds that morality rests on duty and universalisable maxims (the categorical imperative).', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q11', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Gandhi''s core ethical principles included truth (satya) and:', 'Non-violence (ahimsa)', 'Wealth accumulation', 'Militarism', 'Isolation', 'A', 'Gandhi''s ethics centred on satya (truth) and ahimsa (non-violence).', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers-q12', 'upsc-ethics-moral-thinkers-and-philosophers', 'Virtue ethics, focusing on character and virtues, is associated with:', 'Aristotle', 'Bentham', 'Kant', 'Machiavelli', 'A', 'Aristotle''s virtue ethics emphasises cultivating good character traits (the golden mean).', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q09', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Political neutrality in the civil service means officials should:', 'Serve any elected government impartially', 'Support one party', 'Contest elections', 'Ignore ministers', 'A', 'Political neutrality requires civil servants to serve the government of the day impartially.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q10', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Accountability in public service means being:', 'Answerable for one''s actions and decisions', 'Free of all rules', 'Anonymous', 'Above the law', 'A', 'Accountability is the obligation to answer for the exercise of one''s responsibilities.', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q11', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Objectivity as a civil-service value requires decisions based on:', 'Evidence and merit, free of bias', 'Personal preference', 'Bribes', 'Political pressure', 'A', 'Objectivity means basing advice and decisions on evidence and merit without bias.', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values-q12', 'upsc-ethics-public-civil-service-values', 'Empathy in public administration involves:', 'Understanding citizens'' needs and perspectives', 'Ignoring the poor', 'Favouring elites', 'Strict rule-following only', 'A', 'Empathy enables administrators to understand and respond compassionately to citizens'' needs.', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q09', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'Probity in governance essentially means:', 'Integrity and uprightness in public office', 'Speed of files', 'Higher taxation', 'Secrecy', 'A', 'Probity is adherence to the highest standards of honesty and integrity in public life.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q10', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'The Right to Information Act promotes:', 'Transparency and accountability', 'Official secrecy', 'Higher fees', 'Judicial delay', 'A', 'The RTI Act, 2005 empowers citizens to seek information, enhancing transparency and accountability.', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q11', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'A ''conflict of interest'' arises when a public servant''s ___ clashes with public duty.', 'Personal interest', 'Salary', 'Office location', 'Uniform', 'A', 'A conflict of interest occurs when personal interests could improperly influence official duties.', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance-q12', 'upsc-ethics-probity-in-governance', 'A code of conduct for public servants primarily aims to:', 'Guide ethical behaviour and standards', 'Increase pay', 'Reduce work', 'Grant immunity', 'A', 'A code of conduct lays down expected standards of ethical behaviour for public servants.', 11),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q09', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'In an ethics case study, the first step is usually to:', 'Identify the ethical dilemma and stakeholders', 'Punish someone', 'Resign', 'Ignore the issue', 'A', 'One should first identify the dilemma, the stakeholders, and the values in conflict.', 8),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q10', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'A good resolution of an ethical dilemma should be:', 'Legally sound, ethical, and practical', 'Only self-serving', 'Secretive', 'Illegal but fast', 'A', 'The best option balances legality, ethics, and practicality while serving the public interest.', 9),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q11', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', 'When a rule conflicts with the public interest, an official should:', 'Weigh options and seek a lawful, ethical course', 'Always break the rule', 'Always ignore the public', 'Take a bribe', 'A', 'The official should analyse alternatives and choose a lawful course that best serves the public good.', 10),
  ('upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach-q12', 'upsc-ethics-case-studies-approach', '''Whistleblowing'' refers to:', 'Reporting wrongdoing in an organisation', 'Delaying files', 'Accepting gifts', 'Avoiding work', 'A', 'Whistleblowing is disclosing unethical or illegal conduct within an organisation.', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q09', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'E-governance primarily aims to make service delivery more:', 'Efficient, transparent, and citizen-friendly', 'Secretive', 'Expensive', 'Slow', 'A', 'E-governance uses ICT to make public services efficient, transparent, and accessible.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q10', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'The ''G2C'' in e-governance stands for:', 'Government to Citizen', 'Government to Corporate', 'Global to Central', 'Grant to Community', 'A', 'G2C denotes government-to-citizen electronic service delivery.', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q11', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'Aadhaar is primarily a system of:', 'Unique biometric digital identity', 'Land records', 'Voter registration only', 'Passport issuance', 'A', 'Aadhaar provides a unique 12-digit biometric-linked digital identity used for service delivery.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance-q12', 'upsc-governance-governance-and-e-governance', 'Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) aims to:', 'Transfer subsidies directly to beneficiaries'' bank accounts', 'Increase paperwork', 'Delay payments', 'Remove subsidies', 'A', 'DBT routes subsidies and benefits straight into beneficiaries'' accounts, reducing leakage.', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q09', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'The RTI Act was enacted in:', '2005', '2013', '1999', '2016', 'A', 'The Right to Information Act was enacted in 2005.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q10', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'The apex appellate authority under the RTI Act is the:', 'Central Information Commission', 'Supreme Court', 'Lok Sabha', 'RBI', 'A', 'The Central Information Commission is the top appellate body under the RTI Act at the central level.', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q11', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'A Lokpal is an institution to inquire into allegations of ___ against public functionaries.', 'Corruption', 'Tax evasion by citizens', 'Traffic violations', 'Cricket matches', 'A', 'The Lokpal (and Lokayuktas) inquire into corruption allegations against public functionaries.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability-q12', 'upsc-governance-transparency-rti-and-accountability', 'Social audit is a tool for:', 'Community monitoring of public schemes', 'Financial trading', 'Military review', 'Space research', 'A', 'Social audit lets citizens review and verify the implementation of public programmes (e.g., MGNREGA).', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q09', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'Reservation for SCs and STs in India is a form of:', 'Affirmative action', 'Taxation', 'Trade policy', 'Foreign aid', 'A', 'Reservation is affirmative action to uplift historically disadvantaged Scheduled Castes and Tribes.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q10', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The National Commission for Scheduled Castes is a:', 'Constitutional body', 'Private NGO', 'Foreign body', 'Judicial court', 'A', 'The National Commission for SCs is a constitutional body under Article 338.', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q11', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The ICDS scheme mainly targets:', 'Children (0–6) and mothers (nutrition, health)', 'College students', 'Farmers only', 'Industrial workers', 'A', 'Integrated Child Development Services provides nutrition, health, and pre-school care to young children and mothers.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections-q12', 'upsc-governance-welfare-schemes-and-vulnerable-sections', 'The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act (2016) increased the number of recognised disabilities to:', '21', '7', '40', '10', 'A', 'The RPwD Act, 2016 expanded the list of recognised disabilities from 7 to 21.', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q09', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The Right to Education is a Fundamental Right under which article?', 'Article 21A', 'Article 19', 'Article 32', 'Article 14', 'A', 'Article 21A (86th Amendment) makes free and compulsory education for children aged 6–14 a Fundamental Right.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q10', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The National Education Policy 2020 recommends a ___ curricular structure.', '5+3+3+4', '10+2', '8+4', '6+6', 'A', 'NEP 2020 introduced the 5+3+3+4 school structure replacing the 10+2 system.', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q11', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'Ayushman Bharat''s health and wellness centres aim to strengthen:', 'Primary healthcare', 'Space research', 'Defence', 'Taxation', 'A', 'Health and Wellness Centres under Ayushman Bharat strengthen comprehensive primary healthcare.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources-q12', 'upsc-governance-health-education-and-human-resources', 'The ''demographic dividend'' refers to growth potential from a:', 'Large working-age population', 'Small population', 'Ageing population', 'High death rate', 'A', 'The demographic dividend is the economic boost from a rising share of working-age people.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'Left-Wing Extremism in India is also known as:', 'Naxalism', 'Insurgency in the northeast', 'Cross-border terrorism', 'Cyber warfare', 'A', 'Left-Wing Extremism (Naxalism/Maoism) affects parts of central and eastern India.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'The nodal ministry for internal security in India is the:', 'Ministry of Home Affairs', 'Ministry of Defence', 'Ministry of External Affairs', 'Ministry of Finance', 'A', 'The Ministry of Home Affairs is responsible for India''s internal security.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'The National Investigation Agency (NIA) chiefly investigates:', 'Terrorism-related offences', 'Income tax fraud', 'Traffic violations', 'Land disputes', 'A', 'The NIA is India''s central counter-terrorism agency investigating terror-related crimes.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-internal-security-challenges', 'AFSPA, often debated in security policy, stands for the:', 'Armed Forces (Special Powers) Act', 'Air Force Special Purpose Act', 'All-Force Support Act', 'Army Financial Services Act', 'A', 'AFSPA grants special powers to the armed forces in ''disturbed areas''.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'Money laundering is the process of:', 'Making illegally obtained money appear legitimate', 'Printing currency', 'Paying taxes', 'Opening bank branches', 'A', 'Money laundering disguises the origins of illegally gained money to make it appear lawful.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'The law to combat money laundering in India is the:', 'Prevention of Money Laundering Act (PMLA)', 'RTI Act', 'IPC only', 'FEMA only', 'A', 'The PMLA, 2002 is India''s principal anti-money-laundering law, enforced by the ED.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'CERT-In is India''s nodal agency for:', 'Cyber security incident response', 'Election management', 'Tax collection', 'Space launches', 'A', 'CERT-In (Indian Computer Emergency Response Team) coordinates responses to cyber-security incidents.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-cyber-security-and-money-laundering', 'The global watchdog against money laundering and terror financing is the:', 'FATF', 'WTO', 'WHO', 'UNESCO', 'A', 'The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) sets standards against money laundering and terror financing.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The force that guards the India–Pakistan and India–Bangladesh borders is the:', 'Border Security Force (BSF)', 'CRPF', 'ITBP', 'CISF', 'A', 'The BSF is the primary force guarding the India–Pakistan and India–Bangladesh borders.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The Indo-Tibetan Border Police (ITBP) guards the border with:', 'China', 'Pakistan', 'Nepal', 'Myanmar', 'A', 'The ITBP guards the India–China border along the Himalayas.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'The Sashastra Seema Bal (SSB) guards India''s borders with:', 'Nepal and Bhutan', 'Pakistan', 'China', 'Bangladesh', 'A', 'The SSB guards the open India–Nepal and India–Bhutan borders.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-border-management-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-border-management', 'Coastal security in India is primarily the responsibility of the ___ and the Navy.', 'Indian Coast Guard', 'BSF', 'ITBP', 'SSB', 'A', 'The Indian Coast Guard, alongside the Navy and marine police, handles coastal security.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The apex body for disaster management in India is the:', 'National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA)', 'RBI', 'NITI Aayog', 'Election Commission', 'A', 'The NDMA, chaired by the Prime Minister, is the apex body for disaster management.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The specialised force for disaster response in India is the:', 'NDRF', 'BSF', 'CRPF', 'ITBP', 'A', 'The National Disaster Response Force (NDRF) is the specialised force for disaster response.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'Earthquakes are measured for magnitude on the:', 'Richter (moment magnitude) scale', 'Beaufort scale', 'pH scale', 'Celsius scale', 'A', 'Earthquake magnitude is measured on the Richter/moment magnitude scale.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-disaster-management-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-disaster-management', 'The Sendai Framework is an international agreement on:', 'Disaster risk reduction', 'Trade', 'Climate finance only', 'Nuclear arms', 'A', 'The Sendai Framework (2015–2030) guides global disaster risk reduction efforts.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The Early Vedic (Rig Vedic) people are associated with which region?', 'Sapta Sindhu (land of seven rivers)', 'The Deccan plateau', 'The Gangetic delta', 'The Malabar coast', 'A', 'The Rig Vedic Aryans lived in the Sapta Sindhu region of Punjab and the north-west.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The oldest of the four Vedas is the:', 'Sama Veda', 'Rig Veda', 'Yajur Veda', 'Atharva Veda', 'B', 'The Rig Veda, a collection of hymns, is the oldest Vedic (and Indo-Aryan) text.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The two tribal assemblies of the Rig Vedic polity were the:', 'Sabha and Samiti', 'Ur and Sabha', 'Mahasabha and Nagaram', 'Gana and Sangha', 'A', 'The Sabha and Samiti were the key tribal assemblies advising the raja.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The chief measure of wealth in Rig Vedic society was:', 'Land', 'Cattle (gau)', 'Gold coins', 'Slaves', 'B', 'Cattle were the main form of wealth; many words for war meant ''search for cattle''.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The most frequently invoked deity in the Rig Veda is:', 'Vishnu', 'Shiva', 'Indra', 'Brahma', 'C', 'Indra, god of war and rain, has the most hymns addressed to him in the Rig Veda.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'In the Later Vedic period, the centre of activity shifted to the:', 'Ganga–Yamuna doab', 'Indus valley', 'Coromandel coast', 'Kashmir valley', 'A', 'The Later Vedic people moved east into the fertile Ganga–Yamuna doab.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The philosophical texts that form the concluding part of the Vedas are the:', 'Puranas', 'Upanishads', 'Dharmashastras', 'Smritis', 'B', 'The Upanishads (Vedanta) are the philosophical culmination of Vedic literature.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The national motto ''Satyameva Jayate'' is taken from the:', 'Rig Veda', 'Mundaka Upanishad', 'Bhagavad Gita', 'Arthashastra', 'B', '''Satyameva Jayate'' (Truth alone triumphs) comes from the Mundaka Upanishad.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The technology that spread widely in the Later Vedic period, aiding expansion, was:', 'Bronze casting', 'Iron (krishna ayas)', 'Steam power', 'Gunpowder', 'B', 'Iron (''krishna ayas'', black metal) enabled forest clearing and farming in the doab.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The great royal sacrifices such as Rajasuya and Ashvamedha became prominent in the:', 'Harappan period', 'Later Vedic period', 'Sangam Age', 'Gupta period', 'B', 'Later Vedic kings performed elaborate sacrifices to assert power and status.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'Which Veda deals mainly with magic, charms, and everyday life?', 'Atharva Veda', 'Rig Veda', 'Sama Veda', 'Yajur Veda', 'A', 'The Atharva Veda contains spells and charms reflecting popular beliefs.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-vedic-age', 'The Sama Veda is significant because it is the source of Indian:', 'Music', 'Medicine', 'Mathematics', 'Architecture', 'A', 'The Sama Veda, set to melody for chanting, is regarded as the root of Indian music.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'How many Mahajanapadas are listed in Buddhist texts like the Anguttara Nikaya?', '16', '8', '12', '24', 'A', 'The Buddhist tradition names sixteen (Solasa) Mahajanapadas of the 6th century BCE.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The Vajji confederacy is an example of a Mahajanapada that was a:', 'Monarchy', 'Republic (gana-sangha)', 'Theocracy', 'Colony', 'B', 'The Vajji (Lichchhavi) confederacy was a republic or gana-sangha, not a monarchy.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The earliest capital of Magadha was:', 'Pataliputra', 'Rajgir (Girivraja)', 'Ujjain', 'Taxila', 'B', 'Magadha''s first capital was Rajgir (Girivraja); it later shifted to Pataliputra.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'Which Haryanka ruler is known for a policy of matrimonial alliances to expand Magadha?', 'Bimbisara', 'Ashoka', 'Kanishka', 'Chandragupta II', 'A', 'Bimbisara used marriage alliances with Kosala, Vaishali, and others to expand Magadha.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'Ajatashatru is best known for defeating the:', 'Vajji confederacy', 'Cholas', 'Kushanas', 'Satavahanas', 'A', 'Ajatashatru waged a long war and defeated the Vajjis (Lichchhavis) of Vaishali.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The dynasty overthrown by Chandragupta Maurya was the:', 'Nanda dynasty', 'Shunga dynasty', 'Gupta dynasty', 'Pallava dynasty', 'A', 'Chandragupta Maurya, aided by Chanakya, overthrew the Nanda dynasty around 321 BCE.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The 6th century BCE urban growth in the Ganga valley is called the:', 'First urbanisation', 'Second urbanisation', 'Green revolution', 'Iron collapse', 'B', 'This period is the ''second urbanisation'' (the first being the Harappan cities).', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The characteristic coins of the Mahajanapada period were:', 'Punch-marked coins', 'Gold dinars', 'Paper notes', 'Cowrie shells only', 'A', 'Silver and copper punch-marked coins were the earliest coinage of this era.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'Which powerful Mahajanapada had Ujjain as an important centre?', 'Avanti', 'Anga', 'Gandhara', 'Kamboja', 'A', 'Avanti, with centres at Ujjain and Mahishmati, was among the strongest Mahajanapadas.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'The founder of the Nanda dynasty is generally taken to be:', 'Mahapadma Nanda', 'Bindusara', 'Bimbisara', 'Pushyamitra', 'A', 'Mahapadma Nanda founded the powerful Nanda dynasty of Magadha.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'Which geographical advantage helped Magadha''s rise?', 'Fertile land, iron ore, and elephants', 'Desert isolation', 'Coastal trade only', 'Mountain barriers', 'A', 'Fertile Gangetic soil, nearby iron mines, timber, and war-elephants powered Magadha.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-mahajanapadas', 'Two heterodox religions that arose in this age were:', 'Buddhism and Jainism', 'Sikhism and Islam', 'Christianity and Zoroastrianism', 'Shaivism and Vaishnavism', 'A', 'Buddhism and Jainism emerged in the 6th century BCE amid the Mahajanapadas.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The general who founded the Shunga dynasty by killing the last Maurya was:', 'Pushyamitra Shunga', 'Vasudeva Kanva', 'Simuka', 'Kanishka', 'A', 'Pushyamitra Shunga killed the last Maurya, Brihadratha, in 185 BCE.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The greatest ruler of the Satavahana dynasty was:', 'Gautamiputra Satakarni', 'Rudradaman I', 'Menander', 'Kanishka', 'A', 'Gautamiputra Satakarni was the most powerful Satavahana ruler.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Kushana king associated with the Shaka era (78 CE) is:', 'Kanishka I', 'Ashoka', 'Chandragupta I', 'Kadphises', 'A', 'Kanishka I is traditionally linked with the start of the Shaka era in 78 CE.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Fourth Buddhist Council was convened under the patronage of:', 'Ashoka', 'Kanishka', 'Harsha', 'Ajatashatru', 'B', 'Kanishka convened the Fourth Buddhist Council in Kashmir, promoting Mahayana.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Gandhara school of art shows strong influence of:', 'Greco-Roman (Hellenistic) styles', 'Chinese styles', 'Egyptian styles', 'Sumerian styles', 'A', 'Gandhara art blended Greco-Roman techniques with Buddhist themes.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Indo-Greek rulers were the first in India to issue:', 'Gold coins and portrait coins', 'Paper money', 'Iron coins', 'Cowrie currency', 'A', 'The Indo-Greeks introduced die-struck gold coins bearing rulers'' portraits.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Junagadh rock inscription in Sanskrit was issued by the Shaka ruler:', 'Rudradaman I', 'Nahapana', 'Menander', 'Kanishka', 'A', 'Rudradaman I''s Junagadh inscription is the first long inscription in chaste Sanskrit.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Milindapanho records a dialogue between the monk Nagasena and the Indo-Greek king:', 'Menander (Milinda)', 'Demetrius', 'Seleucus', 'Antiochus', 'A', 'The Milindapanho is a dialogue between Nagasena and King Menander (Milinda).', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Satavahanas issued coins primarily made of:', 'Lead and potin', 'Pure gold', 'Platinum', 'Paper', 'A', 'The Satavahanas commonly issued lead and potin coins.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The Kushana capital Purushapura corresponds to modern:', 'Peshawar', 'Patna', 'Lahore', 'Mathura', 'A', 'Purushapura, the Kushana capital, is modern Peshawar in Pakistan.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'Kanishka was a great patron of which branch of Buddhism?', 'Mahayana', 'Theravada only', 'Vajrayana', 'None', 'A', 'Kanishka patronised Mahayana Buddhism, which spread to Central Asia and China.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-post-mauryan-age', 'The post-Mauryan centuries saw flourishing long-distance trade along the:', 'Silk Route', 'Grand Trunk Road only', 'Suez Canal', 'Trans-Siberian route', 'A', 'The Silk Route linked India to Central Asia, China, and Rome in this period.', 11),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q01', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'Sangam literature was composed primarily in which language?', 'Sanskrit', 'Tamil', 'Prakrit', 'Telugu', 'B', 'Sangam literature is the earliest body of classical Tamil poetry.', 0),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q02', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The three ruling dynasties of the Sangam Age were the Cheras, Cholas, and:', 'Pandyas', 'Pallavas', 'Chalukyas', 'Rashtrakutas', 'A', 'The muvendar — Cheras, Cholas, and Pandyas — ruled the Tamil country.', 1),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q03', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The Sangam assemblies of poets were held under the patronage of the:', 'Pandyas at Madurai', 'Cholas at Thanjavur', 'Cheras at Vanji', 'Pallavas at Kanchi', 'A', 'The Pandya kings of Madurai are traditionally credited with hosting the sangams.', 2),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q04', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The Tolkappiyam, the earliest Tamil text, is a work on:', 'Grammar and poetics', 'Medicine', 'Astronomy', 'Warfare', 'A', 'The Tolkappiyam is the oldest Tamil grammar and treatise on poetics.', 3),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q05', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The royal emblem of the Cholas was the:', 'Tiger', 'Fish', 'Bow', 'Lion', 'A', 'The tiger was the Chola emblem; the Pandyas used the fish and Cheras the bow.', 4),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q06', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The capital of the Pandyas was:', 'Madurai', 'Uraiyur', 'Vanji', 'Kanchipuram', 'A', 'Madurai was the Pandya capital; Uraiyur was Chola and Vanji was Chera.', 5),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q07', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'Sangam-age trade with which empire brought large quantities of gold coins to South India?', 'The Roman Empire', 'The Chinese Empire', 'The Persian Empire', 'The Mauryan Empire', 'A', 'Brisk trade with Rome (spices, pearls, muslin) brought Roman gold to the Tamil ports.', 6),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q08', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The Tamil epic Silappadikaram was authored by:', 'Ilango Adigal', 'Sittalai Sattanar', 'Tiruvalluvar', 'Kamban', 'A', 'Silappadikaram (''the tale of the anklet'') is attributed to Ilango Adigal.', 7),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q09', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'Memorial stones honouring fallen heroes in the Sangam age were called:', 'Nadukal (hero-stones)', 'Stupas', 'Menhirs', 'Rathas', 'A', 'Nadukal or hero-stones commemorated warriors who died in battle.', 8),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q10', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The famous Chola king of the Sangam age, credited with building embankments on the Kaveri, was:', 'Karikala', 'Rajaraja I', 'Senguttuvan', 'Nedunjeliyan', 'A', 'Karikala Chola is celebrated in Sangam poetry and linked with Kaveri irrigation works.', 9),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q11', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'The important Chola port town of the Sangam age was:', 'Puhar (Kaveripattinam)', 'Tamralipti', 'Bharuch', 'Sopara', 'A', 'Puhar/Kaveripattinam was the great Chola port described in Sangam literature.', 10),
  ('upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age-q12', 'upsc-ancient-history-sangam-age', 'Sangam poems classify land into ecological zones known as:', 'Tinai', 'Janapada', 'Vishaya', 'Ahara', 'A', 'The tinai concept divided the landscape into five poetic/ecological zones.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Brihadeeswarar temple at Thanjavur was built by:', 'Rajaraja Chola I', 'Rajendra Chola I', 'Krishnadevaraya', 'Narasimhavarman I', 'A', 'Rajaraja Chola I built the Brihadeeswarar (Rajarajeshwara) temple, a UNESCO site.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'Which Chola king led a famous naval expedition to Srivijaya in Southeast Asia?', 'Rajendra Chola I', 'Rajaraja Chola I', 'Kulottunga I', 'Vijayalaya', 'A', 'Rajendra Chola I sent a naval expedition against Srivijaya, showing Chola sea power.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Uttaramerur inscriptions are famous for describing Chola:', 'Local self-government / village assemblies', 'Naval battles', 'Coinage', 'Temple rituals only', 'A', 'The Uttaramerur inscriptions detail the working of elected village assemblies (sabha).', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'Chola bronze sculpture is most iconically represented by the figure of:', 'Nataraja (dancing Shiva)', 'Buddha', 'Mahavira', 'Vishnu Anantasayana', 'A', 'The dancing Shiva (Nataraja) is the masterpiece of Chola bronze art.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Pallava rock-cut monuments and shore temple are located at:', 'Mahabalipuram', 'Thanjavur', 'Hampi', 'Halebidu', 'A', 'The Pallavas created the rock-cut rathas and shore temple at Mahabalipuram.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Chalukya king who defeated Harshavardhana was:', 'Pulakeshin II', 'Mangalesha', 'Kirtivarman', 'Vikramaditya VI', 'A', 'Pulakeshin II of Badami checked Harsha''s advance to the Deccan, per the Aihole inscription.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The magnificent Kailasa temple at Ellora was carved by the:', 'Rashtrakutas', 'Cholas', 'Pandyas', 'Hoysalas', 'A', 'The Rashtrakuta king Krishna I had the monolithic Kailasa temple at Ellora carved.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Chola capital was:', 'Thanjavur', 'Madurai', 'Kanchipuram', 'Badami', 'A', 'Thanjavur (Tanjore) was the imperial Chola capital.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'Chola temple architecture belongs to which broad style?', 'Dravidian', 'Nagara', 'Vesara', 'Indo-Saracenic', 'A', 'Chola temples, with tall pyramidal vimanas, epitomise the Dravidian style.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Pallava ruler who defeated the Chalukyas and took the title ''Vatapikonda'' was:', 'Narasimhavarman I', 'Mahendravarman II', 'Nandivarman', 'Simhavishnu', 'A', 'Narasimhavarman I captured the Chalukya capital Vatapi, earning ''Vatapikonda''.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'The Hoysala kingdom is known for its ornate temples at Belur and:', 'Halebidu', 'Konark', 'Khajuraho', 'Modhera', 'A', 'The Hoysalas built star-shaped, intricately carved temples at Belur and Halebidu.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-cholas-and-south-india', 'Chola village assemblies used which method to elect members, per Uttaramerur?', 'Kudavolai (drawing lots from a pot)', 'Hereditary succession', 'Nomination by the king', 'Purchase of office', 'A', 'The kudavolai system drew palm-leaf ballots from a pot to select committee members.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The Vijayanagara Empire was founded in 1336 by:', 'Harihara and Bukka', 'Krishnadevaraya', 'Alauddin Bahman Shah', 'Mahmud Gawan', 'A', 'Brothers Harihara and Bukka of the Sangama dynasty founded Vijayanagara in 1336.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The capital of the Vijayanagara Empire was:', 'Hampi', 'Bidar', 'Golconda', 'Gulbarga', 'A', 'Hampi (Vijayanagara) on the Tungabhadra was the empire''s magnificent capital.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The greatest Vijayanagara ruler, of the Tuluva dynasty, was:', 'Krishnadevaraya', 'Harihara II', 'Deva Raya I', 'Rama Raya', 'A', 'Krishnadevaraya (r. 1509–29) marked the empire''s zenith in power and culture.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'Krishnadevaraya wrote the Telugu classic:', 'Amuktamalyada', 'Prithviraj Raso', 'Rajatarangini', 'Gita Govinda', 'A', 'Krishnadevaraya authored the Telugu poem Amuktamalyada and patronised the ''ashtadiggajas''.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The 1565 battle that led to Vijayanagara''s decline was the Battle of:', 'Talikota', 'Panipat', 'Plassey', 'Haldighati', 'A', 'The Battle of Talikota (1565) saw a Deccan-sultanate coalition crush Vijayanagara.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The Bahmani Sultanate was founded in 1347 by:', 'Alauddin Bahman Shah', 'Mahmud Gawan', 'Yusuf Adil Shah', 'Quli Qutb Shah', 'A', 'Alauddin Bahman Shah (Hasan Gangu) founded the Bahmani Sultanate in the Deccan.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The famous reforming prime minister of the Bahmani kingdom was:', 'Mahmud Gawan', 'Todar Mal', 'Chanakya', 'Birbal', 'A', 'Mahmud Gawan, a Persian minister, reformed the Bahmani administration and finances.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The Bahmani kingdom later broke up into how many Deccan Sultanates?', 'Five', 'Three', 'Seven', 'Two', 'A', 'It fragmented into five Deccan Sultanates: Bijapur, Golconda, Ahmadnagar, Bidar, Berar.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The Gol Gumbaz, famous for its whispering gallery, is at Bijapur and was built by the:', 'Adil Shahi dynasty', 'Qutb Shahi dynasty', 'Nizam Shahi dynasty', 'Sangama dynasty', 'A', 'The Gol Gumbaz is the tomb of Adil Shahi ruler Mohammed Adil Shah at Bijapur.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'The Charminar in Hyderabad was built by the:', 'Qutb Shahi dynasty', 'Adil Shahi dynasty', 'Tughlaqs', 'Cholas', 'A', 'The Charminar was built by Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah of Golconda in 1591.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'Foreign travellers Nicolo Conti and Abdur Razzaq described the wealth of:', 'Vijayanagara (Hampi)', 'Delhi', 'Agra', 'Bengal', 'A', 'Conti, Razzaq, and Paes left vivid accounts of prosperous Vijayanagara.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-vijayanagara-and-bahmani', 'Vijayanagara and the Bahmani kingdom fought recurrently over the fertile:', 'Raichur doab', 'Ganga delta', 'Malwa plateau', 'Konkan coast', 'A', 'The Raichur doab between the Krishna and Tungabhadra was long contested.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The founder of the Maratha Empire, crowned Chhatrapati in 1674, was:', 'Shivaji', 'Baji Rao I', 'Shahu', 'Balaji Vishwanath', 'A', 'Shivaji was crowned Chhatrapati at Raigad in 1674, founding the Maratha state.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'Shivaji''s council of eight ministers was called the:', 'Ashtapradhan', 'Diwan-i-Am', 'Ashtadiggaja', 'Navaratna', 'A', 'The Ashtapradhan was Shivaji''s council of eight ministers, headed by the Peshwa.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The taxes levied by the Marathas on neighbouring territories were chauth and:', 'Sardeshmukhi', 'Jizya', 'Zakat', 'Khums', 'A', 'Chauth (one-fourth of revenue) and sardeshmukhi (an extra 10%) funded the Maratha state.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'Shivaji''s capital fort was:', 'Raigad', 'Sinhagad', 'Purandar', 'Panhala', 'A', 'Raigad served as Shivaji''s capital and coronation site.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'After Shivaji, effective power passed to hereditary prime ministers called the:', 'Peshwas', 'Nawabs', 'Subedars', 'Diwans', 'A', 'The Peshwas (Chitpavan Brahmins based at Pune) became the real rulers of the empire.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The Peshwa who greatly expanded Maratha power across India was:', 'Baji Rao I', 'Balaji Baji Rao', 'Madhav Rao II', 'Narayan Rao', 'A', 'Baji Rao I (r. 1720–40) expanded Maratha influence deep into north India.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'In the Maratha confederacy, the Scindia family was based at:', 'Gwalior', 'Indore', 'Baroda', 'Nagpur', 'A', 'The Scindias ruled from Gwalior; Holkars from Indore, Gaekwads from Baroda, Bhonsles from Nagpur.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The Third Battle of Panipat (1761) was fought between the Marathas and:', 'Ahmad Shah Abdali (Durrani)', 'The British', 'The Mughals', 'The Portuguese', 'A', 'The Marathas suffered a heavy defeat by Ahmad Shah Abdali at Panipat in 1761.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'Shivaji''s guerrilla warfare tactics were known as:', 'Ganimi kava', 'Blitzkrieg', 'Chakravyuha', 'Fabian strategy', 'A', 'Shivaji perfected ''ganimi kava'', hit-and-run guerrilla warfare suited to the hills.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The Maratha Empire finally ended after the:', 'Third Anglo-Maratha War (1818)', 'Battle of Plassey', 'First Anglo-Sikh War', 'Revolt of 1857', 'A', 'The Third Anglo-Maratha War (1817–18) ended Maratha power and the Peshwa''s rule.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'The first Peshwa to make the office powerful and hereditary was:', 'Balaji Vishwanath', 'Baji Rao II', 'Nana Saheb', 'Raghunath Rao', 'A', 'Balaji Vishwanath consolidated the Peshwa office under Chhatrapati Shahu.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-maratha-empire', 'Shivaji escaped from the captivity of which Mughal emperor at Agra in 1666?', 'Aurangzeb', 'Akbar', 'Jahangir', 'Shah Jahan', 'A', 'Shivaji famously escaped from Aurangzeb''s court at Agra in 1666.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The sea route to India via the Cape of Good Hope was discovered in 1498 by:', 'Vasco da Gama', 'Christopher Columbus', 'Ferdinand Magellan', 'Bartolomeu Dias', 'A', 'Vasco da Gama, a Portuguese explorer, reached Calicut in 1498.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The English East India Company was chartered by Queen Elizabeth I in:', '1600', '1757', '1526', '1858', 'A', 'The English East India Company received its royal charter in 1600.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The Battle of Plassey (1757) was won for the British by:', 'Robert Clive', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Cornwallis', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'A', 'Robert Clive defeated Siraj-ud-Daulah at Plassey, aided by Mir Jafar''s treachery.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The Nawab of Bengal defeated at the Battle of Plassey was:', 'Siraj-ud-Daulah', 'Mir Jafar', 'Mir Qasim', 'Alivardi Khan', 'A', 'Siraj-ud-Daulah was defeated at Plassey; Mir Jafar was installed as a puppet Nawab.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The Battle of Buxar (1764) established British supremacy over the combined forces of Mir Qasim, the Nawab of Awadh, and:', 'Mughal emperor Shah Alam II', 'The Marathas', 'Tipu Sultan', 'The Nizam', 'A', 'At Buxar the British defeated Mir Qasim, Shuja-ud-Daulah, and Shah Alam II together.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The Diwani of Bengal, Bihar, and Odisha was granted to the Company by the Treaty of:', 'Allahabad (1765)', 'Bassein', 'Salbai', 'Seringapatam', 'A', 'The 1765 Treaty of Allahabad gave the Company Diwani (revenue) rights over Bengal, Bihar, Odisha.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The decisive battle by which the English ended French ambitions in India was the Battle of:', 'Wandiwash (1760)', 'Plassey', 'Panipat', 'Buxar', 'A', 'At Wandiwash (1760) the English defeated the French, ending the Carnatic wars in their favour.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The ''Subsidiary Alliance'' system was introduced by:', 'Lord Wellesley', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Ripon', 'A', 'Lord Wellesley used the Subsidiary Alliance to bring Indian states under British control.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The ''Doctrine of Lapse'' to annex states without a natural heir was applied by:', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'Lord Canning', 'Lord Curzon', 'Lord Minto', 'A', 'Lord Dalhousie annexed states like Satara, Jhansi, and Nagpur under the Doctrine of Lapse.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The Portuguese governor who established Goa as their Indian base was:', 'Alfonso de Albuquerque', 'Francisco de Almeida', 'Vasco da Gama', 'Pedro Cabral', 'A', 'Alfonso de Albuquerque captured Goa in 1510, making it the Portuguese headquarters.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'Which European power was the last to arrive but first to establish, and last to leave, territory in India?', 'The Portuguese', 'The Dutch', 'The Danes', 'The French', 'A', 'The Portuguese came first (1498) and left last (Goa liberated in 1961).', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-advent-of-europeans', 'The dual system of government in Bengal (Company revenue, Nawab administration) was established by:', 'Robert Clive', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Cornwallis', 'Lord Wellesley', 'A', 'Clive''s ''dual government'' (1765) split power between Company and Nawab; Hastings ended it.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The ''Drain of Wealth'' theory was most notably expounded by:', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak', 'M. K. Gandhi', 'Subhas Bose', 'A', 'Dadabhai Naoroji articulated the drain theory in ''Poverty and Un-British Rule in India''.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The Permanent Settlement of 1793 in Bengal was introduced by:', 'Lord Cornwallis', 'Thomas Munro', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Ripon', 'A', 'Lord Cornwallis introduced the Permanent Settlement, fixing revenue with zamindars.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The Ryotwari system, settling revenue directly with cultivators, was associated with:', 'Thomas Munro', 'Cornwallis', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Wellesley', 'A', 'Thomas Munro (and Reed) developed the Ryotwari system in Madras and Bombay.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The decline of Indian handicrafts under British trade policy is called:', 'Deindustrialisation', 'Commercialisation', 'Urbanisation', 'Monetisation', 'A', 'One-way free trade ruined Indian handicrafts, a process termed deindustrialisation.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The land-revenue system prevalent in most of northern India was the:', 'Mahalwari system', 'Ryotwari system', 'Permanent Settlement', 'Jagirdari system', 'A', 'The Mahalwari system settled revenue with the village (mahal) in north India.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The famous book ''Poverty and Un-British Rule in India'' was written by:', 'Dadabhai Naoroji', 'R. C. Dutt', 'Gopal Krishna Gokhale', 'M. G. Ranade', 'A', 'Dadabhai Naoroji, the ''Grand Old Man of India'', wrote this on the economic drain.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The first railway line in India (1853) ran between:', 'Bombay and Thane', 'Calcutta and Delhi', 'Madras and Bangalore', 'Howrah and Raniganj', 'A', 'India''s first passenger railway ran from Bombay to Thane in 1853.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The forced cultivation that led to the Indigo Revolt (1859) affected peasants in:', 'Bengal', 'Punjab', 'Madras', 'Gujarat', 'A', 'The Indigo Revolt of 1859–60 protested oppressive forced indigo cultivation in Bengal.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'Under British rule, India was primarily converted into a:', 'Supplier of raw materials and a market for finished goods', 'Leading industrial exporter', 'Self-sufficient closed economy', 'Global financial hub', 'A', 'Colonial policy made India export raw materials and import British manufactures.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', '''Home Charges'' in the drain theory referred to:', 'Payments made in Britain out of Indian revenues', 'Household taxes in India', 'Charges for postal services', 'Municipal taxes', 'A', 'Home Charges were expenses (pensions, interest, salaries) paid in Britain from Indian revenue.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'The shift of Indian agriculture to cash crops for the market is called:', 'Commercialisation of agriculture', 'Collectivisation', 'Land reform', 'Consolidation', 'A', 'The British encouraged commercialisation, pushing farmers toward cash crops like cotton and indigo.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-economic-impact-of-british-rule', 'Recurrent famines under British rule were worsened by:', 'High revenue demand and export of food grains', 'Overproduction of food', 'Excessive irrigation', 'Land redistribution', 'A', 'Heavy revenue extraction and grain exports intensified famine mortality.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The first Governor-General of Bengal was:', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Cornwallis', 'Robert Clive', 'Lord Wellesley', 'A', 'Warren Hastings became the first Governor-General of Bengal in 1774.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'Sati was legally abolished in 1829 by:', 'Lord William Bentinck', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'Lord Curzon', 'Lord Ripon', 'A', 'Lord William Bentinck, with Raja Ram Mohan Roy''s support, abolished Sati in 1829.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'Lord Cornwallis is often called the ''father of'' which service?', 'The civil service in India', 'The Indian Army', 'The Indian Railways', 'The police force', 'A', 'Cornwallis reformed and organised the Company''s civil service, earning that title.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'Railways, telegraph, and the modern Post Office in India were introduced under:', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'Warren Hastings', 'Lord Ripon', 'Lord Minto', 'A', 'Lord Dalhousie introduced railways, the telegraph, and a modern postal system.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'After 1858, the Governor-General was also designated as the:', 'Viceroy', 'Prime Minister', 'President', 'Secretary of State', 'A', 'The Government of India Act 1858 made the Governor-General also the Viceroy (Crown''s representative).', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The first Viceroy of India was:', 'Lord Canning', 'Lord Curzon', 'Lord Ripon', 'Lord Mayo', 'A', 'Lord Canning, in office during the 1857 revolt, became the first Viceroy in 1858.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The Partition of Bengal in 1905 was carried out by:', 'Lord Curzon', 'Lord Minto', 'Lord Hardinge', 'Lord Ripon', 'A', 'Lord Curzon partitioned Bengal in 1905, sparking the Swadeshi movement.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'Separate electorates for Muslims were introduced by the Morley-Minto Reforms of:', '1909', '1919', '1935', '1892', 'A', 'The Indian Councils Act 1909 (Morley-Minto) introduced separate communal electorates.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'Lord Ripon is remembered for the Resolution on:', 'Local self-government (1882)', 'Partition of Bengal', 'The Doctrine of Lapse', 'The Rowlatt Act', 'A', 'Lord Ripon, the ''father of local self-government'', passed the 1882 resolution.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The Jallianwala Bagh massacre (1919) occurred during the viceroyalty of:', 'Lord Chelmsford', 'Lord Reading', 'Lord Irwin', 'Lord Curzon', 'A', 'The 1919 massacre took place under Viceroy Lord Chelmsford (General Dyer ordered firing).', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The Government of India Act 1858 transferred power from the Company to the:', 'British Crown', 'Indian National Congress', 'Provincial legislatures', 'The Mughal emperor', 'A', 'The 1858 Act ended Company rule and vested Indian governance in the British Crown.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-governor-generals-and-administration', 'The last Viceroy of India, who oversaw the transfer of power in 1947, was:', 'Lord Mountbatten', 'Lord Wavell', 'Lord Linlithgow', 'Lord Willingdon', 'A', 'Lord Mountbatten was the last Viceroy and presided over Partition and independence.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The Quit India Movement was launched in:', '1942', '1930', '1919', '1946', 'A', 'Gandhi launched the Quit India Movement in August 1942 with the call ''Do or Die''.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'Gandhi''s famous slogan during the Quit India Movement was:', 'Do or Die', 'Inquilab Zindabad', 'Swaraj is my birthright', 'Jai Hind', 'A', '''Do or Die'' (Karo ya Maro) was Gandhi''s call during the 1942 movement.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The Cripps Mission (1942) offer was famously described by Gandhi as:', 'A post-dated cheque', 'A magna carta', 'A blank cheque', 'A fair deal', 'A', 'Gandhi called the Cripps offer ''a post-dated cheque on a crashing bank''.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The Indian National Army (INA) was reorganised and led by:', 'Subhas Chandra Bose', 'Bhagat Singh', 'Chandra Shekhar Azad', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'A', 'Subhas Chandra Bose revitalised the INA with the slogan ''Give me blood, I will give you freedom''.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The Muslim League observed ''Direct Action Day'' on 16 August 1946 to demand:', 'Pakistan', 'Dominion status', 'A united India', 'Separate electorates only', 'A', 'Direct Action Day pressed the demand for Pakistan and triggered communal riots in Calcutta.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The Cabinet Mission came to India in:', '1946', '1942', '1935', '1947', 'A', 'The Cabinet Mission (1946) proposed a federal plan and framework for a Constituent Assembly.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The plan that finally accepted the partition of India was announced on 3 June 1947 by:', 'Lord Mountbatten', 'Lord Wavell', 'Stafford Cripps', 'Clement Attlee', 'A', 'The Mountbatten Plan (3 June 1947) set out the terms for partition and transfer of power.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The boundary line dividing India and Pakistan was drawn by:', 'Cyril Radcliffe', 'Louis Mountbatten', 'Cyril Jackson', 'Stafford Cripps', 'A', 'The Radcliffe Line, drawn by Sir Cyril Radcliffe, partitioned Punjab and Bengal.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'India became independent on:', '15 August 1947', '26 January 1950', '26 January 1930', '2 October 1947', 'A', 'India gained independence on 15 August 1947 under the Indian Independence Act.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The integration of over 560 princely states into India was led chiefly by:', 'Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Rajendra Prasad', 'Maulana Azad', 'A', 'Sardar Patel, with V. P. Menon, integrated the princely states into the Indian Union.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The 1946 mutiny that shook British confidence was the:', 'Royal Indian Navy (RIN) mutiny', 'Barrackpore mutiny', 'Vellore mutiny', 'Meerut mutiny', 'A', 'The 1946 RIN naval ratings'' mutiny in Bombay signalled crumbling British authority.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-towards-independence-and-partition', 'The legislation that created the two dominions of India and Pakistan was the:', 'Indian Independence Act 1947', 'Government of India Act 1935', 'Regulating Act 1773', 'Rowlatt Act 1919', 'A', 'The Indian Independence Act 1947 partitioned British India into India and Pakistan.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q01', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The innermost layer of the Earth, composed mainly of iron and nickel, is the:', 'Crust', 'Mantle', 'Core', 'Asthenosphere', 'C', 'The core (NIFE — nickel and iron) is the Earth''s innermost layer.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q02', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'Which seismic waves cannot pass through liquids, proving the outer core is liquid?', 'P-waves', 'S-waves', 'L-waves', 'Sound waves', 'B', 'S-waves travel only through solids; their shadow zone shows the outer core is liquid.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q03', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The boundary between the crust and the mantle is the:', 'Mohorovicic discontinuity', 'Gutenberg discontinuity', 'Lehmann discontinuity', 'Conrad discontinuity', 'A', 'The Mohorovicic (Moho) discontinuity separates the crust from the mantle.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q04', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The theory of continental drift was proposed by:', 'Alfred Wegener', 'Harry Hess', 'Charles Darwin', 'James Hutton', 'A', 'Alfred Wegener proposed continental drift and the supercontinent Pangaea.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q05', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The Himalayas were formed by the collision of the Indian plate with the:', 'Eurasian plate', 'Pacific plate', 'African plate', 'Nazca plate', 'A', 'The Himalayas are fold mountains from the Indian–Eurasian plate convergence.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q06', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'New oceanic crust is created at which type of plate boundary?', 'Divergent boundary', 'Convergent boundary', 'Transform boundary', 'Passive margin', 'A', 'At divergent boundaries (mid-ocean ridges), magma rises and forms new crust.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q07', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The zone with the world''s most intense volcanic and earthquake activity is the:', 'Pacific Ring of Fire', 'Mid-Atlantic Ridge only', 'Sahara belt', 'Great Rift Valley only', 'A', 'The Pacific ''Ring of Fire'' has the highest concentration of volcanoes and quakes.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q08', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The San Andreas Fault is an example of which plate boundary?', 'Transform (conservative)', 'Divergent', 'Convergent', 'Subduction', 'A', 'The San Andreas Fault is a transform boundary where plates slide past each other.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q09', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'Sea-floor spreading was proposed by:', 'Harry Hess', 'Alfred Wegener', 'Arthur Holmes', 'Charles Lyell', 'A', 'Harry Hess proposed sea-floor spreading, supporting plate tectonics.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q10', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'The plastic layer of the upper mantle on which plates move is the:', 'Asthenosphere', 'Lithosphere', 'Barysphere', 'Stratosphere', 'A', 'Plates of the lithosphere ride on the semi-molten asthenosphere.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q11', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'Deep ocean trenches are typically formed at:', 'Convergent (subduction) boundaries', 'Divergent boundaries', 'Transform faults', 'Continental shields', 'A', 'Subduction of one plate under another at convergent boundaries creates trenches.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics-q12', 'upsc-geography-geomorphology-and-plate-tectonics', 'A volcano that has not erupted in recorded history but may erupt again is termed:', 'Dormant', 'Active', 'Extinct', 'Shield', 'A', 'A dormant (''sleeping'') volcano is currently inactive but capable of erupting again.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q01', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'The lowest atmospheric layer, where all weather occurs, is the:', 'Troposphere', 'Stratosphere', 'Mesosphere', 'Thermosphere', 'A', 'The troposphere is the weather layer, where temperature falls with height.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q02', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'The ozone layer that absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation lies in the:', 'Stratosphere', 'Troposphere', 'Exosphere', 'Mesosphere', 'A', 'The ozone layer is in the stratosphere and shields the surface from UV rays.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q03', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Meteors typically burn up in which atmospheric layer?', 'Mesosphere', 'Troposphere', 'Stratosphere', 'Exosphere', 'A', 'The mesosphere is the coldest layer, where most meteors burn on entry.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q04', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'The apparent deflection of winds due to the Earth''s rotation is the:', 'Coriolis force', 'Centrifugal force', 'Gravitational force', 'Frictional force', 'A', 'The Coriolis force deflects winds right in the N. Hemisphere and left in the S.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q05', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Winds that blow from the subtropical high toward the equatorial low are the:', 'Trade winds', 'Westerlies', 'Polar easterlies', 'Monsoons', 'A', 'The trade winds blow from subtropical highs toward the equator.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q06', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Rainfall caused by air rising over mountains is called:', 'Orographic (relief) rainfall', 'Convectional rainfall', 'Cyclonic rainfall', 'Frontal rainfall', 'A', 'Orographic rainfall occurs when moist air is forced up over mountains and cools.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q07', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Tropical cyclones are known as ''typhoons'' in which region?', 'The China Sea / western Pacific', 'The Atlantic', 'The Indian Ocean', 'Australia', 'A', 'They are called typhoons in the western Pacific and hurricanes in the Atlantic.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q08', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'The hot, dry local wind of northern India in summer is the:', 'Loo', 'Chinook', 'Foehn', 'Mistral', 'A', 'The Loo is a hot, dry summer wind of the northern Indian plains.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q09', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'The layer that reflects radio waves back to Earth (aiding communication) is the:', 'Ionosphere (thermosphere)', 'Troposphere', 'Stratosphere', 'Exosphere', 'A', 'The ionosphere reflects radio waves, enabling long-distance radio communication.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q10', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Incoming solar radiation received by the Earth is called:', 'Insolation', 'Albedo', 'Radiation fog', 'Terrestrial radiation', 'A', 'Insolation is the incoming solar radiation reaching the Earth''s surface.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q11', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Feathery, high-altitude ice clouds are called:', 'Cirrus', 'Cumulus', 'Stratus', 'Nimbus', 'A', 'Cirrus clouds are wispy, high-altitude clouds made of ice crystals.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds-q12', 'upsc-geography-climatology-atmosphere-and-winds', 'Atmospheric pressure with increasing altitude generally:', 'Decreases', 'Increases', 'Stays constant', 'Doubles', 'A', 'Air pressure decreases with altitude as the overlying air column shrinks.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q01', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The shallow, gently sloping margin of a continent under the sea is the:', 'Continental shelf', 'Continental slope', 'Abyssal plain', 'Oceanic trench', 'A', 'The continental shelf is shallow, rich in fish, and holds most offshore petroleum.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q02', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The deepest known point in the oceans is the:', 'Mariana Trench', 'Puerto Rico Trench', 'Java Trench', 'Peru-Chile Trench', 'A', 'The Mariana Trench (Challenger Deep) in the Pacific is the deepest ocean point.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q03', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The warm ocean current off the eastern coast of North America is the:', 'Gulf Stream', 'Labrador Current', 'Benguela Current', 'Humboldt Current', 'A', 'The warm Gulf Stream flows north along eastern North America and warms NW Europe.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q04', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'Spring tides, the highest tides, occur when the Sun, Moon, and Earth are:', 'Aligned (new/full moon)', 'At right angles', 'Farthest apart', 'In an eclipse only', 'A', 'Spring tides occur at new and full moon when Sun and Moon pull in a line.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q05', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'Rich fishing grounds like the Grand Banks form where:', 'Warm and cold currents meet', 'Rivers dry up', 'Trenches deepen', 'Salinity is highest', 'A', 'The mixing of warm and cold currents brings nutrients, creating rich fisheries.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q06', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The average salinity of ocean water is about:', '35 parts per thousand', '3.5 parts per thousand', '350 parts per thousand', '10 parts per thousand', 'A', 'Ocean water averages about 35 ppt (grams of salt per kilogram of water).', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q07', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The periodic warming of the eastern Pacific that disrupts the Indian monsoon is:', 'El Niño', 'La Niña', 'The Gulf Stream', 'The Humboldt Current', 'A', 'El Niño (warming of the eastern Pacific) is often linked with weak Indian monsoons.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q08', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'Neap tides, the lowest tides, occur during the:', 'First and third quarter moons', 'Full moon', 'New moon', 'Solar eclipse', 'A', 'Neap tides occur at quarter moons when Sun and Moon pull at right angles.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q09', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The cold current along the western coast of South America is the:', 'Humboldt (Peru) Current', 'Gulf Stream', 'Kuroshio Current', 'Agulhas Current', 'A', 'The cold Humboldt (Peru) Current flows along western South America.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q10', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The highest salinity is found in which of the following?', 'The Dead Sea', 'The Baltic Sea', 'The mouth of the Amazon', 'The Arctic Ocean', 'A', 'Enclosed, highly evaporating water bodies like the Dead Sea have extreme salinity.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q11', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'Ocean currents are set in motion primarily by:', 'Prevailing winds (and temperature/salinity differences)', 'Earthquakes', 'Tsunamis', 'River discharge only', 'A', 'Surface currents are driven mainly by prevailing winds, modified by Coriolis and density.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-oceanography-q12', 'upsc-geography-oceanography', 'The daily rise and fall of sea level caused by gravitational pull is called:', 'Tides', 'Currents', 'Waves', 'Upwelling', 'A', 'Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level due to lunar and solar gravity.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q01', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'India''s richest mineral belt is the:', 'Chota Nagpur plateau', 'Thar desert', 'Indo-Gangetic plain', 'Konkan coast', 'A', 'The Chota Nagpur plateau (Jharkhand–Odisha–Chhattisgarh) is India''s mineral heartland.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q02', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'The bulk of India''s coal reserves are of which geological type?', 'Gondwana coal', 'Tertiary coal', 'Anthracite', 'Peat', 'A', 'Most Indian coal is Gondwana coal, found in the Damodar, Son, and Mahanadi valleys.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q03', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'India''s oldest oil field, in Assam, is:', 'Digboi', 'Mumbai High', 'Bombay High', 'Ankleshwar', 'A', 'Digboi in Assam is India''s oldest oil field, operational since the 19th century.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q04', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'Bauxite is the chief ore for producing:', 'Aluminium', 'Iron', 'Copper', 'Zinc', 'A', 'Bauxite is refined into alumina and then smelted into aluminium.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q05', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'India''s leading offshore oil producer is:', 'Mumbai High', 'Digboi', 'Neyveli', 'Singareni', 'A', 'Mumbai High, off the Maharashtra coast, is India''s largest offshore oil field.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q06', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'The monazite sands of Kerala are an important source of:', 'Thorium', 'Uranium only', 'Gold', 'Diamond', 'A', 'Kerala''s monazite sands hold thorium, central to India''s three-stage nuclear programme.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q07', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'The Bhakra-Nangal multipurpose project is built on the river:', 'Sutlej', 'Mahanadi', 'Damodar', 'Krishna', 'A', 'The Bhakra-Nangal project is on the Sutlej river in Punjab/Himachal.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q08', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'The Hirakud dam, one of the world''s longest, is on the river:', 'Mahanadi', 'Godavari', 'Narmada', 'Kaveri', 'A', 'The Hirakud dam in Odisha is built across the Mahanadi river.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q09', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'India is a world leader in the production of which mineral used in electrical insulation?', 'Mica', 'Gold', 'Petroleum', 'Nickel', 'A', 'India has long been a leading producer of mica, valued for electrical insulation.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q10', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'Lignite (brown coal) is mined chiefly at:', 'Neyveli (Tamil Nadu)', 'Jharia (Jharkhand)', 'Raniganj (West Bengal)', 'Korba (Chhattisgarh)', 'A', 'Neyveli in Tamil Nadu is India''s main lignite (brown coal) mining centre.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q11', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'The Kudankulam nuclear power plant is located in:', 'Tamil Nadu', 'Gujarat', 'Rajasthan', 'Maharashtra', 'A', 'The Kudankulam nuclear plant is in Tamil Nadu, built with Russian cooperation.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals-q12', 'upsc-geography-indian-resources-and-minerals', 'Nehru famously called multipurpose river valley projects the:', '''Temples of modern India''', '''Lungs of the nation''', '''Arteries of trade''', '''Engines of growth''', 'A', 'Nehru called large dams and river valley projects the ''temples of modern India''.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q01', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'According to the 2011 Census, India''s sex ratio was about:', '943 females per 1000 males', '1000 females per 1000 males', '850 females per 1000 males', '990 females per 1000 males', 'A', 'The 2011 Census recorded a sex ratio of 943 females per 1000 males.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q02', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The Indian state with the highest literacy rate is:', 'Kerala', 'Bihar', 'Uttar Pradesh', 'Rajasthan', 'A', 'Kerala consistently has the highest literacy rate among Indian states.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q03', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The Tata Iron and Steel Company (TISCO) is located at:', 'Jamshedpur', 'Bhilai', 'Rourkela', 'Bokaro', 'A', 'TISCO, India''s first major steel plant, is at Jamshedpur (Jharkhand).', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q04', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The ''demographic dividend'' refers to the growth potential from:', 'A large working-age population', 'A shrinking population', 'An ageing population', 'High mortality', 'A', 'The demographic dividend is the economic boost from a rising working-age share.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q05', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The black cotton (regur) soil of the Deccan is best suited for growing:', 'Cotton', 'Tea', 'Rice', 'Coffee', 'A', 'Black (regur) soil retains moisture and is ideal for cotton cultivation.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q06', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The Hooghly industrial region is historically famous for which industry?', 'Jute', 'Cotton textiles', 'Automobiles', 'Petrochemicals', 'A', 'The Hooghly belt around Kolkata is the centre of India''s jute industry.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q07', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'India''s Silicon Valley, a hub of the IT industry, is:', 'Bengaluru', 'Kanpur', 'Ludhiana', 'Surat', 'A', 'Bengaluru (Bangalore) is India''s leading information-technology hub.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q08', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The tea-growing region concentrated in the north-east of India is:', 'Assam', 'Punjab', 'Gujarat', 'Haryana', 'A', 'Assam is India''s largest tea-producing region, along with the Nilgiris in the south.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q09', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'Jawaharlal Nehru Port (JNPT), India''s largest container port, is near:', 'Mumbai', 'Chennai', 'Kolkata', 'Kochi', 'A', 'JNPT (Nhava Sheva) near Mumbai is India''s largest container-handling port.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q10', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'In the demographic transition model, India is broadly in:', 'Stage III (falling birth and death rates)', 'Stage I (high birth and death rates)', 'Stage V (declining population)', 'Stage IV only', 'A', 'India is largely in Stage III, with both birth and death rates declining.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q11', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The steel plant at Bhilai is located in the state of:', 'Chhattisgarh', 'Odisha', 'Jharkhand', 'West Bengal', 'A', 'The Bhilai Steel Plant (SAIL) is in Chhattisgarh; Rourkela is in Odisha.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography-q12', 'upsc-geography-economic-and-population-geography', 'The wheat-growing heartland of India is the:', 'North-western plains (Punjab, Haryana, western UP)', 'Eastern coastal plains', 'Deccan plateau', 'North-eastern hills', 'A', 'The fertile, irrigated north-western plains are India''s wheat bowl.', 11),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q01', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The Prime Meridian (0° longitude) passes through:', 'Greenwich', 'Paris', 'Washington', 'Delhi', 'A', 'The Prime Meridian passes through Greenwich, London.', 0),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q02', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The Tropic of Cancer lies at a latitude of:', '23.5° North', '23.5° South', '66.5° North', '0°', 'A', 'The Tropic of Cancer is at 23.5° North; the Tropic of Capricorn is at 23.5° South.', 1),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q03', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The largest hot desert in the world is the:', 'Sahara', 'Gobi', 'Thar', 'Kalahari', 'A', 'The Sahara in North Africa is the world''s largest hot desert.', 2),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q04', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The temperate grasslands of North America are called the:', 'Prairies', 'Steppes', 'Pampas', 'Velds', 'A', 'The Prairies are North America''s temperate grasslands; Steppes are in Eurasia.', 3),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q05', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The Suez Canal connects the Mediterranean Sea with the:', 'Red Sea', 'Black Sea', 'Caspian Sea', 'Arabian Sea', 'A', 'The Suez Canal links the Mediterranean and Red Seas, shortening Europe–Asia trade.', 4),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q06', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'Indian Standard Time (IST) is based on the meridian passing at:', '82.5° East', '0°', '90° East', '75° East', 'A', 'IST is set to 82.5°E (near Mirzapur), 5 hours 30 minutes ahead of GMT.', 5),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q07', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The temperate grasslands of South America are the:', 'Pampas', 'Prairies', 'Downs', 'Savanna', 'A', 'The Pampas are South America''s grasslands; the Downs are in Australia.', 6),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q08', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The Strait of Malacca is a key shipping route between the Indian Ocean and the:', 'Pacific Ocean (South China Sea)', 'Atlantic Ocean', 'Arctic Ocean', 'Mediterranean Sea', 'A', 'The Strait of Malacca links the Indian Ocean with the South China Sea/Pacific.', 7),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q09', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The world''s largest continent by area is:', 'Asia', 'Africa', 'North America', 'Europe', 'A', 'Asia is the largest continent both in area and population.', 8),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q10', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The 180° meridian roughly corresponds to the:', 'International Date Line', 'Prime Meridian', 'Equator', 'Tropic of Capricorn', 'A', 'The International Date Line roughly follows the 180° meridian in the Pacific.', 9),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q11', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'Mediterranean-type climate regions are characterised by:', 'Dry summers and wet winters', 'Wet summers and dry winters', 'Year-round rainfall', 'No rainfall at all', 'A', 'Mediterranean climates have hot dry summers and mild wet winters.', 10),
  ('upsc-geography-world-regional-geography-q12', 'upsc-geography-world-regional-geography', 'The Panama Canal connects the Atlantic Ocean with the:', 'Pacific Ocean', 'Indian Ocean', 'Arctic Ocean', 'Mediterranean Sea', 'A', 'The Panama Canal links the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans across Central America.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The melodic framework of Indian classical music is called:', 'Raga', 'Tala', 'Kriti', 'Gharana', 'A', 'A raga is the melodic mode; tala is the rhythmic cycle.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The rhythmic cycle in Indian classical music is known as:', 'Tala', 'Raga', 'Alap', 'Sur', 'A', 'Tala is the metrical/rhythmic cycle marked by beats.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'Indian music traces its origins to which Veda?', 'Samaveda', 'Rigveda', 'Yajurveda', 'Atharvaveda', 'A', 'The Samaveda, meant for melodic chanting, is the root of Indian music.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The oldest and most austere form of Hindustani vocal music is:', 'Dhrupad', 'Khayal', 'Thumri', 'Ghazal', 'A', 'Dhrupad is the oldest, most austere genre of Hindustani classical vocal music.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The legendary musician in Akbar''s court was:', 'Tansen', 'Amir Khusrau', 'Baiju Bawra', 'Swami Haridas', 'A', 'Tansen, one of Akbar''s Navaratnas, was a legendary Hindustani musician.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The main composition form of Carnatic music is the:', 'Kriti', 'Khayal', 'Dhrupad', 'Tarana', 'A', 'The kriti is the principal composition form in Carnatic music.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'Tyagaraja, Muthuswami Dikshitar, and Syama Sastri are known as the:', 'Trinity of Carnatic music', 'Trinity of Hindustani music', 'Tansen''s disciples', 'Bhakti poets', 'A', 'They are revered as the Trinity of Carnatic music.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'Which instrument did Pandit Ravi Shankar make world-famous?', 'Sitar', 'Tabla', 'Shehnai', 'Veena', 'A', 'Ravi Shankar was a globally renowned sitar maestro.', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The shehnai is most associated with which maestro?', 'Bismillah Khan', 'Zakir Hussain', 'Hariprasad Chaurasia', 'Amjad Ali Khan', 'A', 'Ustad Bismillah Khan was the doyen of the shehnai.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The veena and mridangam are chiefly instruments of which tradition?', 'Carnatic music', 'Hindustani music', 'Sufi qawwali', 'Folk music', 'A', 'The veena and mridangam are central to Carnatic music.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The 72 ''melakarta'' system is used to classify ragas in:', 'Carnatic music', 'Hindustani music', 'Western classical music', 'Folk music', 'A', 'The melakarta system organises the parent ragas of Carnatic music.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-indian-music', 'The Baul tradition is a folk music form from:', 'Bengal', 'Punjab', 'Rajasthan', 'Kerala', 'A', 'The Baul are mystic minstrels of Bengal, recognised by UNESCO.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The epic Ramayana is traditionally attributed to:', 'Valmiki', 'Vyasa', 'Kalidasa', 'Tulsidas', 'A', 'Valmiki composed the Sanskrit Ramayana; Vyasa is credited with the Mahabharata.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The play Abhijnana Shakuntalam was written by:', 'Kalidasa', 'Banabhatta', 'Bhasa', 'Sudraka', 'A', 'Kalidasa, the great Sanskrit poet-dramatist, wrote Abhijnana Shakuntalam.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The Arthashastra, a treatise on statecraft, was written by:', 'Kautilya (Chanakya)', 'Kalidasa', 'Panini', 'Patanjali', 'A', 'Kautilya (Chanakya) authored the Arthashastra on polity and economy.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'How many languages are listed in the Eighth Schedule of the Constitution?', '22', '14', '18', '28', 'A', 'The Eighth Schedule currently lists 22 scheduled languages.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The first language to be granted ''Classical Language'' status in India (2004) was:', 'Tamil', 'Sanskrit', 'Telugu', 'Kannada', 'A', 'Tamil was the first to be declared a Classical Language of India in 2004.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'Rabindranath Tagore won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1913 for:', 'Gitanjali', 'Gora', 'The Home and the World', 'Kabuliwala', 'A', 'Tagore won the 1913 Nobel Prize for his collection of poems Gitanjali.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'India''s highest literary award is the:', 'Jnanpith Award', 'Bharat Ratna', 'Padma Shri', 'Sahitya Ratna', 'A', 'The Jnanpith Award is India''s highest literary honour.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The Bhagavad Gita is a part of which epic?', 'Mahabharata', 'Ramayana', 'Raghuvamsa', 'Meghaduta', 'A', 'The Bhagavad Gita is a dialogue within the Mahabharata (Bhishma Parva).', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The Ramcharitmanas, a Hindi (Awadhi) retelling of the Ramayana, was written by:', 'Tulsidas', 'Surdas', 'Kabir', 'Mirabai', 'A', 'Tulsidas wrote the Ramcharitmanas in the Awadhi dialect.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The early Buddhist canonical texts were composed largely in which language?', 'Pali', 'Sanskrit', 'Persian', 'Tamil', 'A', 'The Theravada Buddhist canon (Tripitaka) was composed in Pali.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'Amir Khusrau, credited with developing Hindavi and qawwali, was a disciple of the Sufi saint:', 'Nizamuddin Auliya', 'Moinuddin Chishti', 'Baba Farid', 'Salim Chishti', 'A', 'Amir Khusrau was a devoted disciple of Nizamuddin Auliya of Delhi.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-literature-and-languages', 'The two official languages of the Union Government of India are:', 'Hindi and English', 'Hindi and Sanskrit', 'English and Urdu', 'Hindi and Tamil', 'A', 'Hindi (in Devanagari) is the official language; English is the associate official language.', 11),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q01', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The Taj Mahal, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is located in:', 'Agra', 'Delhi', 'Fatehpur Sikri', 'Jaipur', 'A', 'The Taj Mahal, built by Shah Jahan, is in Agra, Uttar Pradesh.', 0),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q02', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The Ajanta and Ellora caves are located in which state?', 'Maharashtra', 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Karnataka', 'Odisha', 'A', 'The Ajanta and Ellora rock-cut caves are in Maharashtra.', 1),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q03', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The Sun Temple, a UNESCO site famous for its chariot form, is at:', 'Konark', 'Khajuraho', 'Hampi', 'Modhera', 'A', 'The Konark Sun Temple in Odisha is designed as the Sun God''s chariot.', 2),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q04', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The Kumbh Mela, inscribed on UNESCO''s Intangible Heritage list, rotates among how many cities?', 'Four', 'Two', 'Six', 'Eight', 'A', 'The Kumbh Mela rotates among Prayagraj, Haridwar, Ujjain, and Nashik.', 3),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q05', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Onam is the harvest festival primarily of which state?', 'Kerala', 'Tamil Nadu', 'Assam', 'Punjab', 'A', 'Onam is Kerala''s major harvest festival, marked by the Vamana-Mahabali legend.', 4),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q06', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Bihu is a set of festivals celebrated in:', 'Assam', 'Odisha', 'Gujarat', 'Karnataka', 'A', 'Bihu comprises the seasonal festivals of Assam.', 5),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q07', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The famous Pushkar Camel Fair is held in:', 'Rajasthan', 'Gujarat', 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Haryana', 'A', 'The Pushkar Fair, a major livestock and cultural fair, is held in Rajasthan.', 6),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q08', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Which of these was inscribed as a UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of India in 2016?', 'Yoga', 'The Taj Mahal', 'Kaziranga', 'Hampi', 'A', 'Yoga was inscribed on UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2016.', 7),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q09', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Kaziranga National Park, a natural World Heritage Site, is famous for the:', 'One-horned rhinoceros', 'Asiatic lion', 'Snow leopard', 'Great Indian Bustard', 'A', 'Kaziranga in Assam protects the one-horned rhinoceros.', 8),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q10', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'The tag protecting products of specific geographical origin (e.g., Darjeeling tea) is the:', 'Geographical Indication (GI) tag', 'Trademark', 'Copyright', 'Patent', 'A', 'A GI tag protects goods with a specific geographical origin and reputation.', 9),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q11', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Durga Puja of which city was inscribed on UNESCO''s Intangible Heritage list in 2021?', 'Kolkata', 'Mumbai', 'Chennai', 'Varanasi', 'A', 'Durga Puja in Kolkata was added to UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2021.', 10),
  ('upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs-q12', 'upsc-art-and-culture-heritage-festivals-and-fairs', 'Yakshagana is a traditional theatre form of:', 'Karnataka', 'Kerala', 'West Bengal', 'Manipur', 'A', 'Yakshagana is a folk theatre form of coastal Karnataka.', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q01', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The umbrella environmental legislation passed after the Bhopal tragedy is the:', 'Environment (Protection) Act, 1986', 'Water Act, 1974', 'Wildlife Protection Act, 1972', 'Air Act, 1981', 'A', 'The Environment (Protection) Act, 1986 was enacted following the Bhopal disaster.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q02', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The National Green Tribunal (NGT) was established in:', '2010', '1986', '2000', '2016', 'A', 'The NGT was set up under the NGT Act, 2010, for speedy environmental justice.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q03', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'Which Directive Principle enjoins the State to protect the environment?', 'Article 48A', 'Article 21', 'Article 32', 'Article 19', 'A', 'Article 48A directs the State to protect and improve the environment.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q04', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'National parks and wildlife sanctuaries are governed by the:', 'Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972', 'Forest Rights Act, 2006', 'Air Act, 1981', 'EPA, 1986', 'A', 'The Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 provides for protected areas and species.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q05', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The bodies set up under the Water Act (1974) to monitor pollution are the:', 'Pollution Control Boards', 'Panchayats', 'Zila Parishads', 'Gram Sabhas', 'A', 'The Water Act created the Central and State Pollution Control Boards.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q06', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'Project Tiger was launched in:', '1973', '1992', '1986', '2006', 'A', 'Project Tiger, India''s flagship tiger-conservation programme, began in 1973.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q07', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The principle that the person causing pollution should bear its cost is the:', 'Polluter Pays Principle', 'Precautionary Principle', 'Public Trust Doctrine', 'Sustainable Yield', 'A', 'The Polluter Pays Principle makes polluters bear the cost of the damage they cause.', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q08', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The process to assess a project''s likely environmental effects before clearance is the:', 'Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA)', 'GDP calculation', 'Census', 'Social audit', 'A', 'EIA evaluates the environmental consequences of a proposed project before approval.', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q09', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The Forest Rights Act was passed in:', '2006', '1980', '1972', '1996', 'A', 'The Scheduled Tribes and Other Traditional Forest Dwellers (Recognition of Forest Rights) Act was passed in 2006.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q10', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The Fundamental Duty to protect the natural environment is under:', 'Article 51A(g)', 'Article 21', 'Article 48A', 'Article 39', 'A', 'Article 51A(g) makes protecting the environment a Fundamental Duty of citizens.', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q11', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'Diversion of forest land for non-forest use is regulated by the:', 'Forest (Conservation) Act, 1980', 'Air Act, 1981', 'Water Act, 1974', 'Wildlife Act, 1972', 'A', 'The Forest (Conservation) Act, 1980 requires central approval to divert forest land.', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions-q12', 'upsc-environment-laws-and-institutions', 'The principle requiring caution when an activity''s harm is scientifically uncertain is the:', 'Precautionary Principle', 'Polluter Pays Principle', 'Absolute Liability', 'Sustainable Yield', 'A', 'The Precautionary Principle urges preventive action under scientific uncertainty.', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q01', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'India''s first national park (1936) is now known as:', 'Jim Corbett National Park', 'Kaziranga National Park', 'Gir National Park', 'Ranthambore National Park', 'A', 'Established in 1936 as Hailey National Park, it is now Jim Corbett National Park.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q02', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'The Asiatic lion is found in the wild only in:', 'Gir (Gujarat)', 'Kaziranga (Assam)', 'Sundarbans (West Bengal)', 'Ranthambore (Rajasthan)', 'A', 'The last wild Asiatic lions survive in Gir National Park, Gujarat.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q03', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'Wetlands of international importance are designated under which convention?', 'Ramsar Convention', 'CITES', 'Kyoto Protocol', 'Montreal Protocol', 'A', 'The Ramsar Convention designates wetlands of international importance.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q04', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'The convention that regulates international trade in endangered species is:', 'CITES', 'CBD', 'UNFCCC', 'Ramsar', 'A', 'CITES regulates and restricts trade in endangered species of flora and fauna.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q05', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'The IUCN Red List category just above ''Endangered'' in threat level is:', 'Critically Endangered', 'Vulnerable', 'Near Threatened', 'Least Concern', 'A', 'The order of increasing threat is Vulnerable → Endangered → Critically Endangered.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q06', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'Which of these is a globally recognised biodiversity hotspot in India?', 'The Western Ghats', 'The Thar Desert', 'The Deccan plateau', 'The Gangetic plain', 'A', 'The Western Ghats are one of the world''s biodiversity hotspots.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q07', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'The critically endangered Great Indian Bustard is the state bird of:', 'Rajasthan', 'Kerala', 'Assam', 'Punjab', 'A', 'The Great Indian Bustard, critically endangered, is Rajasthan''s state bird.', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q08', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'Biosphere reserves in India that are internationally recognised are part of UNESCO''s:', 'Man and the Biosphere (MAB) Programme', 'World Food Programme', 'Green Climate Fund', 'Global Environment Facility', 'A', 'Recognised biosphere reserves belong to UNESCO''s Man and the Biosphere network.', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q09', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'The Sundarbans, a UNESCO site and tiger habitat, is a large:', 'Mangrove forest', 'Coral reef', 'Alpine meadow', 'Desert', 'A', 'The Sundarbans is the world''s largest mangrove forest, shared by India and Bangladesh.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q10', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'In a wildlife sanctuary, as compared with a national park, human activities are:', 'Somewhat permitted (limited)', 'Completely banned', 'Unrestricted', 'Encouraged commercially', 'A', 'Sanctuaries allow certain regulated human activities; national parks are stricter.', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q11', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'Keoladeo National Park, a famous Ramsar site for migratory birds, is in:', 'Rajasthan', 'Gujarat', 'Odisha', 'Assam', 'A', 'Keoladeo (Bharatpur) in Rajasthan is a renowned bird sanctuary and Ramsar site.', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife-q12', 'upsc-environment-protected-areas-and-wildlife', 'Project Elephant was launched to protect elephants in the year:', '1992', '1973', '2006', '1986', 'A', 'Project Elephant was launched in 1992 to conserve elephants and their habitats.', 11),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q01', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The Air Quality Index (AQI) chiefly tracks fine particulate matter measured as:', 'PM2.5 and PM10', 'CO2 only', 'Ozone only', 'Methane', 'A', 'AQI tracks pollutants including PM2.5 and PM10 particulates, NO₂, SO₂, CO, and O₃.', 0),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q02', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The Namami Gange programme is aimed at cleaning the river:', 'Ganga', 'Yamuna', 'Godavari', 'Narmada', 'A', 'Namami Gange is the flagship programme for cleaning and conserving the Ganga.', 1),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q03', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The Bhopal Gas Tragedy (1984) was caused by the leak of:', 'Methyl isocyanate (MIC)', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Chlorine', 'Ammonia', 'A', 'The Bhopal disaster resulted from a methyl isocyanate (MIC) gas leak.', 2),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q04', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'India''s current vehicular emission norms are:', 'Bharat Stage VI (BS-VI)', 'Bharat Stage II', 'Euro 2', 'BS-III', 'A', 'India moved to Bharat Stage VI (BS-VI) emission standards in 2020.', 3),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q05', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The nutrient enrichment of water bodies leading to algal blooms is called:', 'Eutrophication', 'Biomagnification', 'Desalination', 'Acidification', 'A', 'Eutrophication is nutrient over-enrichment causing algal blooms and oxygen depletion.', 4),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q06', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'High Biological Oxygen Demand (BOD) in water indicates:', 'Heavy organic pollution', 'Clean water', 'High salinity', 'Low temperature', 'A', 'A high BOD means microbes consume more oxygen, signalling organic pollution.', 5),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q07', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The policy making producers responsible for the disposal of their products'' waste is:', 'Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR)', 'Minimum Support Price', 'Cess', 'Feed-in tariff', 'A', 'EPR makes producers responsible for managing post-consumer product waste (e.g., plastics, e-waste).', 6),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q08', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The ''3 Rs'' of sustainable waste management are:', 'Reduce, Reuse, Recycle', 'Read, Write, Recall', 'Repair, Rebuild, Renew', 'Reform, Reset, Restore', 'A', 'The 3 Rs — Reduce, Reuse, Recycle — guide sustainable waste management.', 7),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q09', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission is primarily aimed at:', 'Sanitation and cleanliness', 'Rural electrification', 'Digital literacy', 'Crop insurance', 'A', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission focuses on sanitation, cleanliness, and waste management.', 8),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q10', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'Solid waste rules require households to segregate waste into wet (biodegradable) and:', 'Dry (non-biodegradable)', 'Radioactive', 'Liquid only', 'Gaseous', 'A', 'Waste is segregated at source into wet (biodegradable) and dry (non-biodegradable) streams.', 9),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q11', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'The Minamata disease in Japan was caused by pollution from:', 'Mercury', 'Lead', 'Arsenic', 'Cadmium', 'A', 'Minamata disease resulted from mercury poisoning of seafood in Japan.', 10),
  ('upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management-q12', 'upsc-environment-pollution-and-waste-management', 'An economic model that designs out waste and keeps resources in use is the:', 'Circular economy', 'Linear economy', 'Barter economy', 'Command economy', 'A', 'The circular economy minimises waste by reusing, repairing, and recycling resources.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'The ''brain'' of a computer that performs processing is the:', 'CPU', 'Monitor', 'Keyboard', 'Printer', 'A', 'The Central Processing Unit (CPU) executes instructions and performs computations.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'Computers fundamentally represent data in which number system?', 'Binary', 'Decimal', 'Roman', 'Hexadecimal only', 'A', 'Computers use the binary system of 0s and 1s (bits).', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'Volatile memory that loses data when power is off is:', 'RAM', 'ROM', 'Hard disk', 'SSD', 'A', 'RAM (Random Access Memory) is volatile and loses its contents when powered off.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'A decentralised, tamper-evident digital ledger underlying cryptocurrencies is called:', 'Blockchain', 'Spreadsheet', 'Firewall', 'Router', 'A', 'Blockchain is a distributed, tamper-evident ledger technology.', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'The subfield of AI where systems learn patterns from data is:', 'Machine learning', 'Word processing', 'Compilation', 'Defragmentation', 'A', 'Machine learning lets systems learn from data rather than explicit programming.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'India''s real-time mobile payments system, now used globally, is:', 'UPI', 'SWIFT', 'RTGS only', 'PayPal', 'A', 'The Unified Payments Interface (UPI) enables instant real-time mobile payments.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'Aadhaar is best described as India''s:', 'Biometric-based unique identity system', 'Payment gateway', 'Stock exchange', 'Search engine', 'A', 'Aadhaar provides a biometric-linked unique identity number to residents.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'The basic unit of quantum computing is the:', 'Qubit', 'Bit', 'Byte', 'Pixel', 'A', 'Quantum computers use qubits, which can exist in superposition of states.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'The network of internet-connected everyday devices is called the:', 'Internet of Things (IoT)', 'Intranet', 'Dark web', 'Ethernet', 'A', 'The Internet of Things (IoT) connects sensors and devices over the internet.', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'AI techniques using multi-layered neural networks are called:', 'Deep learning', 'Shallow sorting', 'Batch processing', 'Caching', 'A', 'Deep learning uses many-layered neural networks to model complex patterns.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'India''s data-protection law enacted in 2023 is the:', 'Digital Personal Data Protection Act', 'IT Act, 2000', 'RTI Act', 'Aadhaar Act', 'A', 'The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 governs the processing of personal data.', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-it-computers-and-ai', 'Delivering computing resources over the internet on demand is called:', 'Cloud computing', 'Edge etching', 'Grid drawing', 'Local hosting', 'A', 'Cloud computing provides on-demand computing resources (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS) over the internet.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The process of splitting a heavy nucleus to release energy is:', 'Nuclear fission', 'Nuclear fusion', 'Radioactive decay only', 'Ionisation', 'A', 'Nuclear fission splits heavy nuclei (e.g., U-235) in a chain reaction, releasing energy.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The Sun produces its energy mainly through:', 'Nuclear fusion', 'Nuclear fission', 'Combustion', 'Chemical reactions', 'A', 'The Sun fuses hydrogen into helium (nuclear fusion), releasing vast energy.', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The ''father of the Indian nuclear programme'' is:', 'Homi Bhabha', 'Vikram Sarabhai', 'C. V. Raman', 'A. P. J. Abdul Kalam', 'A', 'Homi Bhabha founded India''s nuclear programme and conceived the three-stage plan.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The third stage of India''s nuclear programme is designed to use its large reserves of:', 'Thorium', 'Uranium', 'Coal', 'Plutonium', 'A', 'Stage three exploits India''s abundant thorium (from Kerala''s monazite sands).', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'In a nuclear reactor, control rods (e.g., cadmium/boron) serve to:', 'Absorb neutrons and control the reaction', 'Speed up the reaction indefinitely', 'Generate steam', 'Store the fuel', 'A', 'Control rods absorb neutrons to regulate or stop the fission chain reaction.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The moderator in many reactors, used to slow down neutrons, can be:', 'Heavy water or graphite', 'Cadmium', 'Uranium', 'Concrete', 'A', 'Moderators like heavy water or graphite slow neutrons to sustain fission.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The Kudankulam and Tarapur facilities are examples of:', 'Nuclear power plants', 'Thermal power plants', 'Hydroelectric dams', 'Wind farms', 'A', 'Kudankulam and Tarapur are Indian nuclear power stations.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The International Solar Alliance (ISA) is headquartered in:', 'India (Gurugram)', 'France', 'the USA', 'the UAE', 'A', 'The ISA, co-founded by India and France, is headquartered in Gurugram, India.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'India got a waiver to trade in nuclear technology through the 2008:', 'Indo-US Nuclear Deal', 'Simla Agreement', 'Panchsheel Agreement', 'Tashkent Declaration', 'A', 'The 2008 Indo-US civil nuclear deal secured an NSG waiver for India.', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The second stage of India''s nuclear plan relies on:', 'Fast Breeder Reactors using plutonium', 'Solar panels', 'Coal gasification', 'Wind turbines', 'A', 'Stage two uses Fast Breeder Reactors that breed more fissile material from plutonium.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'The international project to demonstrate fusion power, of which India is a partner, is:', 'ITER', 'CERN', 'ISS', 'LIGO', 'A', 'ITER is the international thermonuclear (fusion) experimental reactor project.', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-nuclear-technology-and-energy', 'India''s premier nuclear research centre near Mumbai is:', 'BARC', 'ISRO', 'DRDO', 'CSIR', 'A', 'The Bhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC) is India''s premier nuclear research institution.', 11),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q01', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'Malaria is caused by a protozoan of the genus Plasmodium, spread by the:', 'Female Anopheles mosquito', 'Aedes mosquito', 'Housefly', 'Tsetse fly', 'A', 'Malaria is transmitted by the bite of the female Anopheles mosquito.', 0),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q02', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'Dengue and chikungunya are transmitted mainly by the:', 'Aedes mosquito', 'Anopheles mosquito', 'Culex mosquito', 'Sandfly', 'A', 'Dengue and chikungunya are spread by the Aedes aegypti mosquito.', 1),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q03', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'India was declared polio-free in:', '2014', '2000', '1975', '2020', 'A', 'The WHO declared India polio-free in 2014 after sustained immunisation.', 2),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q04', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'Antibiotics are effective against which type of pathogen?', 'Bacteria', 'Viruses', 'All viruses and bacteria equally', 'Only fungi', 'A', 'Antibiotics treat bacterial infections; they do not work against viruses.', 3),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q05', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'The overuse of antibiotics leads to the growing problem of:', 'Antimicrobial resistance (AMR)', 'Herd immunity', 'Eutrophication', 'Vaccination', 'A', 'Overuse of antibiotics drives antimicrobial resistance (AMR), a major health threat.', 4),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q06', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'COVID-19 is caused by which virus?', 'SARS-CoV-2', 'HIV', 'Influenza H1N1', 'Ebola', 'A', 'COVID-19 is caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus.', 5),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q07', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'India''s indigenously developed COVID-19 vaccine is:', 'Covaxin', 'Sputnik V', 'Pfizer', 'Moderna', 'A', 'Covaxin, by Bharat Biotech and ICMR, is India''s indigenous COVID-19 vaccine.', 6),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q08', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'Diseases like diabetes and cancer, not spread by pathogens, are classed as:', 'Non-communicable diseases', 'Communicable diseases', 'Epidemics', 'Zoonoses', 'A', 'Non-communicable (lifestyle) diseases are not transmitted between people.', 7),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q09', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'When enough of a population is immune to protect the rest, it is called:', 'Herd immunity', 'Passive immunity', 'Autoimmunity', 'Immunodeficiency', 'A', 'Herd immunity slows disease spread when a large share of a population is immune.', 8),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q10', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'Ayushman Bharat provides health insurance cover along with:', 'Health and Wellness Centres', 'Crop loans', 'Free laptops', 'Housing loans', 'A', 'Ayushman Bharat combines the PM-JAY insurance scheme with Health and Wellness Centres.', 9),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q11', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'The disease officially eradicated worldwide through vaccination is:', 'Smallpox', 'Malaria', 'Tuberculosis', 'Dengue', 'A', 'Smallpox is the only human disease declared eradicated (WHO, 1980).', 10),
  ('upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines-q12', 'upsc-science-technology-health-diseases-and-vaccines', 'The global body that coordinates international public health is the:', 'World Health Organization (WHO)', 'World Trade Organization', 'UNESCO', 'World Bank', 'A', 'The WHO, a UN agency, directs and coordinates international health work.', 11),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q01', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Human Development Report and the HDI are published by:', 'UNDP', 'World Bank', 'IMF', 'WEF', 'A', 'The UN Development Programme (UNDP) publishes the Human Development Report and HDI.', 0),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q02', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Economic Survey of India is prepared by the:', 'Chief Economic Adviser (Ministry of Finance)', 'RBI Governor', 'NITI Aayog CEO', 'Comptroller and Auditor General', 'A', 'The Economic Survey is prepared under the Chief Economic Adviser and tabled before the Budget.', 1),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q03', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Corruption Perceptions Index is released by:', 'Transparency International', 'The World Bank', 'The IMF', 'The UN', 'A', 'Transparency International publishes the annual Corruption Perceptions Index.', 2),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q04', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Global Gender Gap Report is published by the:', 'World Economic Forum', 'UN Women', 'World Bank', 'ILO', 'A', 'The World Economic Forum (WEF) publishes the Global Gender Gap Report.', 3),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q05', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The World Economic Outlook is a flagship publication of the:', 'IMF', 'World Bank', 'WTO', 'OECD', 'A', 'The International Monetary Fund (IMF) publishes the World Economic Outlook.', 4),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q06', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The SDG India Index, tracking states on the Sustainable Development Goals, is released by:', 'NITI Aayog', 'the RBI', 'the Election Commission', 'the Finance Commission', 'A', 'NITI Aayog publishes the SDG India Index ranking states and UTs.', 5),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q07', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Global Innovation Index is co-published by the:', 'World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO)', 'World Bank', 'IMF', 'UNDP', 'A', 'WIPO co-publishes the Global Innovation Index.', 6),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q08', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The State of the World''s Children report is published by:', 'UNICEF', 'WHO', 'UNESCO', 'UNHCR', 'A', 'UNICEF publishes the annual State of the World''s Children report.', 7),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q09', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Ease of Doing Business rankings were released by the:', 'World Bank', 'World Economic Forum', 'IMF', 'OECD', 'A', 'The World Bank published the (now discontinued) Ease of Doing Business report.', 8),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q10', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Press Freedom Index is compiled by:', 'Reporters Without Borders', 'UNESCO', 'Amnesty International', 'the WEF', 'A', 'Reporters Without Borders (RSF) publishes the World Press Freedom Index.', 9),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q11', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'NITI Aayog''s programme to rapidly develop the most backward districts is the:', 'Aspirational Districts Programme', 'Smart Cities Mission', 'AMRUT', 'Digital India', 'A', 'The Aspirational Districts Programme targets rapid improvement in India''s most underdeveloped districts.', 10),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees-q12', 'upsc-current-affairs-reports-and-committees', 'The Emissions Gap Report is published by the:', 'UN Environment Programme (UNEP)', 'IPCC', 'World Bank', 'IEA', 'A', 'UNEP publishes the annual Emissions Gap Report ahead of climate summits.', 11),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q01', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'India hosted the G20 Leaders'' Summit in 2023 in:', 'New Delhi', 'Mumbai', 'Bengaluru', 'Hyderabad', 'A', 'India''s G20 presidency culminated in the September 2023 New Delhi Summit.', 0),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q02', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The theme of India''s G20 presidency was:', 'Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam — One Earth, One Family, One Future', 'Make in India', 'Digital First', 'Sabka Saath Sabka Vikas', 'A', 'India''s G20 theme was ''Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam — One Earth, One Family, One Future''.', 1),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q03', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The Paris Agreement on climate change was adopted at which COP?', 'COP21 (2015)', 'COP15', 'COP26', 'COP3', 'A', 'The Paris Agreement was adopted at COP21 in 2015.', 2),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q04', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The QUAD grouping comprises India, the USA, Japan, and:', 'Australia', 'the UK', 'France', 'Russia', 'A', 'The QUAD is India, the USA, Japan, and Australia.', 3),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q05', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'At COP26 (Glasgow), India pledged to achieve net-zero emissions by:', '2070', '2050', '2030', '2100', 'A', 'At COP26, India announced a net-zero target by 2070 (the ''Panchamrit'' pledges).', 4),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q06', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The original members of BRICS were Brazil, Russia, India, China, and:', 'South Africa', 'Argentina', 'Egypt', 'Iran', 'A', 'BRICS added South Africa in 2010 (BRIC → BRICS), later expanding further.', 5),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q07', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The new permanent member admitted to the G20 in 2023 was the:', 'African Union', 'European Union', 'ASEAN', 'SAARC', 'A', 'The African Union was admitted as a permanent G20 member at the 2023 New Delhi Summit.', 6),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q08', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'India''s highest civilian award is the:', 'Bharat Ratna', 'Padma Vibhushan', 'Param Vir Chakra', 'Ashoka Chakra', 'A', 'The Bharat Ratna is India''s highest civilian honour.', 7),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q09', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The SCO, which India joined as a full member in 2017, stands for the:', 'Shanghai Cooperation Organisation', 'South China Organisation', 'Strategic Cooperation Order', 'SAARC Coordination Office', 'A', 'India became a full member of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) in 2017.', 8),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q10', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'BIMSTEC is a regional grouping of countries around which body of water?', 'The Bay of Bengal', 'The Arabian Sea', 'The Mediterranean', 'The Caspian Sea', 'A', 'BIMSTEC links Bay of Bengal littoral and adjacent countries in South and Southeast Asia.', 9),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q11', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'COP28, which agreed to ''transition away'' from fossil fuels, was held in:', 'Dubai (UAE)', 'Glasgow', 'Sharm el-Sheikh', 'Paris', 'A', 'COP28 was held in Dubai, UAE, and called for transitioning away from fossil fuels.', 10),
  ('upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events-q12', 'upsc-current-affairs-global-summits-and-events', 'The Nobel Peace Prize is awarded in which city?', 'Oslo', 'Stockholm', 'Geneva', 'The Hague', 'A', 'The Nobel Peace Prize is awarded in Oslo, Norway; the others are given in Stockholm.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The 2020 India-China military clash occurred in which valley?', 'Galwan Valley', 'Nubra Valley', 'Kashmir Valley', 'Silent Valley', 'A', 'The June 2020 clash occurred in the Galwan Valley along the LAC in Ladakh.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'India''s purchase of the S-400 air-defence system was from:', 'Russia', 'the USA', 'France', 'Israel', 'A', 'India signed a deal with Russia for the S-400 Triumf air-defence systems.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The India-US foundational defence agreement enabling geospatial cooperation is:', 'BECA', 'SAARC', 'CEPA', 'TAPI', 'A', 'BECA (Basic Exchange and Cooperation Agreement) enables geospatial intelligence sharing.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The BrahMos missile is a joint development between India and:', 'Russia', 'France', 'the USA', 'Israel', 'A', 'BrahMos is a supersonic cruise missile co-developed by India and Russia.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The China-Pakistan Economic Corridor (CPEC), which India objects to, passes through:', 'Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK)', 'Nepal', 'Bhutan', 'Bangladesh', 'A', 'India objects to CPEC because it runs through Pakistan-occupied Kashmir, violating sovereignty.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'India''s foreign policy of engaging multiple power centres without binding alliances is termed:', 'Strategic autonomy / multi-alignment', 'Isolationism', 'Bandwagoning', 'Containment', 'A', 'India follows strategic autonomy (multi-alignment), the successor to non-alignment.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The disputed, undemarcated India-China boundary is called the:', 'Line of Actual Control (LAC)', 'Line of Control (LoC)', 'Radcliffe Line', 'Durand Line', 'A', 'The Line of Actual Control (LAC) is the effective India-China boundary.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The India-US initiative for cooperation on Critical and Emerging Technology is:', 'iCET', 'LEMOA', 'QUAD', 'IPEF', 'A', 'iCET (initiative on Critical and Emerging Technology) deepens India-US tech cooperation.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The 2017 India-China standoff at Doklam involved a tri-junction with:', 'Bhutan', 'Nepal', 'Myanmar', 'Bangladesh', 'A', 'The Doklam standoff occurred at the India-China-Bhutan tri-junction.', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'India''s relationship with Russia is officially described as a:', 'Special and Privileged Strategic Partnership', 'Military alliance', 'Free trade area', 'Customs union', 'A', 'India and Russia share a ''Special and Privileged Strategic Partnership''.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'The India-US logistics agreement allowing use of each other''s military facilities is:', 'LEMOA', 'BECA', 'COMCASA', 'GSOMIA', 'A', 'LEMOA (Logistics Exchange Memorandum of Agreement) enables reciprocal logistics support.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-india-and-major-powers', 'India began normalising trade in nuclear technology after the NSG waiver secured via the deal with:', 'the USA (2008)', 'Russia', 'France', 'Japan', 'A', 'The 2008 India-US civil nuclear deal led to the NSG waiver enabling nuclear commerce.', 11),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q01', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The Line of Control (LoC) separates India from Pakistan in:', 'Jammu & Kashmir', 'Punjab', 'Rajasthan', 'Gujarat', 'A', 'The LoC divides Indian- and Pakistan-administered Kashmir.', 0),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q02', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The McMahon Line demarcates the boundary between India and:', 'China (in Arunachal Pradesh)', 'Pakistan', 'Nepal', 'Myanmar', 'A', 'The McMahon Line is the India-China boundary in the eastern sector, disputed by China.', 1),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q03', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'India''s maritime vision for the Indian Ocean region is called:', 'SAGAR', 'SAGARMALA only', 'BharatNet', 'UDAN', 'A', 'SAGAR — Security and Growth for All in the Region — is India''s Indian Ocean vision.', 2),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q04', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'Under UNCLOS, a coastal state''s Exclusive Economic Zone extends up to:', '200 nautical miles', '12 nautical miles', '50 nautical miles', '500 nautical miles', 'A', 'The EEZ extends 200 nautical miles from the baseline under UNCLOS.', 3),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q05', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The Simla Agreement (1972), which converted the ceasefire line into the LoC, was signed with:', 'Pakistan', 'China', 'Bangladesh', 'Sri Lanka', 'A', 'The 1972 Simla Agreement between India and Pakistan established the LoC.', 4),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q06', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The Strait of Hormuz, a critical oil choke point, connects the Persian Gulf to the:', 'Gulf of Oman / Arabian Sea', 'Red Sea', 'Mediterranean Sea', 'Black Sea', 'A', 'The Strait of Hormuz links the Persian Gulf to the Gulf of Oman and Arabian Sea.', 5),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q07', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'Aksai Chin, a disputed region administered by China, is claimed by India as part of:', 'Ladakh', 'Arunachal Pradesh', 'Sikkim', 'Nagaland', 'A', 'India claims Aksai Chin (under Chinese control) as part of Ladakh.', 6),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q08', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The Durand Line is the disputed border between:', 'Afghanistan and Pakistan', 'India and Pakistan', 'India and China', 'India and Nepal', 'A', 'The Durand Line separates Afghanistan and Pakistan.', 7),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q09', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'India is often described in the Indian Ocean as a:', 'Net security provider', 'Landlocked state', 'Non-littoral power', 'Neutral bystander', 'A', 'India acts as a ''net security provider'' in the Indian Ocean region.', 8),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q10', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The strategically vital Andaman & Nicobar Islands host India''s only:', 'Tri-services theatre command', 'Nuclear plant', 'Spaceport', 'Oil refinery', 'A', 'The Andaman & Nicobar Command is India''s first and only tri-services theatre command.', 9),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q11', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The Strait of Malacca, a key shipping lane, lies between the Malay Peninsula and:', 'Sumatra (Indonesia)', 'Sri Lanka', 'Japan', 'Australia', 'A', 'The Strait of Malacca runs between the Malay Peninsula and the Indonesian island of Sumatra.', 10),
  ('upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security-q12', 'upsc-international-relations-border-and-maritime-security', 'The 2017 India-China standoff at Doklam was primarily over a Chinese attempt to build a:', 'Road near the tri-junction', 'Naval base', 'Dam', 'Railway line', 'A', 'The Doklam standoff arose over Chinese road construction near the tri-junction with Bhutan.', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q01', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'A document declaring an organisation''s service standards to the public is a:', 'Citizens'' Charter', 'White Paper', 'Gazette', 'Ordinance', 'A', 'A Citizens'' Charter publicly commits an agency to service standards and timelines.', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q02', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'In ''SMART'' governance, the ''T'' stands for:', 'Transparent', 'Technical', 'Timely', 'Trustworthy', 'A', 'SMART governance = Simple, Moral, Accountable, Responsive, and Transparent.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q03', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'Transferring subsidies straight to beneficiaries'' bank accounts to cut leakages is called:', 'Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT)', 'Cross-subsidy', 'Deficit financing', 'Quantitative easing', 'A', 'DBT transfers benefits directly to beneficiaries, reducing intermediary leakages.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q04', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The Sevottam model is a framework to assess and improve:', 'Public service delivery', 'Tax collection', 'Election conduct', 'Judicial appointments', 'A', 'Sevottam is a service-delivery excellence model for public organisations.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q05', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The e-governance interaction between government and citizens is abbreviated:', 'G2C', 'B2B', 'C2C', 'P2P', 'A', 'G2C (Government-to-Citizen) covers services delivered to citizens.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q06', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'Social audits as an accountability tool were pioneered in India under:', 'MGNREGA', 'the GST', 'the RBI Act', 'the Companies Act', 'A', 'MGNREGA institutionalised social audits by gram sabhas to check corruption.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q07', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The central public grievance redressal portal is:', 'CPGRAMS', 'DigiLocker', 'GeM', 'e-NAM', 'A', 'CPGRAMS is the Centralised Public Grievance Redress and Monitoring System.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q08', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The Right to Information Act was enacted in:', '2005', '2013', '1998', '2019', 'A', 'The RTI Act, empowering citizens to seek public information, was passed in 2005.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q09', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The digital platform for storing and sharing official documents securely is:', 'DigiLocker', 'CPGRAMS', 'UPI', 'NATGRID', 'A', 'DigiLocker lets citizens store and share verified digital documents.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q10', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The Second Administrative Reforms Commission (ARC) was chaired initially by:', 'Veerappa Moily', 'Morarji Desai', 'B. R. Ambedkar', 'K. Santhanam', 'A', 'The 2nd ARC was chaired by Veerappa Moily (later M. Veerappa Moily/Y. K. Alagh phases).', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q11', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'Many states guarantee time-bound public services through laws known as the:', 'Right to Public Services Acts', 'Official Secrets Acts', 'Contempt of Court Acts', 'Sedition laws', 'A', 'Right to Public Services Acts guarantee time-bound delivery of notified services.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance-q12', 'upsc-governance-citizen-centric-governance', 'The slogan capturing the aim of efficient, limited government is:', 'Minimum Government, Maximum Governance', 'Garibi Hatao', 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan', 'Inclusive Growth', 'A', '''Minimum Government, Maximum Governance'' expresses the drive for efficient administration.', 11),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q01', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'The All India Services include the IAS, IPS, and the:', 'Indian Forest Service (IFoS)', 'Indian Foreign Service', 'Indian Revenue Service', 'Indian Railway Service', 'A', 'The three All India Services are the IAS, IPS, and Indian Forest Service (IFoS).', 0),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q02', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'The constitutional article providing for All India Services is:', 'Article 312', 'Article 356', 'Article 21', 'Article 370', 'A', 'Article 312 empowers Parliament to create All India Services.', 1),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q03', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Civil servants are expected to be politically:', 'Neutral', 'Partisan', 'Elected', 'Temporary', 'A', 'Political neutrality and anonymity are core values of a permanent civil service.', 2),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q04', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Self-Help Groups (SHGs) primarily promote:', 'Financial inclusion and micro-credit', 'National defence', 'Foreign trade', 'Space research', 'A', 'SHGs pool savings and provide micro-credit, advancing financial inclusion, especially for women.', 3),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q05', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'The Amul dairy success is a model of which type of organisation?', 'Cooperative', 'Multinational corporation', 'Public sector undertaking', 'Sole proprietorship', 'A', 'Amul exemplifies the cooperative model of collective, farmer-owned enterprise.', 4),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q06', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Foreign funding of NGOs in India is regulated under the:', 'FCRA', 'FEMA only', 'RTI Act', 'IPC', 'A', 'The Foreign Contribution (Regulation) Act (FCRA) governs foreign funding of NGOs.', 5),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q07', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'The media is often referred to as the:', 'Fourth estate', 'Fifth column', 'Third house', 'Second chamber', 'A', 'The media is called the ''fourth estate'' for its role in a democracy.', 6),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q08', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Kudumbashree, a large women''s empowerment network, is a programme of:', 'Kerala', 'Gujarat', 'Bihar', 'Punjab', 'A', 'Kudumbashree is Kerala''s flagship women''s SHG and poverty-eradication programme.', 7),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q09', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Mandatory Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) spending for large firms is under the:', 'Companies Act', 'Income Tax Act', 'RTI Act', 'GST Act', 'A', 'The Companies Act, 2013 mandates CSR spending by qualifying companies.', 8),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q10', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Bringing in domain experts from outside the regular services to government posts is called:', 'Lateral entry', 'Deputation only', 'Reservation', 'Impeachment', 'A', 'Lateral entry recruits specialists directly into senior government positions.', 9),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q11', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'Groups that seek to influence policy without contesting elections are called:', 'Pressure groups', 'Political parties', 'Electoral colleges', 'Tribunals', 'A', 'Pressure/interest groups influence policy without seeking to form a government.', 10),
  ('upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors-q12', 'upsc-governance-civil-services-and-non-state-actors', 'The principle that civil servants give ''frank and fearless'' advice but implement the minister''s final decision reflects:', 'Political neutrality and accountability', 'Judicial review', 'Separation of powers', 'Federal supremacy', 'A', 'Civil servants advise honestly yet remain accountable to elected ministers — a neutrality norm.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'India''s external intelligence agency is the:', 'Research and Analysis Wing (RAW)', 'Intelligence Bureau (IB)', 'CBI', 'NIA', 'A', 'RAW is India''s external intelligence agency; the IB handles internal intelligence.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The largest Central Armed Police Force, key to internal security and anti-Naxal operations, is the:', 'CRPF', 'BSF', 'CISF', 'ITBP', 'A', 'The Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF) is India''s largest CAPF.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The elite counter-terrorism force known as the ''Black Cats'' is the:', 'National Security Guard (NSG)', 'CISF', 'SSB', 'Assam Rifles', 'A', 'The NSG (''Black Cats'') is India''s elite counter-terrorism and hostage-rescue force.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The force responsible for security of airports and vital installations is the:', 'CISF', 'BSF', 'ITBP', 'SSB', 'A', 'The Central Industrial Security Force (CISF) guards airports and industrial installations.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The head of India''s tri-services integration, created in 2019, is the:', 'Chief of Defence Staff (CDS)', 'Cabinet Secretary', 'Home Secretary', 'National Security Adviser', 'A', 'The Chief of Defence Staff (CDS) heads the Department of Military Affairs and integrates the services.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The agency that investigates economic offences under the PMLA and FEMA is the:', 'Enforcement Directorate (ED)', 'NIA', 'IB', 'RAW', 'A', 'The Enforcement Directorate (ED) enforces the PMLA and FEMA against economic offences.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'In the Indian Constitution, ''police'' and ''public order'' are placed in the:', 'State List', 'Union List', 'Concurrent List', 'Residuary powers', 'A', '''Police'' and ''public order'' are State List subjects under the Seventh Schedule.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The apex body advising the PM on national security, headed by the NSA, is the:', 'National Security Council (NSC)', 'Finance Commission', 'NITI Aayog', 'Election Commission', 'A', 'The National Security Council advises the PM, coordinated by the National Security Adviser.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The Assam Rifles primarily operate in which region?', 'The North-East', 'Rajasthan desert', 'The Deccan', 'Gujarat coast', 'A', 'The Assam Rifles are the oldest paramilitary force, guarding the north-eastern frontier.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'The premier agency for investigating major crimes and corruption at the central level is the:', 'CBI', 'CISF', 'BSF', 'NDRF', 'A', 'The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) probes major crimes and corruption cases.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'NATGRID is being developed as a:', 'Networked intelligence/database grid for security agencies', 'Power transmission grid', 'Weather monitoring system', 'Payment system', 'A', 'NATGRID is an integrated intelligence grid linking databases for security agencies.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-security-forces-and-agencies', 'India''s internal intelligence agency is the:', 'Intelligence Bureau (IB)', 'RAW', 'NIA', 'ED', 'A', 'The Intelligence Bureau (IB) is India''s domestic (internal) intelligence agency.', 11),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q01', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The belt worst affected by Left-Wing Extremism is often called the:', 'Red Corridor', 'Golden Triangle', 'Chicken''s Neck', 'Cotton Belt', 'A', 'The ''Red Corridor'' spans LWE-affected districts of central and eastern India.', 0),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q02', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The main anti-terror law under which terror offences are prosecuted in India is the:', 'UAPA', 'RTI Act', 'RTE Act', 'MGNREGA', 'A', 'The Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (UAPA) is India''s principal anti-terror law.', 1),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q03', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The global watchdog whose ''grey list'' pressures states on terror financing is the:', 'FATF', 'WTO', 'UNESCO', 'IMF', 'A', 'The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) monitors and lists states on money laundering and terror financing.', 2),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q04', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The informal, illegal money-transfer system often misused for terror funding is:', 'Hawala', 'UPI', 'RTGS', 'NEFT', 'A', 'Hawala is an informal value-transfer system exploited to move illicit funds.', 3),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q05', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The government''s strategy doctrine to tackle Left-Wing Extremism is called:', 'SAMADHAN', 'SAGAR', 'UDAN', 'AMRUT', 'A', 'SAMADHAN is the multi-pronged strategy against Left-Wing Extremism.', 4),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q06', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The central agency that investigates terror-related cases is the:', 'NIA', 'CISF', 'NDRF', 'SSB', 'A', 'The National Investigation Agency (NIA) investigates terrorism-related offences.', 5),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q07', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The use of the internet to recruit and incite attackers is known as:', 'Online radicalisation', 'Phishing', 'Firewalling', 'Encryption', 'A', 'Online radicalisation uses social media and the internet to spread extremist propaganda and recruit.', 6),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q08', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'An attacker who acts alone, often self-radicalised online, is called a:', 'Lone wolf', 'Double agent', 'Whistle-blower', 'Sleeper cell', 'A', 'A ''lone wolf'' attacker operates independently, frequently after online self-radicalisation.', 7),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q09', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'Terror financing through counterfeit currency is countered partly by tracking:', 'Fake Indian Currency Notes (FICN)', 'Postage stamps', 'Coins only', 'Bearer bonds', 'A', 'Fake Indian Currency Notes (FICN) are a known channel of terror financing.', 8),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q10', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'The law used to attach and confiscate proceeds of crime linked to terror funding is the:', 'PMLA', 'RTI Act', 'RTE Act', 'Companies Act', 'A', 'The Prevention of Money Laundering Act (PMLA) allows attachment of proceeds of crime.', 9),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q11', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'Programmes to reintegrate former militants into society are known as:', 'De-radicalisation programmes', 'Encryption drives', 'Surveillance audits', 'Cordon operations', 'A', 'De-radicalisation programmes aim to rehabilitate and reintegrate former extremists.', 10),
  ('upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing-q12', 'upsc-internal-security-extremism-and-terror-financing', 'Rapidly spreading false information online that can inflame tensions is termed:', 'Fake news / disinformation', 'Open data', 'Metadata', 'Firmware', 'A', 'Fake news/disinformation spread via social media can incite unrest and aid radicalisation.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q01', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Constitution was:', 'Dr. B. R. Ambedkar', 'Dr. Rajendra Prasad', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Sardar Patel', 'A', 'Dr. B. R. Ambedkar chaired the Drafting Committee and is called the ''Father of the Constitution''.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q02', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The Constitution of India came into force on:', '26 January 1950', '15 August 1947', '26 November 1949', '9 December 1946', 'A', 'The Constitution came into force on 26 January 1950, celebrated as Republic Day.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q03', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The President of the Constituent Assembly was:', 'Dr. Rajendra Prasad', 'Dr. B. R. Ambedkar', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Sachchidananda Sinha', 'A', 'Dr. Rajendra Prasad was the permanent President of the Constituent Assembly.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q04', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The Directive Principles of State Policy were borrowed from the Constitution of:', 'Ireland', 'the USA', 'Britain', 'Canada', 'A', 'The DPSP were inspired by the Irish Constitution.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q05', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The idea of Fundamental Rights and judicial review was drawn mainly from:', 'the USA', 'Britain', 'Ireland', 'the USSR', 'A', 'Fundamental Rights, judicial review, and the preamble were inspired by the US Constitution.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q06', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The words ''Socialist'' and ''Secular'' were added to the Preamble by which amendment?', '42nd Amendment (1976)', '44th Amendment (1978)', '1st Amendment (1951)', '52nd Amendment (1985)', 'A', 'The 42nd Amendment (1976) added ''Socialist'', ''Secular'', and ''Integrity'' to the Preamble.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q07', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The Objectives Resolution, which inspired the Preamble, was moved by:', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'B. R. Ambedkar', 'Rajendra Prasad', 'Vallabhbhai Patel', 'A', 'Nehru moved the Objectives Resolution, later reflected in the Preamble.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q08', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The bulk of the federal scheme and administrative provisions came from the:', 'Government of India Act, 1935', 'US Constitution', 'Irish Constitution', 'Charter Act, 1833', 'A', 'The Government of India Act, 1935 supplied the federal structure and many administrative details.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q09', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'Fundamental Duties were inspired by the Constitution of:', 'the USSR', 'the USA', 'Ireland', 'Australia', 'A', 'Fundamental Duties were borrowed from the erstwhile USSR (Soviet) Constitution.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q10', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The Constitution was adopted by the Constituent Assembly on:', '26 November 1949', '26 January 1950', '15 August 1947', '2 October 1949', 'A', 'The Constitution was adopted on 26 November 1949, now marked as Constitution Day.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q11', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'In the Kesavananda Bharati case, the Preamble was held to be:', 'A part of the Constitution', 'Not a part of the Constitution', 'Superior to the Constitution', 'Legally unenforceable and separate', 'A', 'Kesavananda Bharati (1973) held the Preamble is a part of the Constitution, reversing Berubari.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution-q12', 'upsc-polity-making-of-the-constitution', 'The parliamentary form of government was adopted mainly from:', 'Britain', 'the USA', 'France', 'Switzerland', 'A', 'India''s parliamentary system, rule of law, and single citizenship follow the British model.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q01', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The Election Commission of India is established under which article?', 'Article 324', 'Article 280', 'Article 148', 'Article 315', 'A', 'Article 324 vests the superintendence of elections in the Election Commission of India.', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q02', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The system used to elect members of the Lok Sabha is:', 'First-Past-The-Post', 'Proportional representation', 'Single transferable vote', 'List system', 'A', 'Lok Sabha and Assembly members are elected by the First-Past-The-Post system.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q03', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The voting age in India was lowered from 21 to 18 by which amendment?', '61st Amendment (1989)', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '73rd Amendment', 'A', 'The 61st Amendment (1989) lowered the voting age to 18 years.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q04', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The set of norms that becomes operational once elections are announced is the:', 'Model Code of Conduct', 'Whip', 'Anti-Defection Law', 'Money Bill rule', 'A', 'The Model Code of Conduct governs parties and candidates once elections are notified.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q05', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The conduct of elections is chiefly governed by the:', 'Representation of the People Acts (1950/1951)', 'Indian Penal Code', 'Contract Act', 'RTI Act', 'A', 'The Representation of the People Acts, 1950 and 1951 govern electoral rolls and the conduct of elections.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q06', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The NOTA (None of the Above) option was introduced in Indian elections in:', '2013', '1999', '2004', '2019', 'A', 'The Supreme Court ordered the NOTA option, introduced in 2013.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q07', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'Members of the Rajya Sabha are elected by:', 'Proportional representation by single transferable vote', 'Direct election', 'First-Past-The-Post', 'Nomination only', 'A', 'Rajya Sabha members are elected by state legislators using proportional representation (STV).', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q08', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The device that lets a voter verify their vote was recorded correctly is the:', 'VVPAT', 'EVM only', 'Ballot box', 'NOTA', 'A', 'The Voter-Verifiable Paper Audit Trail (VVPAT) prints a slip confirming the vote.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q09', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The Chief Election Commissioner can be removed from office in the manner of a:', 'Supreme Court judge', 'Governor', 'Cabinet minister', 'Civil servant', 'A', 'The CEC can be removed only through the process used for a Supreme Court judge, ensuring independence.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q10', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The electoral bonds scheme for political funding was struck down in 2024 by the:', 'Supreme Court', 'Election Commission', 'Parliament', 'RBI', 'A', 'The Supreme Court struck down the electoral bonds scheme as unconstitutional in 2024.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q11', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The right of every adult citizen to vote regardless of status is called:', 'Universal adult franchise', 'Restricted suffrage', 'Proportional voting', 'Weighted voting', 'A', 'Universal adult franchise gives every adult citizen the right to vote, a hallmark of Indian democracy.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-elections-and-representation-q12', 'upsc-polity-elections-and-representation', 'The proposal to hold simultaneous Lok Sabha and Assembly elections is popularly called:', 'One Nation, One Election', 'One Nation, One Tax', 'One Nation, One Ration Card', 'One Nation, One Grid', 'A', '''One Nation, One Election'' proposes holding Lok Sabha and state Assembly polls together.', 11),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q01', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The Anti-Defection Law is contained in which schedule of the Constitution?', 'Tenth Schedule', 'Seventh Schedule', 'Ninth Schedule', 'Fifth Schedule', 'A', 'The Anti-Defection Law is in the Tenth Schedule, added by the 52nd Amendment (1985).', 0),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q02', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The Anti-Defection Law was added by which amendment?', '52nd Amendment (1985)', '42nd Amendment', '44th Amendment', '73rd Amendment', 'A', 'The 52nd Amendment (1985) introduced the anti-defection provisions.', 1),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q03', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'Under the anti-defection law, disqualification is decided by the:', 'Presiding officer (Speaker/Chairman)', 'President', 'Supreme Court directly', 'Election Commission', 'A', 'The Speaker or Chairman decides on disqualification, subject to judicial review.', 2),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q04', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The 91st Amendment (2003) removed the exemption for a party:', 'Split', 'Merger', 'Alliance', 'Coalition', 'A', 'The 91st Amendment deleted the ''split'' exemption, leaving only ''merger'' (two-thirds) valid.', 3),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q05', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The Public Accounts Committee (PAC) mainly examines the:', 'Audited accounts and the CAG''s reports', 'Foreign policy', 'Election disputes', 'Judicial appointments', 'A', 'The PAC scrutinises government spending using the CAG''s audit reports.', 4),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q06', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'By convention, the Chairman of the Public Accounts Committee is from the:', 'Opposition', 'Ruling party', 'Rajya Sabha only', 'Council of Ministers', 'A', 'By convention the PAC chair is from the Opposition, strengthening accountability.', 5),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q07', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The committee often called the ''continuous economy committee'' is the:', 'Estimates Committee', 'Public Accounts Committee', 'Business Advisory Committee', 'Rules Committee', 'A', 'The Estimates Committee, examining budget estimates for economy, is called the ''continuous economy committee''.', 6),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q08', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'A directive by a party to its legislators on how to vote is called a:', 'Whip', 'Writ', 'Warrant', 'Motion', 'A', 'A whip is a party directive on voting; defying it can attract disqualification.', 7),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q09', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'Committees that examine bills, budgets, and policy of specific ministries are the:', 'Department-Related Standing Committees', 'Ad hoc committees', 'Select committees', 'Privileges committees', 'A', 'Department-Related Standing Committees (DRSCs) examine ministries'' bills, budgets, and policies.', 8),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q10', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'The Committee on Public Undertakings scrutinises the working of:', 'Public sector undertakings (PSUs)', 'Private companies', 'Foreign firms', 'Cooperative banks', 'A', 'The Committee on Public Undertakings reviews the accounts and working of PSUs.', 9),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q11', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'A temporary committee formed to examine a specific bill is an example of a(n):', 'Ad hoc committee', 'Standing committee', 'Financial committee', 'Constitutional body', 'A', 'Ad hoc committees (like Select/Joint Committees on a bill) are temporary and task-specific.', 10),
  ('upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees-q12', 'upsc-polity-anti-defection-and-committees', 'After the 91st Amendment, a valid defection escape requires a merger involving at least:', 'Two-thirds of the members', 'One-third of the members', 'One-half of the members', 'All the members', 'A', 'A merger needs at least two-thirds of a legislature party''s members to agree.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q01', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The regulator of the securities market in India is:', 'SEBI', 'RBI', 'IRDAI', 'PFRDA', 'A', 'The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) regulates the securities market.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q02', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The market where new securities are issued for the first time is the:', 'Primary market', 'Secondary market', 'Money market', 'Forex market', 'A', 'The primary market is where companies issue new securities (e.g., via IPOs).', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q03', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The first public sale of a company''s shares is called a(n):', 'IPO', 'FPO only', 'Buyback', 'Rights issue', 'A', 'An Initial Public Offering (IPO) is a company''s first sale of shares to the public.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q04', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The benchmark index of the Bombay Stock Exchange is the:', 'Sensex', 'Nifty', 'Dow Jones', 'Nikkei', 'A', 'The Sensex is the BSE''s benchmark index; the Nifty is the NSE''s.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q05', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The money market, dealing in short-term funds, is regulated by the:', 'RBI', 'SEBI', 'IRDAI', 'PFRDA', 'A', 'The RBI regulates the money market (short-term instruments like T-bills and call money).', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q06', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'Buying or selling shares based on unpublished price-sensitive information is:', 'Insider trading', 'Arbitrage', 'Hedging', 'Short selling', 'A', 'Insider trading — using confidential information — is illegal and policed by SEBI.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q07', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'A pooled investment vehicle managed professionally is a:', 'Mutual fund', 'Treasury Bill', 'Debenture', 'Promissory note', 'A', 'A mutual fund pools investors'' money and invests it in a diversified portfolio.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q08', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'Holding shares in electronic rather than physical form is called:', 'Dematerialisation', 'Securitisation', 'Nationalisation', 'Amortisation', 'A', 'Dematerialisation converts physical share certificates into electronic form (via NSDL/CDSL).', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q09', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'A rising market marked by optimism is called a:', 'Bull market', 'Bear market', 'Flat market', 'Grey market', 'A', 'A bull market denotes rising prices and investor optimism; a bear market is falling.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q10', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'The insurance sector in India is regulated by:', 'IRDAI', 'SEBI', 'RBI', 'PFRDA', 'A', 'The Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI) regulates insurance.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q11', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'Financial contracts whose value derives from an underlying asset are:', 'Derivatives', 'Equities', 'Fixed deposits', 'Currency notes', 'A', 'Derivatives (futures, options) derive their value from an underlying asset or index.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi-q12', 'upsc-economy-financial-markets-and-sebi', 'Foreign investors buying Indian stocks and bonds without controlling stakes are classed as:', 'Foreign Portfolio Investors (FPI)', 'Foreign Direct Investors (FDI)', 'NRIs only', 'Sovereign funds only', 'A', 'FPI (portfolio) investment is in securities without management control, unlike FDI.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q01', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The Planning Commission of India was set up in:', '1950', '1947', '1935', '1991', 'A', 'The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate Five-Year Plans.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q02', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'India''s Five-Year Plans were modelled partly on the planning experience of:', 'the USSR', 'the USA', 'Japan', 'Britain', 'A', 'India''s central planning drew on the Soviet (USSR) model of Five-Year Plans.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q03', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The Second Five-Year Plan, stressing heavy industry, was based on the model of:', 'P. C. Mahalanobis', 'Amartya Sen', 'Manmohan Singh', 'Vakil and Brahmananda', 'A', 'The Second Plan followed the Mahalanobis model emphasising heavy industry.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q04', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The economic reforms of 1991 are collectively known as:', 'LPG (Liberalisation, Privatisation, Globalisation)', 'GST', 'MGNREGA', 'Green Revolution', 'A', 'The 1991 reforms are called LPG — Liberalisation, Privatisation, and Globalisation.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q05', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The 1991 reforms were triggered by a crisis in the:', 'Balance of payments', 'Monsoon', 'Banking licences', 'Stock market', 'A', 'A severe 1991 balance-of-payments crisis forced India to liberalise.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q06', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The Finance Minister who spearheaded the 1991 reforms was:', 'Manmohan Singh', 'P. Chidambaram', 'Yashwant Sinha', 'Pranab Mukherjee', 'A', 'Manmohan Singh, as FM under PM Narasimha Rao, led the 1991 reforms.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q07', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The Planning Commission was replaced in 2015 by:', 'NITI Aayog', 'the Finance Commission', 'the RBI', 'the CAG', 'A', 'NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015 as a policy think tank.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q08', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The restrictive pre-1991 regime of licences and permits was nicknamed the:', 'Licence-Permit-Quota Raj', 'Green Revolution', 'Welfare State', 'Mixed Economy Charter', 'A', 'The pre-reform regime of pervasive controls was the ''Licence-Permit-Quota Raj''.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q09', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'NITI Aayog primarily functions as a:', 'Policy think tank promoting cooperative federalism', 'Fund-allocating body', 'Tax collector', 'Monetary authority', 'A', 'Unlike the Planning Commission, NITI Aayog is an advisory think tank, not a fund allocator.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q10', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The slow growth of the pre-1991 decades was pejoratively called the:', 'Hindu rate of growth', 'Great Leap', 'Dragon growth', 'Tiger economy', 'A', 'The sluggish ~3-4% pre-reform growth was dubbed the ''Hindu rate of growth''.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q11', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The 2016 law to resolve corporate insolvency in a time-bound manner is the:', 'Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code', 'Companies Act', 'SARFAESI Act', 'FEMA', 'A', 'The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC), 2016 provides a time-bound insolvency resolution process.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms-q12', 'upsc-economy-planning-and-economic-reforms', 'The campaign for self-reliant domestic manufacturing is called:', 'Atmanirbhar Bharat', 'Garibi Hatao', 'Look East', 'Shining India', 'A', '''Atmanirbhar Bharat'' (Self-Reliant India) promotes domestic manufacturing and self-reliance.', 11),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q01', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'MSME stands for Micro, Small and Medium:', 'Enterprises', 'Exports', 'Estates', 'Economies', 'A', 'MSME = Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises, a major source of employment.', 0),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q02', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The scheme giving output-linked incentives to boost manufacturing is the:', 'PLI scheme', 'MGNREGA', 'PM-KISAN', 'Ujjwala scheme', 'A', 'The Production-Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme rewards incremental manufacturing output.', 1),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q03', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The flagship programme for developing highways is:', 'Bharatmala', 'Sagarmala', 'UDAN', 'BharatNet', 'A', 'Bharatmala is the umbrella programme for highway and road development.', 2),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q04', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The Sagarmala programme focuses on the development of:', 'Ports and coastal economy', 'Airports', 'Rural roads', 'Power plants', 'A', 'Sagarmala aims at port-led development and modernising India''s coastline.', 3),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q05', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The UDAN scheme is aimed at improving:', 'Regional air connectivity', 'Rural broadband', 'Urban housing', 'River transport', 'A', 'UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Naagrik) promotes affordable regional air connectivity.', 4),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q06', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'In infrastructure financing, BOT stands for:', 'Build-Operate-Transfer', 'Buy-Own-Trade', 'Bond-Option-Trust', 'Basic Output Target', 'A', 'BOT (Build-Operate-Transfer) is a common PPP model for infrastructure projects.', 5),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q07', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'Partnerships between government and private firms for public projects are called:', 'Public-Private Partnerships (PPP)', 'Joint families', 'Cooperatives', 'Cartels', 'A', 'PPPs share the costs, risks, and rewards of infrastructure between the public and private sectors.', 6),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q08', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The ''eight core industries'' index includes coal, crude oil, steel, cement, electricity and:', 'Natural gas, refinery products, and fertilisers', 'Textiles and food processing', 'IT and telecom', 'Banking and insurance', 'A', 'The eight core industries are coal, crude oil, natural gas, refinery products, fertilisers, steel, cement, and electricity.', 7),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q09', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The initiative for integrated infrastructure planning across ministries is:', 'PM Gati Shakti', 'Make in India', 'Digital India', 'Skill India', 'A', 'PM Gati Shakti is a national master plan for coordinated, multimodal infrastructure planning.', 8),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q10', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The programme to provide broadband to rural gram panchayats is:', 'BharatNet', 'Bharatmala', 'Sagarmala', 'AMRUT', 'A', 'BharatNet aims to connect all gram panchayats with high-speed broadband.', 9),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q11', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'Long-term foreign investment in businesses with management interest is called:', 'Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)', 'Foreign Portfolio Investment', 'External commercial borrowing', 'Remittances', 'A', 'FDI is long-term investment giving a lasting interest and often management control in a business.', 10),
  ('upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure-q12', 'upsc-economy-industry-and-infrastructure', 'The Hybrid Annuity Model (HAM) is used to finance which kind of projects?', 'Highways/infrastructure (a PPP variant)', 'Agricultural loans', 'Mutual funds', 'Insurance policies', 'A', 'HAM is a hybrid PPP model mixing government annuity and private investment for highways.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The founder of Sikhism was:', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'Guru Arjan', 'Guru Tegh Bahadur', 'A', 'Guru Nanak (1469–1539) was the first Guru and founder of Sikhism.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'How many human Gurus were there in the Sikh tradition?', 'Ten', 'Five', 'Twelve', 'Seven', 'A', 'There were ten human Gurus, after whom the Guru Granth Sahib became the eternal Guru.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The Khalsa was founded in 1699 by:', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Hargobind', 'Banda Singh Bahadur', 'A', 'Guru Gobind Singh, the tenth Guru, founded the Khalsa at Anandpur Sahib in 1699.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The Adi Granth was compiled by:', 'Guru Arjan', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Angad', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'A', 'Guru Arjan, the fifth Guru, compiled the Adi Granth (Sikh scripture).', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The city of Amritsar was founded by:', 'Guru Ram Das', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'Maharaja Ranjit Singh', 'A', 'Guru Ram Das, the fourth Guru, founded Amritsar, home to the Golden Temple.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'Which Guru was executed by the Mughal emperor Aurangzeb?', 'Guru Tegh Bahadur', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Amar Das', 'Guru Angad', 'A', 'Guru Tegh Bahadur, the ninth Guru, was executed by Aurangzeb for defending religious freedom.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The Gurmukhi script was developed by:', 'Guru Angad', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Arjan', 'Guru Ram Das', 'A', 'Guru Angad, the second Guru, standardised and popularised the Gurmukhi script.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The community kitchen central to Sikh practice is the:', 'Langar', 'Sangat', 'Diwan', 'Akhara', 'A', 'The langar (free community kitchen) embodies equality; it was institutionalised by Guru Amar Das.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The Sikh Empire in Punjab in the early 19th century was built by:', 'Maharaja Ranjit Singh', 'Banda Singh Bahadur', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'Hari Singh Nalwa', 'A', 'Maharaja Ranjit Singh forged a powerful Sikh Empire with its capital at Lahore.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The eternal Guru of the Sikhs, declared by Guru Gobind Singh, is the:', 'Guru Granth Sahib', 'Adi Granth only', 'Dasam Granth', 'Janamsakhi', 'A', 'Guru Gobind Singh declared the Guru Granth Sahib the eternal Guru after the ten human Gurus.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The Harmandir Sahib (Golden Temple) construction was overseen by:', 'Guru Arjan', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Gobind Singh', 'Guru Tegh Bahadur', 'A', 'Guru Arjan oversaw the building of the Harmandir Sahib at Amritsar.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-sikhism-and-the-gurus', 'The concept of Miri-Piri (temporal and spiritual power) was introduced by:', 'Guru Hargobind', 'Guru Nanak', 'Guru Amar Das', 'Guru Ram Das', 'A', 'Guru Hargobind, the sixth Guru, introduced Miri-Piri, militarising the community.', 11),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q01', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The Qutb Minar in Delhi was begun by:', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak', 'Akbar', 'Shah Jahan', 'Sher Shah Suri', 'A', 'Qutb-ud-din Aibak began the Qutb Minar; Iltutmish completed it.', 0),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q02', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The Taj Mahal was built by which Mughal emperor?', 'Shah Jahan', 'Akbar', 'Aurangzeb', 'Humayun', 'A', 'Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal at Agra in memory of Mumtaz Mahal.', 1),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q03', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'Fatehpur Sikri, with the Buland Darwaza, was built by:', 'Akbar', 'Shah Jahan', 'Babur', 'Aurangzeb', 'A', 'Akbar built Fatehpur Sikri in red sandstone, including the towering Buland Darwaza.', 2),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q04', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'Which tomb introduced the Persian charbagh garden and is a precursor to the Taj Mahal?', 'Humayun''s Tomb', 'Akbar''s Tomb', 'Itmad-ud-Daula''s Tomb', 'Jahangir''s Tomb', 'A', 'Humayun''s Tomb in Delhi introduced the charbagh layout and double dome.', 3),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q05', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The decorative inlay of semi-precious stones seen in the Taj Mahal is called:', 'Pietra dura', 'Fresco', 'Filigree', 'Terracotta', 'A', 'Pietra dura is the inlay of semi-precious stones into marble, used lavishly in the Taj Mahal.', 4),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q06', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The older Indian post-and-lintel building method is called:', 'Trabeate', 'Arcuate', 'Cantilever', 'Corbel', 'A', 'The trabeate (post-and-lintel) style predates the arcuate (true arch) style Islam introduced.', 5),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q07', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The Red Fort and Jama Masjid of Delhi were built by:', 'Shah Jahan', 'Akbar', 'Humayun', 'Babur', 'A', 'Shah Jahan built the Red Fort (Lal Qila) and the Jama Masjid in Delhi.', 6),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q08', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'A defining feature of Islamic architecture, avoiding human figures, is the use of:', 'Calligraphy and geometric/arabesque designs', 'Portrait sculpture', 'Animal frescoes', 'Idol niches', 'A', 'Islamic architecture favours calligraphy and geometric/arabesque ornament over figural images.', 7),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q09', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The Gol Gumbaz at Bijapur is famous for its:', 'Whispering gallery and huge dome', 'Leaning tower', 'Rock-cut caves', 'Stepwell', 'A', 'The Gol Gumbaz has one of the world''s largest domes and a famous whispering gallery.', 8),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q10', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The Alai Darwaza was added to the Qutb complex by:', 'Alauddin Khalji', 'Iltutmish', 'Balban', 'Firoz Shah Tughlaq', 'A', 'Alauddin Khalji added the Alai Darwaza, an early example of a true dome and arch.', 9),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q11', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The vertical tower attached to mosques for the call to prayer is the:', 'Minaret', 'Gopuram', 'Shikhara', 'Vimana', 'A', 'The minaret is the tower from which the call to prayer is given; gopuram/shikhara are Hindu temple features.', 10),
  ('upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture-q12', 'upsc-medieval-history-indo-islamic-architecture', 'The colonial-era style blending Indian and Islamic motifs with European forms is called:', 'Indo-Saracenic', 'Gothic only', 'Baroque', 'Dravidian', 'A', 'The Indo-Saracenic style merged Indo-Islamic elements with European architecture under the British.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Munda uprising (Ulgulan) was led by:', 'Birsa Munda', 'Sidhu Murmu', 'Tantia Bhil', 'Alluri Sitarama Raju', 'A', 'Birsa Munda led the Munda rebellion (Ulgulan) in the Chotanagpur region around 1899–1900.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Santhal Rebellion (1855–56) was led by:', 'Sidhu and Kanhu', 'Birsa Munda', 'Bhagat Singh', 'Chittaranjan Das', 'A', 'The Santhal Rebellion against moneylenders and the British was led by brothers Sidhu and Kanhu.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'Gandhi''s first satyagraha in India, in 1917, was the:', 'Champaran Satyagraha', 'Bardoli Satyagraha', 'Kheda Satyagraha', 'Salt Satyagraha', 'A', 'The Champaran Satyagraha (1917) against forced indigo cultivation was Gandhi''s first in India.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Bardoli Satyagraha (1928) was led by:', 'Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Bhagat Singh', 'C. Rajagopalachari', 'A', 'The Bardoli Satyagraha, a no-tax peasant movement, was led by Vallabhbhai Patel, who earned the title ''Sardar''.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The All India Trade Union Congress (AITUC) was founded in:', '1920', '1885', '1947', '1936', 'A', 'The AITUC, India''s first major trade union body, was founded in 1920.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Tebhaga movement of sharecroppers took place in:', 'Bengal', 'Punjab', 'Kerala', 'Bihar', 'A', 'The Tebhaga movement (1946) demanded a larger crop share for sharecroppers in Bengal.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Telangana peasant movement was directed against the:', 'Nizam of Hyderabad', 'British Raj', 'Nawab of Awadh', 'Zamindars of Bengal', 'A', 'The Telangana movement (1946–51) was an armed peasant struggle against the Nizam''s feudal rule.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The All India Kisan Sabha was formed in:', '1936', '1920', '1885', '1942', 'A', 'The All India Kisan Sabha, mobilising peasants nationally, was formed in 1936.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Deccan Riots of 1875 were directed mainly against:', 'Moneylenders', 'Factory owners', 'Railway companies', 'Tea planters', 'A', 'The Deccan Riots targeted moneylenders (sahukars) who exploited indebted peasants.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Congress Socialist Party was formed within the Congress in:', '1934', '1920', '1947', '1885', 'A', 'The Congress Socialist Party was founded in 1934 by Jayaprakash Narayan, Acharya Narendra Deva and others.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Moplah (Malabar) rebellion of 1921 occurred in present-day:', 'Kerala', 'Tamil Nadu', 'Karnataka', 'Andhra Pradesh', 'A', 'The Moplah rebellion took place in the Malabar region of present-day Kerala.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-peasant-tribal-and-left-movements', 'The Kheda Satyagraha (1918) demanded relief from land revenue due to:', 'Crop failure/famine', 'War taxes', 'Salt tax', 'Forest laws', 'A', 'The Kheda Satyagraha sought remission of land revenue after crop failure in Gujarat.', 11),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q01', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The integration of the princely states was led chiefly by:', 'Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Rajendra Prasad', 'C. Rajagopalachari', 'A', 'Sardar Patel, aided by V. P. Menon, integrated over 560 princely states into India.', 0),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q02', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'Hyderabad was integrated into India in 1948 through:', 'Operation Polo', 'Operation Vijay', 'Operation Blue Star', 'Operation Cactus', 'A', 'Operation Polo (1948) was the police action that integrated Hyderabad into India.', 1),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q03', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The first state to be created on a linguistic basis (1953) was:', 'Andhra', 'Kerala', 'Gujarat', 'Maharashtra', 'A', 'Andhra became the first linguistic state in 1953 after Potti Sriramulu''s death.', 2),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q04', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The States Reorganisation Act, redrawing states on linguistic lines, was passed in:', '1956', '1947', '1950', '1966', 'A', 'The States Reorganisation Act, 1956 reorganised Indian states largely on a linguistic basis.', 3),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q05', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'Goa was liberated from Portuguese rule in:', '1961', '1947', '1975', '1956', 'A', 'Goa was liberated from Portuguese control in 1961 via Operation Vijay.', 4),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q06', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'India''s foreign policy under Nehru was based on:', 'Non-alignment', 'Military alliance with the USA', 'Membership of the Warsaw Pact', 'Isolationism', 'A', 'Nehru championed non-alignment, steering clear of Cold War blocs.', 5),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q07', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The 1971 India-Pakistan war led to the creation of:', 'Bangladesh', 'Nepal', 'Sri Lanka', 'Myanmar', 'A', 'The 1971 war resulted in the independence of East Pakistan as Bangladesh.', 6),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q08', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The five principles of peaceful coexistence articulated by India and China were called:', 'Panchsheel', 'Panchayat', 'Panchamrit', 'Panchvarsha', 'A', 'Panchsheel (1954) set out five principles of peaceful coexistence between India and China.', 7),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q09', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'India''s first general elections were held in:', '1951–52', '1947', '1950', '1957', 'A', 'India held its first general elections in 1951–52, based on universal adult franchise.', 8),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q10', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The border war with China took place in:', '1962', '1965', '1971', '1948', 'A', 'India and China fought a border war in 1962.', 9),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q11', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The accession of Junagadh was ultimately settled by:', 'A plebiscite', 'Military conquest only', 'A UN mandate', 'Partition', 'A', 'Junagadh''s accession to India was confirmed through a plebiscite in 1948.', 10),
  ('upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation-q12', 'upsc-modern-history-post-independence-consolidation', 'The 1955 conference of Afro-Asian nations that promoted non-alignment was held at:', 'Bandung', 'Belgrade', 'Geneva', 'Colombo', 'A', 'The 1955 Bandung Conference (Indonesia) advanced Afro-Asian solidarity and non-alignment.', 11),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q01', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'A body starts from rest and accelerates at 2 m/s². How far does it travel in 5 s?', '20 m', '25 m', '50 m', '10 m', 'B', 's = ut + ½at² = 0 + ½(2)(25) = 25 m.', 0),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q02', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'A stone is dropped from rest. Its velocity after 3 s (g = 10 m/s²) is:', '10 m/s', '30 m/s', '20 m/s', '45 m/s', 'B', 'v = u + gt = 0 + 10 × 3 = 30 m/s.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q03', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'The area under a velocity–time graph represents:', 'Acceleration', 'Displacement', 'Jerk', 'Average speed', 'B', 'Integrating velocity over time gives displacement, which is the area under the v–t curve.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q04', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'A car moving at 20 m/s decelerates uniformly and stops in 100 m. The deceleration is:', '2 m/s²', '10 m/s²', '1 m/s²', '4 m/s²', 'A', 'Using v² = u² + 2as: 0 = 400 + 2a(100), so a = −2 m/s².', 3),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q05', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'The distance covered in the n-th second by a body from rest with acceleration a is:', '(a/2)(2n − 1)', 'an', '½an²', 'a(n − 1)', 'A', 's_nth = u + (a/2)(2n − 1); with u = 0 it reduces to (a/2)(2n − 1).', 4),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q06', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'A ball thrown vertically up with 20 m/s reaches a maximum height of (g = 10 m/s²):', '20 m', '10 m', '30 m', '40 m', 'A', 'At the top v = 0, so h = u²/2g = 400/20 = 20 m.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q07', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'If velocity is negative and acceleration is positive, the body is:', 'Slowing down', 'Speeding up', 'At rest', 'Moving at constant speed', 'A', 'Opposite signs of v and a mean the speed (magnitude) is decreasing.', 6),
  ('jee-physics-kinematics-1d-q08', 'jee-physics-kinematics-1d', 'Two balls are dropped 1 s apart from the same height. As they fall, the gap between them:', 'Stays constant', 'Decreases', 'First increases then decreases', 'Increases', 'D', 'The earlier ball is always faster, so the separation grows with time.', 7),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q01', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'The moment of inertia of a solid sphere about a diameter is:', 'MR²', '(2/5)MR²', '(1/2)MR²', '(2/3)MR²', 'B', 'A uniform solid sphere has I = (2/5)MR² about any diameter.', 0),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q02', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'The rotational analogue of force is:', 'Momentum', 'Torque', 'Impulse', 'Power', 'B', 'Torque τ = Iα plays the role of force F = ma in rotation.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q03', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'A skater pulls in her arms while spinning. Her angular velocity:', 'Stays the same', 'Decreases', 'Increases', 'Becomes zero', 'C', 'With torque zero, L = Iω is conserved; reducing I increases ω.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q04', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'Which body reaches the bottom of an incline first while rolling without slipping?', 'Solid sphere', 'Hollow sphere', 'Ring', 'Hollow cylinder', 'A', 'The solid sphere has the smallest I/MR² (2/5), giving the largest acceleration.', 3),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q05', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'The parallel axis theorem states I = :', 'I_cm − Md²', 'I_cm + Md²', 'I_cm + ½Md²', '2I_cm + Md²', 'B', 'I about a parallel axis equals the centre-of-mass value plus Md².', 4),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q06', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'For rolling without slipping, the velocity of the contact point with the ground is:', 'Zero', 'v/2', '2v', 'v', 'A', 'In pure rolling, the instantaneous velocity of the contact point is zero.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q07', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'The rotational kinetic energy of a body is:', '½Iω²', 'Iω²', '½Iω', '½I²ω', 'A', 'Rotational KE = ½Iω², analogous to ½mv² for translation.', 6),
  ('jee-physics-rotational-motion-q08', 'jee-physics-rotational-motion', 'A disc of moment of inertia 2 kg·m² spins at 3 rad/s. Its angular momentum is:', '3 kg·m²/s', '9 kg·m²/s', '6 kg·m²/s', '5 kg·m²/s', 'C', 'L = Iω = 2 × 3 = 6 kg·m²/s.', 7),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q01', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'The shape of a molecule with sp³ hybridisation and no lone pairs is:', 'Trigonal planar', 'Tetrahedral', 'Linear', 'Octahedral', 'B', 'Four equivalent sp³ orbitals point to the corners of a tetrahedron (109.5°).', 0),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q02', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'The bond angle in a water molecule is approximately:', '90°', '109.5°', '104.5°', '120°', 'C', 'Two lone pairs on the sp³ oxygen compress the H–O–H angle to about 104.5°.', 1),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q03', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'Which molecule has a zero net dipole moment despite polar bonds?', 'NH₃', 'CO₂', 'HCl', 'H₂O', 'B', 'CO₂ is linear and symmetric, so the two bond dipoles cancel exactly.', 2),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q04', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'The bond order of the oxygen molecule (O₂) from MO theory is:', '2', '1', '1.5', '3', 'A', 'O₂ has a bond order of 2 and two unpaired electrons, making it paramagnetic.', 3),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q05', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'According to Fajans'' rules, covalent character increases with:', 'Large cation, small anion', 'Small cation, large anion', 'Low cation charge', 'Large anion, large cation', 'B', 'A small, highly charged cation polarises a large anion, increasing covalent character.', 4),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q06', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'The hybridisation of carbon in ethyne (C₂H₂) is:', 'sp³d', 'sp²', 'sp³', 'sp', 'D', 'The triple-bonded carbons in ethyne are sp hybridised, giving a linear molecule.', 5),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q07', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'The unusually high boiling point of water is mainly due to:', 'Ionic bonding', 'Van der Waals forces', 'Hydrogen bonding', 'Metallic bonding', 'C', 'Extensive hydrogen bonding between water molecules requires extra energy to break.', 6),
  ('jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding-q08', 'jee-chemistry-chemical-bonding', 'In the ammonium ion (NH₄⁺), the fourth N–H bond is a:', 'Coordinate bond', 'Metallic bond', 'Hydrogen bond', 'Ionic bond', 'A', 'The lone pair on nitrogen forms a coordinate (dative) bond with the proton.', 7),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q01', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'For the equation x² − 5x + 6 = 0, the sum of the roots is:', '6', '5', '−5', '−6', 'B', 'Sum of roots = −b/a = −(−5)/1 = 5 (roots are 2 and 3).', 0),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q02', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'The discriminant of 2x² + 3x + 5 = 0 is:', '31', '−49', '49', '−31', 'D', 'D = b² − 4ac = 9 − 40 = −31, so the roots are complex.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q03', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'If the roots of a quadratic are equal, the discriminant is:', 'Negative', 'Zero', 'Irrational', 'Positive', 'B', 'Equal real roots occur exactly when D = b² − 4ac = 0.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q04', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'The quadratic equation whose roots are 3 and −2 is:', 'x² − 5x + 6 = 0', 'x² + x − 6 = 0', 'x² − x − 6 = 0', 'x² + 5x + 6 = 0', 'C', 'Sum = 1, product = −6, so x² − (1)x + (−6) = x² − x − 6 = 0.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q05', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'For ax² + bx + c > 0 to hold for all real x, we require:', 'a > 0 and D > 0', 'a < 0 and D > 0', 'a > 0 and D < 0', 'a < 0 and D < 0', 'C', 'An upward parabola (a > 0) that never touches the x-axis (D < 0) is always positive.', 4),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q06', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'If α and β are roots of x² − 6x + 8 = 0, then α² + β² equals:', '16', '20', '36', '52', 'B', 'α² + β² = (α + β)² − 2αβ = 36 − 16 = 20.', 5),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q07', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'The vertex of the parabola y = x² − 4x + 7 lies at x =:', '−2', '1', '4', '2', 'D', 'The vertex is at x = −b/(2a) = 4/2 = 2.', 6),
  ('jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations-q08', 'jee-mathematics-quadratic-equations', 'The product of the roots of 3x² − 12x + 9 = 0 is:', '3', '4', '1', '9', 'A', 'Product = c/a = 9/3 = 3.', 7),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q01', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'A net force of 12 N acts on a 3 kg block. Its acceleration is:', '4 m/s²', '36 m/s²', '9 m/s²', '2 m/s²', 'A', 'By Newton''s second law a = F/m = 12/3 = 4 m/s².', 0),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q02', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'Newton''s third law force pairs always act on:', 'The same body', 'Two different bodies', 'Massless objects only', 'The Earth only', 'B', 'Action and reaction are equal, opposite, and act on different bodies.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q03', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'A block on a horizontal surface has mu_s = 0.5 and mass 4 kg (g = 10). Maximum static friction is:', '20 N', '40 N', '2 N', '10 N', 'A', 'f_max = mu_s x N = 0.5 x 4 x 10 = 20 N.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q04', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'The angle of repose theta for a surface with coefficient of friction mu satisfies:', 'sin(theta) = mu', 'cos(theta) = mu', 'theta = mu', 'tan(theta) = mu', 'D', 'A block just slides when tan(theta) equals the coefficient of static friction.', 3),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q05', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'A person of mass 50 kg stands in a lift accelerating up at 2 m/s² (g = 10). Apparent weight is:', '500 N', '400 N', '600 N', '100 N', 'C', 'Apparent weight = m(g + a) = 50 x 12 = 600 N.', 4),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q06', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'Impulse is equal to the change in:', 'Kinetic energy', 'Momentum', 'Acceleration', 'Power', 'B', 'Impulse J = F x t equals the change in momentum, by the impulse-momentum theorem.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q07', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'Two blocks of 2 kg and 3 kg connected by a string are pulled by 20 N on a frictionless floor. Acceleration is:', '10 m/s²', '4 m/s²', '6.7 m/s²', '2 m/s²', 'B', 'a = F/(m1 + m2) = 20/5 = 4 m/s².', 6),
  ('jee-physics-laws-of-motion-q08', 'jee-physics-laws-of-motion', 'A body in equilibrium under three forces means the forces:', 'Form a closed triangle', 'Are perpendicular', 'Are all equal', 'Have zero magnitude', 'A', 'Three concurrent forces in equilibrium add vectorially to zero, forming a closed triangle.', 7),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q01', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'A force of 10 N moves a body 5 m in its own direction. Work done is:', '2 J', '15 J', '0 J', '50 J', 'D', 'W = F x s x cos(0) = 10 x 5 = 50 J.', 0),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q02', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'The kinetic energy of a 2 kg body moving at 3 m/s is:', '9 J', '6 J', '18 J', '3 J', 'A', 'KE = 0.5 x m x v² = 0.5 x 2 x 9 = 9 J.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q03', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'Work done by a force perpendicular to the displacement is:', 'Zero', 'Equal to F x s', 'Maximum', 'Negative', 'A', 'W = Fs cos(90) = 0; a perpendicular force does no work.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q04', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'A spring of constant 200 N/m is stretched 0.1 m. Potential energy stored is:', '1 J', '2 J', '20 J', '10 J', 'A', 'PE = 0.5 x k x x² = 0.5 x 200 x 0.01 = 1 J.', 3),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q05', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'In a perfectly inelastic collision, the conserved quantity is:', 'Kinetic energy', 'Momentum', 'Both KE and momentum', 'Neither', 'B', 'Momentum is conserved in all collisions; kinetic energy is lost when inelastic.', 4),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q06', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'A 1000 W motor lifting a load does how much work in 10 s?', '10000 J', '1000 J', '100000 J', '100 J', 'A', 'W = P x t = 1000 x 10 = 10000 J.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q07', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'For a perfectly elastic collision, the coefficient of restitution e equals:', '0', '0.5', '1', '2', 'C', 'e = 1 for elastic collisions; e = 0 for perfectly inelastic ones.', 6),
  ('jee-physics-work-energy-power-q08', 'jee-physics-work-energy-power', 'The instantaneous power delivered by a force F to a body moving at velocity v is:', 'F/v', 'F + v', 'F x v', '0.5 F v²', 'C', 'Instantaneous power P equals the dot product F x v.', 7),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q01', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'The escape velocity from Earth is approximately:', '3.0 km/s', '7.9 km/s', '11.2 km/s', '30 km/s', 'C', 'Earth''s escape velocity is about 11.2 km/s, equal to sqrt(2GM/R).', 0),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q02', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'If the distance between two masses is doubled, the gravitational force becomes:', 'One-quarter', 'Four times', 'Double', 'Half', 'A', 'Force varies as 1/r²; doubling r reduces it to one-quarter.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q03', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'The value of g at a height equal to Earth''s radius R above the surface is:', 'g/4', 'g/2', 'g', 'g/9', 'A', 'At height R, distance from centre is 2R, so g'' = g/(2)² = g/4.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q04', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'Kepler''s third law states that the square of the orbital period is proportional to:', 'Cube of the radius', 'Square of the radius', 'Orbital radius', 'Mass of the planet', 'A', 'T² is proportional to r³, Kepler''s law of periods.', 3),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q05', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'The orbital velocity of a satellite close to Earth''s surface relates to escape velocity by:', 'v_e = sqrt(2) v_o', 'v_e = 2 v_o', 'v_e = v_o', 'v_e = v_o/2', 'A', 'Escape velocity is sqrt(2) times the orbital velocity.', 4),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q06', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'The period of a geostationary satellite is:', '365 days', '12 hours', '1 hour', '24 hours', 'D', 'A geostationary satellite matches Earth''s rotation with a 24-hour period.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q07', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'The gravitational potential energy of two masses separated by r is:', '+GMm/r', '-GMm/r', '-GMm/r²', 'GMm/r²', 'B', 'Gravitational PE is negative: U = -GMm/r, taken zero at infinity.', 6),
  ('jee-physics-gravitation-q08', 'jee-physics-gravitation', 'At the centre of the Earth, the acceleration due to gravity is:', 'Zero', 'Equal to surface g', 'Infinite', 'Maximum', 'A', 'g decreases linearly with depth and is zero at the centre.', 7),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q01', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'The time period of a simple pendulum of length L is:', '2*pi*sqrt(L/g)', '2*pi*sqrt(g/L)', '2*pi*sqrt(m/k)', 'sqrt(L/g)', 'A', 'The pendulum period is 2*pi*sqrt(L/g), independent of mass.', 0),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q02', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'In SHM, the acceleration is maximum at:', 'The mean position', 'Halfway', 'The extreme position', 'Everywhere equal', 'C', 'Acceleration a = -omega²x is maximum where displacement x is largest, at the extremes.', 1),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q03', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'A spring-mass system has k = 100 N/m and m = 1 kg. Its angular frequency is:', '5 rad/s', '1 rad/s', '100 rad/s', '10 rad/s', 'D', 'omega = sqrt(k/m) = sqrt(100) = 10 rad/s.', 2),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q04', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'Two tuning forks of 256 Hz and 260 Hz produce beats at a frequency of:', '2 Hz', '8 Hz', '4 Hz', '516 Hz', 'C', 'Beat frequency equals the difference, 260 - 256 = 4 Hz.', 3),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q05', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'The velocity of a wave with frequency 50 Hz and wavelength 4 m is:', '200 m/s', '12.5 m/s', '54 m/s', '100 m/s', 'A', 'v = f x lambda = 50 x 4 = 200 m/s.', 4),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q06', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'The total energy of a particle in SHM is proportional to:', 'Amplitude', 'Frequency only', 'Square of amplitude', 'Inverse of amplitude', 'C', 'Total energy E = 0.5 k A² is proportional to the square of the amplitude.', 5),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q07', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'The speed of a transverse wave on a stretched string depends on tension T and linear density mu as:', 'sqrt(T/mu)', 'sqrt(mu/T)', 'T x mu', 'T/mu', 'A', 'Wave speed on a string is v = sqrt(T/mu).', 6),
  ('jee-physics-shm-waves-q08', 'jee-physics-shm-waves', 'When a source of sound approaches a stationary observer, the observed frequency:', 'Decreases', 'Increases', 'Stays the same', 'Becomes zero', 'B', 'By the Doppler effect, an approaching source raises the observed pitch.', 7),
