  ('jee-mathematics-conic-sections-q08', 'jee-mathematics-conic-sections', 'For the ellipse x squared over a squared plus y squared over b squared equal one with a greater than b, b squared equals:', 'a squared plus e squared', 'a squared times (e squared minus 1)', 'a squared times e squared', 'a squared times (1 minus e squared)', 'D', 'For an ellipse, b squared equals a squared times (1 minus e squared).', 7),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q01', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'The order of a differential equation is the:', 'Highest derivative present', 'Power of the highest derivative', 'Number of terms', 'Degree of the polynomial', 'A', 'The order is the highest-order derivative appearing in the equation.', 0),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q02', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'The integrating factor of dy/dx plus P y equals Q is:', 'The integral of Q dx', 'Exponential of the integral of P dx', 'P times Q', 'One over P', 'B', 'The integrating factor is the exponential of the integral of P with respect to x.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q03', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'To solve a homogeneous differential equation, the usual substitution is:', 'x equals y squared', 'y equals v x', 'y equals constant', 'x equals v over y', 'B', 'Substituting y equals v x reduces a homogeneous equation to a separable one.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q04', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'The general solution of an nth-order differential equation contains how many arbitrary constants?', 'One', 'Two', 'Zero', 'n', 'D', 'A general solution of order n carries n arbitrary constants.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q05', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'Which method solves dy/dx equals f(x) times g(y)?', 'Integrating factor', 'Substitution y equals v x', 'Variable separation', 'Partial fractions only', 'C', 'Such an equation separates the variables onto opposite sides before integrating.', 4),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q06', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'The degree of (dy/dx) squared plus y equals zero is:', 'One', 'Two', 'Three', 'Zero', 'B', 'The highest derivative appears to the power two, so the degree is two.', 5),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q07', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'A first-order linear differential equation has the form dy/dx plus P(x) y equals:', 'Zero always', 'A constant only', 'y squared', 'Q(x)', 'D', 'The standard linear form is dy/dx plus P(x) y equals Q(x).', 6),
  ('jee-mathematics-differential-equations-q08', 'jee-mathematics-differential-equations', 'The solution of dy/dx equals k y represents:', 'Linear growth', 'Exponential growth or decay', 'Constant value', 'Oscillation', 'B', 'dy/dx equals k y integrates to an exponential, giving growth or decay.', 7),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q01', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'The slope of the tangent to a curve at a point equals the:', 'Value of the function', 'First derivative there', 'Second derivative there', 'Integral there', 'B', 'The slope of the tangent at a point is the first derivative at that point.', 0),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q02', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'A function is increasing on an interval where its first derivative is:', 'Positive', 'Zero', 'Negative', 'Undefined', 'A', 'A positive first derivative means the function is increasing.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q03', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'At a local minimum the second derivative is generally:', 'Negative', 'Infinite', 'Zero only', 'Positive', 'D', 'A positive second derivative at a critical point indicates a local minimum.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q04', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'The slope of the normal to a curve is:', 'Equal to the tangent slope', 'Negative reciprocal of the tangent slope', 'Zero always', 'The second derivative', 'B', 'The normal slope is the negative reciprocal of the tangent slope.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q05', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'At a point of inflection, the second derivative:', 'Is always positive', 'Is undefined always', 'Changes sign', 'Equals the first derivative', 'C', 'At an inflection point the second derivative changes sign and concavity flips.', 4),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q06', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'Critical points of a function occur where the first derivative is:', 'Zero or undefined', 'Maximum', 'Always positive', 'Constant', 'A', 'Critical points are where the first derivative is zero or fails to exist.', 5),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q07', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'For a small change, the approximate change in y is given by:', 'dx over f''(x)', 'f(x) times dx', 'f''(x) times dx', 'f''''(x) times dx', 'C', 'The linear approximation gives dy approximately equal to f''(x) times dx.', 6),
  ('jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives-q08', 'jee-mathematics-application-of-derivatives', 'To find the absolute maximum on a closed interval, one must also check the:', 'Endpoints', 'Origin only', 'Asymptotes', 'Inflection points only', 'A', 'The absolute extremum may occur at the endpoints, so they must be checked.', 7),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q01', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'The area under a non-negative curve y equals f(x) from a to b is given by:', 'The definite integral of f from a to b', 'The derivative of f', 'f(b) minus f(a)', 'The slope at b', 'A', 'The area equals the definite integral of f(x) from a to b.', 0),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q02', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'The area enclosed by a circle of radius r is:', '2 pi r', '4 pi r squared', 'pi r', 'pi r squared', 'D', 'The area of a circle of radius r is pi times r squared.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q03', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'The area between two curves uses the integral of:', 'The derivative of each', 'Their product', 'Their sum', 'Upper curve minus lower curve', 'D', 'The area between curves is the integral of the upper minus the lower function.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q04', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'If a region lies below the x-axis, the definite integral over it is:', 'Positive', 'Negative', 'Zero', 'Infinite', 'B', 'Below the x-axis the function is negative, so the integral there is negative.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q05', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'The area of an ellipse with semi-axes a and b is:', '2 pi a b', 'pi (a plus b)', 'pi a b', 'pi a squared b', 'C', 'The area of an ellipse is pi times a times b.', 4),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q06', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'The limits of integration for the area between two curves are found from their:', 'Points of intersection', 'Maximum values', 'Derivatives', 'Asymptotes', 'A', 'The integration limits are the x-coordinates where the two curves intersect.', 5),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q07', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'When integrating with respect to y, the strip used is:', 'Vertical', 'Horizontal', 'Diagonal', 'Circular', 'B', 'Integration with respect to y sums horizontal strips of width dy.', 6),
  ('jee-mathematics-area-under-curves-q08', 'jee-mathematics-area-under-curves', 'For a symmetric region, a useful shortcut is to integrate over half and then:', 'Subtract the result', 'Double the result', 'Square the result', 'Ignore symmetry', 'B', 'Using symmetry, integrate over half the region and double the answer.', 7),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q01', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The most frequently occurring value in a data set is the:', 'Mean', 'Median', 'Mode', 'Range', 'C', 'The mode is the value that occurs most often.', 0),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q02', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The standard deviation is the square root of the:', 'Mean', 'Mode', 'Median', 'Variance', 'D', 'Standard deviation is the positive square root of the variance.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q03', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The contrapositive of the statement if p then q is:', 'If q then p', 'If not q then not p', 'If not p then not q', 'p and not q', 'B', 'The contrapositive of if p then q is if not q then not p, which is equivalent.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q04', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The conjunction of two statements (p and q) is true only when:', 'At least one is true', 'Both are true', 'Both are false', 'They differ', 'B', 'A conjunction is true only when both component statements are true.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q05', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The median of the data 3, 5, 7, 9 is:', 'Five', 'Seven', 'Six', 'Eight', 'C', 'With an even count, the median is the average of 5 and 7, which is 6.', 4),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q06', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'A statement that is always true regardless of its components is called a:', 'Contradiction', 'Tautology', 'Converse', 'Negation', 'B', 'A tautology is true for all truth values of its components.', 5),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q07', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The disjunction (p or q) is false only when:', 'Both are false', 'One is true', 'Both are true', 'They differ', 'A', 'An inclusive or is false only when both statements are false.', 6),
  ('jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning-q08', 'jee-mathematics-statistics-reasoning', 'The mean of the data 2, 4, 6, 8 is:', 'Four', 'Five', 'Six', 'Seven', 'B', 'The sum 20 divided by 4 values gives a mean of 5.', 7),
