  ('jee-mathematics-heights-distances-q02', 'jee-mathematics-heights-distances', 'At an angle of elevation of 45 degrees, the height of an object equals its:', 'Horizontal distance', 'Half the distance', 'Twice the distance', 'Square of the distance', 'A', 'Since tan 45 degrees is one, the height equals the horizontal distance.', 1),
  ('jee-mathematics-heights-distances-q03', 'jee-mathematics-heights-distances', 'The angle of elevation and the angle of depression for the same line of sight are:', 'Complementary', 'Equal', 'Supplementary', 'Always 90 degrees', 'B', 'They are alternate angles for the same line of sight, so they are equal.', 2),
  ('jee-mathematics-heights-distances-q04', 'jee-mathematics-heights-distances', 'A tower casts a shadow equal to its height when the sun''s elevation is:', '30 degrees', '90 degrees', '60 degrees', '45 degrees', 'D', 'Equal height and shadow give tan equal to one, so the elevation is 45 degrees.', 3),
  ('jee-mathematics-heights-distances-q05', 'jee-mathematics-heights-distances', 'For a height h at horizontal distance d, the angle of elevation satisfies tan theta equals:', 'h over d', 'd over h', 'h times d', 'd minus h', 'A', 'tan theta equals the opposite over adjacent, that is h over d.', 4),
