  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q03', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'The roots are real and distinct when the discriminant D is:', 'Greater than 0', 'Equal to 0', 'Less than 0', 'Equal to a', 'A', 'D = b² − 4ac > 0 gives two distinct real roots.', 2),
  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q04', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'If D = 0, the roots are:', 'Real and equal', 'Complex', 'Distinct real', 'Irrational', 'A', 'A zero discriminant gives two equal real roots.', 3),
  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q05', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'For a quadratic with real coefficients, complex roots occur:', 'In conjugate pairs', 'Singly', 'As three roots', 'Never', 'A', 'Complex roots of a real polynomial come in conjugate pairs.', 4),
  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q06', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'The vertex (extremum) of y = ax² + bx + c is at x =:', '−b/2a', '−b/a', 'c/a', 'b/2a', 'A', 'The parabola''s extremum is at x = −b/2a.', 5),
  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q07', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'A quadratic ax² + bx + c (a > 0) has a minimum value; it is positive for all x when:', 'D < 0', 'D > 0', 'D = 0', 'b = 0', 'A', 'With a > 0 and D < 0, the quadratic is always positive.', 6),
  ('jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations-q08', 'jee-adv-math-quadratic-equations', 'If both roots of a quadratic lie on opposite sides of a number k, then:', 'f(k) < 0 (for a > 0)', 'f(k) > 0', 'f(k) = a', 'f(k) = ∞', 'A', 'For a > 0, a·f(k) < 0 means k lies between the roots.', 7),
