  ('neet-physics-atoms-q08', 'neet-physics-atoms', 'The Rydberg formula gives the reciprocal of the wavelength of spectral lines as:', 'R(1/n₁² − 1/n₂²)', 'R(n₁ − n₂)', 'R/n²', 'Rn²', 'A', '1/λ = R(1/n₁² − 1/n₂²) predicts hydrogen''s spectral line wavelengths.', 7),
  ('neet-physics-atoms-q09', 'neet-physics-atoms', 'Bohr''s model successfully explains the spectrum of:', 'Hydrogen (single-electron atoms)', 'All atoms', 'Molecules', 'Metals only', 'A', 'The Bohr model works for hydrogen and hydrogen-like ions but fails for multi-electron atoms.', 8),
  ('neet-physics-atoms-q10', 'neet-physics-atoms', 'In stationary orbits, electrons:', 'Do not radiate energy', 'Continuously radiate', 'Absorb energy always', 'Have zero energy', 'A', 'Bohr postulated that electrons in allowed orbits do not radiate energy.', 9),
  ('neet-physics-atoms-q11', 'neet-physics-atoms', 'The Paschen series of hydrogen lies in which region?', 'Infrared', 'Visible', 'Ultraviolet', 'Gamma', 'A', 'The Paschen series (transitions to n=3) lies in the infrared.', 10),
  ('neet-physics-atoms-q12', 'neet-physics-atoms', 'The radius of the electron''s orbit in the Bohr model is proportional to:', 'n²', '1/n²', 'n', '1/n', 'A', 'The Bohr orbit radius rₙ ∝ n² (rₙ = n²·a₀ for hydrogen).', 11),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q01', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'The particles found in the nucleus (nucleons) are:', 'Protons and neutrons', 'Protons and electrons', 'Electrons and neutrons', 'Photons', 'A', 'The nucleus contains protons and neutrons, collectively called nucleons.', 0),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q02', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'The energy equivalent of a mass defect is given by:', 'E = mc²', 'E = mgh', 'E = ½mv²', 'E = hf only', 'A', 'Einstein''s relation E = Δmc² converts the nuclear mass defect into binding energy.', 1),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q03', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'The binding energy per nucleon is maximum near which element?', 'Iron', 'Hydrogen', 'Uranium', 'Helium', 'A', 'Binding energy per nucleon peaks near iron (A ≈ 56), the most stable nuclei.', 2),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q04', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'Radioactive decay follows the law:', 'N = N₀e^(−λt)', 'N = N₀ + λt', 'N = N₀λt', 'N = N₀/t', 'A', 'The number of undecayed nuclei falls exponentially, N = N₀e^(−λt).', 3),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q05', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'The half-life in terms of the decay constant λ is:', '0.693/λ', 'λ/0.693', 'λ²', '1/λ²', 'A', 'Half-life t½ = ln2/λ = 0.693/λ.', 4),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q06', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'An alpha particle is identical to a:', 'Helium nucleus', 'Electron', 'Proton', 'Photon', 'A', 'An alpha particle is a helium nucleus (2 protons + 2 neutrons).', 5),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q07', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'Nuclear fusion involves:', 'Combining light nuclei to form a heavier one', 'Splitting a heavy nucleus', 'Emitting only alpha particles', 'Electron capture only', 'A', 'Fusion joins light nuclei (as in the Sun), releasing energy.', 6),
