  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q09', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'A beta particle is a(n):', 'Electron (or positron)', 'Helium nucleus', 'Proton', 'Neutron', 'A', 'Beta-minus decay emits a high-energy electron from the nucleus.', 8),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q10', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'Gamma rays emitted during nuclear decay are:', 'High-energy electromagnetic photons', 'Helium nuclei', 'Electrons', 'Neutrons', 'A', 'Gamma rays are highly penetrating electromagnetic radiation with no charge or mass.', 9),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q11', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'Nuclear density is approximately:', 'The same for all nuclei', 'Proportional to mass number', 'Zero', 'Proportional to radius', 'A', 'Since R ∝ A^(1/3), nuclear density is nearly independent of the nucleus (roughly constant).', 10),
  ('neet-physics-nuclei-q12', 'neet-physics-nuclei', 'The Sun''s energy is produced primarily by:', 'Nuclear fusion of hydrogen', 'Nuclear fission of uranium', 'Chemical combustion', 'Radioactive decay only', 'A', 'The Sun fuses hydrogen into helium, releasing enormous energy.', 11),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q01', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Offspring produced by asexual reproduction are:', 'Genetically identical to the parent (clones)', 'Genetically variable', 'Always different sexes', 'Sterile', 'A', 'Asexual reproduction involves one parent and produces genetically identical clones.', 0),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q02', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Binary fission is a mode of asexual reproduction seen in:', 'Amoeba', 'Humans', 'Mango trees', 'Ferns', 'A', 'Amoeba and many unicellular organisms reproduce by binary fission.', 1),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q03', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Budding is a form of asexual reproduction characteristic of:', 'Yeast and Hydra', 'Frogs', 'Birds', 'Ferns', 'A', 'Yeast and Hydra reproduce asexually by budding.', 2),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q04', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'The main advantage of sexual reproduction is:', 'Genetic variation', 'Identical offspring', 'No need for gametes', 'Faster reproduction always', 'A', 'Sexual reproduction generates variation, aiding adaptation and evolution.', 3),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q05', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'An organism having both male and female reproductive organs is called:', 'Unisexual', 'Bisexual (hermaphrodite)', 'Dioecious', 'Sterile', 'B', 'A bisexual (monoecious/hermaphrodite) organism bears both sex organs.', 4),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q06', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Vegetative propagation by runners is seen in:', 'Grass/strawberry', 'Amoeba', 'Yeast', 'Bacteria', 'A', 'Runners are horizontal stems producing new plants (e.g., grass, strawberry).', 5),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q07', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'The fusion of male and female gametes is called:', 'Syngamy (fertilisation)', 'Meiosis', 'Budding', 'Fragmentation', 'A', 'Syngamy is the fusion of gametes to form a zygote.', 6),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q08', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Which cell division reduces the chromosome number during gamete formation?', 'Mitosis', 'Meiosis', 'Binary fission', 'Budding', 'B', 'Meiosis halves the chromosome number, producing haploid gametes.', 7),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q09', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'The potato reproduces vegetatively through its:', 'Tuber (with eyes/buds)', 'Leaves only', 'Flowers', 'Seeds only', 'A', 'Potato tubers bear buds (''eyes'') that grow into new plants.', 8),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q10', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'The zygote formed after fertilisation is:', 'Diploid', 'Haploid', 'Triploid', 'Tetraploid', 'A', 'Fusion of two haploid gametes gives a diploid zygote.', 9),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q11', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'The life span of an organism is:', 'Independent of body size', 'Always proportional to size', 'The same for all organisms', 'Determined only by colour', 'A', 'Life span varies widely and is not related to organism size.', 10),
  ('neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms-q12', 'neet-biology-reproduction-in-organisms', 'Spore formation as a mode of asexual reproduction is common in:', 'Fungi and some plants', 'Mammals', 'Birds', 'Reptiles', 'A', 'Many fungi and lower plants reproduce asexually by producing spores.', 11),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q01', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'The management and breeding of livestock is called:', 'Animal husbandry', 'Apiculture', 'Horticulture', 'Sericulture', 'A', 'Animal husbandry is the scientific rearing and management of livestock.', 0),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q02', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'Apiculture is the rearing of:', 'Honeybees', 'Fish', 'Silkworms', 'Cattle', 'A', 'Apiculture is beekeeping for honey and wax.', 1),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q03', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'Inbreeding, if continued, may reduce fertility and productivity — a phenomenon called:', 'Inbreeding depression', 'Hybrid vigour', 'Heterosis', 'Outbreeding', 'A', 'Continued inbreeding increases homozygosity, causing inbreeding depression.', 2),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q04', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'MOET, used to improve cattle rapidly, stands for:', 'Multiple Ovulation Embryo Transfer', 'Male Ova Extraction Technique', 'Mammalian Oocyte Enzyme Test', 'Milk Output Enhancement Treatment', 'A', 'MOET induces multiple ovulation and transfers embryos to surrogates for faster herd improvement.', 3),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q05', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'The culture of fish for food is called:', 'Pisciculture', 'Apiculture', 'Sericulture', 'Floriculture', 'A', 'Pisciculture is fish farming, a form of aquaculture.', 4),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q06', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'Growing whole plants from small tissue explants in vitro is:', 'Tissue culture (micropropagation)', 'Grafting', 'Layering', 'Budding', 'A', 'Tissue culture exploits totipotency to grow many plants from small explants.', 5),
  ('neet-biology-strategies-food-production-q07', 'neet-biology-strategies-food-production', 'The ability of a single plant cell to develop into a whole plant is:', 'Totipotency', 'Pluripotency', 'Senescence', 'Dormancy', 'A', 'Totipotency is the capacity of a cell to regenerate a complete organism.', 6),
