  ('ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss', 'If the price of an article is increased by 25%, by what percent must it be reduced to restore the original price?', '25%', '20%', '15%', '30%', 'B', 'Reduction % = 25/(100+25) × 100 = 20%.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss', 'An item costing ₹500 is sold at a 20% profit. Its selling price is:', '₹600', '₹520', '₹580', '₹620', 'A', 'SP = 500 × 1.20 = ₹600.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss', '40% of 250 is:', '80', '100', '120', '90', 'B', '40% of 250 = 0.40 × 250 = 100.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-percentages-profit-loss', 'An article bought for ₹400 is sold for ₹360. The loss percent is:', '10%', '8%', '12%', '5%', 'A', 'Loss = 40; loss% = 40/400 × 100 = 10%.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance', 'A car travels 240 km in 4 hours. Its average speed is:', '60 km/h', '50 km/h', '70 km/h', '48 km/h', 'A', 'Speed = distance/time = 240/4 = 60 km/h.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance', '72 km/h expressed in m/s is:', '20 m/s', '18 m/s', '25 m/s', '15 m/s', 'A', 'To convert km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18: 72 × 5/18 = 20 m/s.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance', 'A 150 m long train crosses a pole in 15 seconds. Its speed is:', '10 m/s', '15 m/s', '12 m/s', '9 m/s', 'A', 'Speed = 150/15 = 10 m/s.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-speed-distance', 'Two trains move toward each other at 40 km/h and 50 km/h. Their relative speed is:', '90 km/h', '10 km/h', '45 km/h', '80 km/h', 'A', 'For opposite directions relative speed = 40 + 50 = 90 km/h.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion', 'If a:b = 2:3 and b:c = 4:5, then a:c equals:', '8:15', '2:5', '8:5', '6:5', 'A', 'a:b = 8:12, b:c = 12:15, so a:c = 8:15.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion', '₹600 is divided in the ratio 2:3. The larger share is:', '₹360', '₹240', '₹300', '₹400', 'A', 'Larger share = 600 × 3/5 = ₹360.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion', 'The fourth proportional to 3, 6 and 4 is:', '8', '6', '12', '9', 'A', '3:6 = 4:x → x = 6 × 4 / 3 = 8.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-ratio-proportion', 'The mean proportional between 4 and 9 is:', '6', '5', '13', '36', 'A', 'Mean proportional = √(4 × 9) = √36 = 6.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-averages-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-averages', 'The average of the first 5 natural numbers is:', '3', '2.5', '4', '5', 'A', '(1+2+3+4+5)/5 = 15/5 = 3.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-averages-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-averages', 'The average of 10, 20, 30, 40 and 50 is:', '30', '25', '35', '40', 'A', 'Average = sum ÷ count = (10+20+30+40+50)/5 = 150/5 = 30.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-averages-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-averages', 'The average of 4 numbers is 25. Their sum is:', '100', '50', '125', '75', 'A', 'Sum = average × count = 25 × 4 = 100.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-averages-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-averages', 'The average of the first 10 even numbers (2 to 20) is:', '11', '10', '12', '20', 'A', 'Sum = 110; average = 110/10 = 11.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest', 'The simple interest on ₹1000 at 5% per annum for 2 years is:', '₹100', '₹50', '₹110', '₹200', 'A', 'SI = PRT/100 = 1000 × 5 × 2 / 100 = ₹100.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest', 'The compound interest on ₹1000 at 10% per annum for 2 years is:', '₹210', '₹200', '₹100', '₹220', 'A', 'Amount = 1000 × 1.1² = 1210; CI = 1210 − 1000 = ₹210.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest', 'In how many years will the simple interest on a sum equal the principal at 25% per annum?', '4 years', '5 years', '3 years', '8 years', 'A', 'Time = 100 / rate = 100/25 = 4 years.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simple-compound-interest', 'A sum doubles itself in 8 years at simple interest. The rate per annum is:', '12.5%', '10%', '8%', '15%', 'A', 'To double, SI = principal; rate = 100/8 = 12.5%.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work', 'A can do a work in 10 days and B in 15 days. Working together they finish it in:', '6 days', '5 days', '8 days', '12 days', 'A', '1/10 + 1/15 = 1/6, so together 6 days.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work', 'If 6 men complete a work in 8 days, how many men are needed to finish it in 4 days?', '12', '10', '8', '16', 'A', 'Men × days is constant: 6 × 8 / 4 = 12 men.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work', 'A does 1/4 of a work in 5 days. The whole work takes him:', '20 days', '15 days', '25 days', '10 days', 'A', 'If 1/4 takes 5 days, the full work takes 4 × 5 = 20 days.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-time-and-work', 'A is twice as efficient as B. If A finishes a job in 6 days, B alone takes:', '12 days', '3 days', '9 days', '6 days', 'A', 'Twice as efficient means B takes double the time: 2 × 6 = 12 days.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-number-system-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-number-system', 'The LCM of 12 and 18 is:', '36', '6', '72', '216', 'A', 'The lowest common multiple of 12 and 18 is 36 (12 = 2²·3, 18 = 2·3²).', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-number-system-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-number-system', 'The HCF of 24 and 36 is:', '12', '6', '24', '72', 'A', 'The highest common factor of 24 and 36 is 12, their largest common divisor.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-number-system-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-number-system', 'Two numbers are 12 and 18. If their LCM is 36, their HCF is:', '6', '12', '3', '9', 'A', 'Product = LCM × HCF, so HCF = (12 × 18)/36 = 6.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-number-system-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-number-system', 'The smallest number exactly divisible by both 4 and 6 is:', '12', '24', '10', '8', 'A', 'The smallest such number is their LCM = 12.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration', 'The area of a circle of radius 7 cm (π = 22/7) is:', '154 cm²', '44 cm²', '49 cm²', '22 cm²', 'A', 'Area = πr² = 22/7 × 49 = 154 cm².', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration', 'The volume of a cube of side 5 cm is:', '125 cm³', '25 cm³', '75 cm³', '150 cm³', 'A', 'Volume = side³ = 5³ = 125 cm³.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration', 'The area of a rectangle 8 cm by 5 cm is:', '40 cm²', '13 cm²', '26 cm²', '45 cm²', 'A', 'Area = length × breadth = 8 × 5 = 40 cm².', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mensuration', 'The perimeter of a square of side 9 cm is:', '36 cm', '81 cm', '18 cm', '45 cm', 'A', 'Perimeter = 4 × side = 4 × 9 = 36 cm.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics', 'If x + 1/x = 2, then x² + 1/x² equals:', '2', '4', '0', '1', 'A', '(x + 1/x)² − 2 = 2² − 2 = 2.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics', 'If a + b = 5 and ab = 6, then a² + b² equals:', '13', '11', '25', '19', 'A', 'a² + b² = (a+b)² − 2ab = 25 − 12 = 13.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics', 'The roots of x² − 5x + 6 = 0 are:', '2 and 3', '1 and 6', '−2 and −3', '5 and 6', 'A', 'x² − 5x + 6 = (x−2)(x−3) = 0, so x = 2 or 3.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-algebra-basics', 'If 3x − 7 = 8, then x equals:', '5', '3', '15', '1', 'A', 'Add 7 to both sides to get 3x = 15, then divide by 3: x = 5.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry', 'The value of sin 30° is:', '1/2', '√3/2', '1', '0', 'A', 'The standard trigonometric value of sin 30° is 1/2.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry', 'The value of cos 60° is:', '1/2', '√3/2', '1', '0', 'A', 'The standard trigonometric value of cos 60° is 1/2 (equal to sin 30°).', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry', 'The value of tan 45° is:', '1', '0', '√3', '1/√3', 'A', 'The standard trigonometric value of tan 45° is 1, since sin 45° = cos 45°.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-trigonometry', 'The value of sin²θ + cos²θ is:', '1', '0', '2', 'θ', 'A', 'The identity sin²θ + cos²θ = 1 holds for all θ.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-geometry-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-geometry', 'The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is:', '180°', '360°', '90°', '270°', 'A', 'The interior angles of a triangle add up to 180°.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-geometry-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-geometry', 'The sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral is:', '360°', '180°', '270°', '540°', 'A', 'A quadrilateral''s interior angles sum to 360°.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-geometry-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-geometry', 'Each interior angle of an equilateral triangle measures:', '60°', '90°', '45°', '120°', 'A', 'Each angle = 180°/3 = 60°.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-geometry-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-geometry', 'The angle inscribed in a semicircle is always:', '90°', '60°', '45°', '180°', 'A', 'An angle in a semicircle (subtended by the diameter) is a right angle, 90°.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation', 'In a pie chart, a sector representing 25% of the total corresponds to:', '90°', '72°', '60°', '120°', 'A', 'A full pie chart is 360°, so 25% corresponds to 0.25 × 360° = 90°.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation', 'In a pie chart, 20% of the total is shown by an angle of:', '72°', '90°', '60°', '45°', 'A', 'A full pie chart is 360°, so 20% corresponds to 0.20 × 360° = 72°.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation', 'A bar graph shows sales rising from 40 to 60 units. The percentage increase is:', '50%', '20%', '33%', '40%', 'A', 'Increase = 20 on 40 = 20/40 × 100 = 50%.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-data-interpretation', 'The average of the values 30, 40 and 50 shown in a graph is:', '40', '30', '45', '50', 'A', '(30 + 40 + 50)/3 = 120/3 = 40.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series', 'If CAT is coded as DBU (each letter shifted +1), then DOG is coded as:', 'EPH', 'CPF', 'EPG', 'DPH', 'A', 'Each letter moves one step forward: D→E, O→P, G→H = EPH.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series', 'Find the next term: 2, 4, 8, 16, ?', '32', '24', '20', '18', 'A', 'Each term doubles: 16 × 2 = 32.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series', 'Find the next term: 1, 4, 9, 16, ?', '25', '20', '24', '36', 'A', 'These are perfect squares: 5² = 25.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-coding-decoding-series', 'If A = 1, B = 2, C = 3 …, then the sum of the letters in ''CAB'' is:', '6', '5', '7', '9', 'A', 'C + A + B = 3 + 1 + 2 = 6.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification', 'Bird : Fly :: Fish : ?', 'Swim', 'Walk', 'Run', 'Jump', 'A', 'A bird flies as a fish swims.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification', 'Find the odd one out: Rose, Lotus, Lily, Mango.', 'Mango', 'Rose', 'Lotus', 'Lily', 'A', 'Mango is a fruit; the others are flowers.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification', 'Doctor : Hospital :: Teacher : ?', 'School', 'Book', 'Student', 'Class', 'A', 'A doctor works in a hospital as a teacher works in a school.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-analogy-classification', 'Find the odd one out: 2, 3, 5, 9.', '9', '2', '3', '5', 'A', '2, 3 and 5 are prime; 9 is not.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations', 'A is the father of B. Then A is B''s:', 'Father', 'Son', 'Uncle', 'Brother', 'A', 'If A is the father of B, A is B''s father.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations', 'Your mother''s brother is your:', 'Maternal uncle', 'Paternal uncle', 'Cousin', 'Nephew', 'A', 'The mother''s brother is the maternal uncle (mama).', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations', 'The daughter of your father is your:', 'Sister', 'Aunt', 'Niece', 'Cousin', 'A', 'Your father''s daughter is your sister.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-blood-relations', 'Your father''s father is your:', 'Grandfather', 'Uncle', 'Brother', 'Nephew', 'A', 'The father''s father is the (paternal) grandfather.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense', 'A man walks 3 km north, then 4 km east. His straight-line distance from the start is:', '5 km', '7 km', '1 km', '12 km', 'A', 'By Pythagoras, √(3² + 4²) = √25 = 5 km.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense', 'Facing north, you turn 90° clockwise. You now face:', 'East', 'West', 'South', 'North', 'A', 'A 90° clockwise turn from north points east.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense', 'The sun rises in the:', 'East', 'West', 'North', 'South', 'A', 'The sun rises in the east and sets in the west.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-direction-sense', 'Facing south, you turn 180°. You now face:', 'North', 'East', 'West', 'South', 'A', 'A 180° turn from south points north.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism', 'All cats are animals. All animals are living things. It follows that:', 'All cats are living things', 'All animals are cats', 'No cat is living', 'Some cats are not animals', 'A', 'Chaining the two universals gives: all cats are living things.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism', '''Some pens are red.'' A valid conversion is:', 'Some red things are pens', 'All pens are red', 'No pen is red', 'All red things are pens', 'A', '''Some A are B'' converts to ''Some B are A''.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism', '''No dog is a cat.'' A valid conclusion is:', 'No cat is a dog', 'Some cats are dogs', 'All cats are dogs', 'Some dogs are cats', 'A', 'A universal negative converts: ''No dog is a cat'' ⇒ ''No cat is a dog''.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-syllogism', 'All roses are flowers. Some flowers are red. Which follows?', 'No definite conclusion about roses being red', 'All roses are red', 'No rose is red', 'All flowers are roses', 'A', 'The ''some flowers are red'' need not include roses, so no conclusion about red roses follows.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles', 'In a row of 5 people, the person exactly in the middle is at position:', '3rd', '2nd', '4th', '1st', 'A', 'In a row of 5, the middle is the 3rd position.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles', 'If A is to the immediate right of B, then B is to the ___ of A.', 'Left', 'Right', 'Front', 'Back', 'A', 'If A is on B''s right, B must be on A''s left.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles', 'Eight people sit evenly around a circle facing the centre. The person opposite position 1 is at position:', '5', '4', '8', '6', 'A', 'In a circle of 8, the opposite seat is 4 places away: 1 + 4 = 5.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-seating-puzzles', 'In a row of 6 people, P is 2nd from the left. P''s position from the right is:', '5th', '4th', '6th', '3rd', 'A', 'Position from right = total − position from left + 1 = 6 − 2 + 1 = 5.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar', 'The angle between the hands of a clock at 3:00 is:', '90°', '180°', '45°', '60°', 'A', 'At 3:00 the hands are 3 hours apart: 3 × 30° = 90°.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar', 'In one minute the minute hand of a clock moves through:', '6°', '1°', '12°', '30°', 'A', 'The minute hand covers 360° in 60 minutes = 6° per minute.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar', 'The number of odd days in an ordinary (non-leap) year is:', '1', '2', '0', '3', 'A', '365 days = 52 weeks + 1 day, so 1 odd day.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-clock-calendar', 'If today is Monday, the day after exactly 7 days will be:', 'Monday', 'Sunday', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'A', '7 days is exactly one week, so the same day returns: Monday.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding', 'In a mirror image, the left side of an object appears on the:', 'Right', 'Left', 'Top', 'Bottom', 'A', 'A plane mirror laterally inverts, so left appears on the right.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding', 'The left-right reversal seen in a mirror is called:', 'Lateral inversion', 'Vertical inversion', 'Rotation', 'Magnification', 'A', 'Mirror images show lateral (left-right) inversion.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding', 'The mirror image of the lowercase letter ''b'' most resembles:', 'd', 'p', 'q', 'b', 'A', 'Reflecting ''b'' left-to-right gives a shape like ''d''.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-mirror-paper-folding', 'In a water (surface) reflection, an image is inverted:', 'Top to bottom', 'Left to right', 'Not at all', 'Diagonally', 'A', 'A water reflection flips the image vertically (top-to-bottom).', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion', 'Statement: All students passed the exam. Conclusion:', 'No student failed', 'Some students failed', 'The exam was easy', 'Only some passed', 'A', 'If all passed, then it follows that no student failed.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion', 'Statement: It is raining heavily. Which conclusion is best supported?', 'The ground is likely to get wet', 'It will never stop raining', 'There is a drought', 'The sun is shining', 'A', 'Heavy rain reasonably implies the ground is likely to get wet.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion', 'Statement: ''Smoking is injurious to health.'' The underlying assumption is:', 'People should avoid smoking', 'Everyone smokes', 'Smoking is healthy', 'Health cannot be harmed', 'A', 'The statement implies the advisory that people should avoid smoking.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-statement-conclusion', 'Statement: The library is open from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. Conclusion:', 'It is closed at 6 p.m.', 'It is open all night', 'It never closes', 'It opens at 8 a.m.', 'A', 'Closing at 5 p.m. means it is closed at 6 p.m.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word', 'The idiom ''a piece of cake'' means:', 'Very easy', 'Very tasty', 'Expensive', 'Difficult', 'A', '''A piece of cake'' means something very easy to do.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word', 'One word for ''an animal that eats both plants and meat'' is:', 'Omnivore', 'Herbivore', 'Carnivore', 'Insectivore', 'A', 'An omnivore eats both plants and animals.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word', 'The idiom ''to let the cat out of the bag'' means:', 'To reveal a secret', 'To buy a pet', 'To run away', 'To make noise', 'A', '''Let the cat out of the bag'' means to disclose a secret.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-idioms-one-word', 'One word for ''a place where books are kept for reading'' is:', 'Library', 'Laboratory', 'Gallery', 'Studio', 'A', 'A library is a place where books are kept.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms', 'Choose the synonym of ''HAPPY'':', 'Joyful', 'Sad', 'Angry', 'Tired', 'A', '''Joyful'' is a synonym of ''happy''.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms', 'Choose the antonym of ''ANCIENT'':', 'Modern', 'Old', 'Historic', 'Aged', 'A', '''Modern'' is the opposite of ''ancient''.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms', 'Choose the synonym of ''BRAVE'':', 'Courageous', 'Fearful', 'Weak', 'Timid', 'A', '''Courageous'' is a synonym of ''brave''.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-synonyms-antonyms', 'Choose the antonym of ''EXPAND'':', 'Contract', 'Enlarge', 'Grow', 'Widen', 'A', '''Contract'' is the opposite of ''expand''.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors', 'Find the error: ''He don''t like tea.''', 'don''t (should be doesn''t)', 'He', 'like', 'tea', 'A', 'With a singular third-person subject, use ''doesn''t'', not ''don''t''.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors', 'Find the error: ''She is more taller than me.''', 'more taller (double comparative)', 'She', 'than', 'me', 'A', '''Taller'' is already comparative; ''more taller'' is incorrect.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors', 'Find the error: ''One of the boys are absent.''', 'are (should be is)', 'One', 'boys', 'absent', 'A', '''One of the boys'' is singular, so use ''is'', not ''are''.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-spotting-errors', 'Find the error: ''I have visited him yesterday.''', 'have visited (should be visited)', 'I', 'him', 'yesterday', 'A', '''Yesterday'' needs the simple past ''visited'', not the present perfect.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling', 'Choose the correctly spelt word:', 'Receive', 'Recieve', 'Receeve', 'Receve', 'A', 'The rule ''i before e except after c'' gives ''receive''.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling', 'Choose the correctly spelt word:', 'Accommodate', 'Acommodate', 'Accomodate', 'Acomodate', 'A', '''Accommodate'' has double c and double m.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling', 'Choose the correctly spelt word:', 'Definitely', 'Definately', 'Definatly', 'Definitly', 'A', 'The correct spelling is ''definitely''.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-sentence-improvement-spelling', 'Choose the correctly spelt word:', 'Occurrence', 'Occurence', 'Ocurrence', 'Occurance', 'A', '''Occurrence'' has double c, double r and ends in -ence.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension', 'Passage: ''Regular exercise improves health and reduces stress.'' According to the passage, exercise reduces:', 'Stress', 'Health', 'Sleep', 'Appetite', 'A', 'The passage states exercise reduces stress.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension', 'In the sentence ''The novel was so gripping she read it in one sitting'', ''gripping'' most nearly means:', 'Engrossing', 'Boring', 'Short', 'Difficult', 'A', '''Gripping'' means holding the attention — engrossing.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension', 'The main idea of a paragraph is usually stated in its:', 'Topic sentence', 'Last word', 'Title only', 'Footnote', 'A', 'The topic sentence carries the paragraph''s main idea.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-reading-comprehension', 'To ''infer'' from a passage means to:', 'Draw a conclusion from evidence', 'Copy the text', 'Ignore the details', 'Count the words', 'A', 'Inference is reaching a conclusion based on evidence in the text.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice', 'Change to passive voice: ''She writes a letter.''', 'A letter is written by her', 'A letter was written by her', 'A letter writes her', 'She is written a letter', 'A', 'Simple present passive: ''A letter is written by her.''', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice', 'Change to passive voice: ''They are playing football.''', 'Football is being played by them', 'Football is played by them', 'Football was played by them', 'Football has been played', 'A', 'Present continuous passive: ''Football is being played by them.''', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice', 'In the active voice, the subject is the ___ of the action.', 'Doer', 'Receiver', 'Object', 'Adverb', 'A', 'In the active voice the subject performs (does) the action.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-active-passive-voice', 'Change to passive voice: ''He ate an apple.''', 'An apple was eaten by him', 'An apple is eaten by him', 'An apple has eaten him', 'He was eaten an apple', 'A', 'Simple past passive: ''An apple was eaten by him.''', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test', 'Fill in the blank: ''He is good ___ mathematics.''', 'at', 'in', 'on', 'for', 'A', 'The correct collocation is ''good at'' a subject.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test', 'Fill in the blank: ''She has been living here ___ 2010.''', 'since', 'for', 'from', 'by', 'A', 'Use ''since'' with a point in time (2010).', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test', 'Fill in the blank: ''The book is ___ the table.''', 'on', 'in', 'at', 'of', 'A', 'Something resting on a surface is ''on'' the table.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-cloze-test', 'Fill in the blank: ''I am fond ___ music.''', 'of', 'for', 'with', 'to', 'A', 'The correct phrase is ''fond of''.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts', 'The minimum age to become President of India is:', '35 years', '25 years', '30 years', '40 years', 'A', 'A person must be at least 35 years old to be President.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts', 'The number of members nominated to the Rajya Sabha by the President is:', '12', '2', '10', '20', 'A', 'The President nominates 12 members to the Rajya Sabha.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts', 'The Fundamental Duties are contained in which article of the Constitution?', 'Article 51A', 'Article 21', 'Article 370', 'Article 14', 'A', 'Article 51A lists the Fundamental Duties of citizens.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-indian-polity-facts', 'The minimum age to become a member of the Lok Sabha is:', '25 years', '30 years', '21 years', '35 years', 'A', 'A Lok Sabha member must be at least 25 years old.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history', 'The Quit India Movement was launched in the year:', '1942', '1930', '1919', '1947', 'A', 'Gandhi launched the Quit India Movement in 1942.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history', 'The first Indian Governor-General of independent India was:', 'C. Rajagopalachari', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Lord Mountbatten', 'Rajendra Prasad', 'A', 'C. Rajagopalachari was the first (and only) Indian Governor-General.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in the year:', '1885', '1857', '1905', '1919', 'A', 'The Indian National Congress was founded in 1885.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-history', 'The Battle of Plassey was fought in the year:', '1757', '1764', '1857', '1526', 'A', 'The Battle of Plassey took place in 1757.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography', 'The longest river in India is the:', 'Ganga', 'Yamuna', 'Godavari', 'Narmada', 'A', 'The Ganga is the longest river within India.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography', 'The highest mountain peak located in India is:', 'Kanchenjunga', 'Mount Everest', 'Nanda Devi', 'K2', 'A', 'Kanchenjunga is the highest peak lying within India''s borders.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography', 'The Tropic of Cancer passes through how many Indian states?', '8', '5', '10', '6', 'A', 'The Tropic of Cancer passes through 8 Indian states.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-geography', 'The largest Indian state by area is:', 'Rajasthan', 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Maharashtra', 'Uttar Pradesh', 'A', 'Rajasthan is the largest Indian state by area.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science', 'The chemical symbol for gold is:', 'Au', 'Ag', 'Gd', 'Go', 'A', 'Gold''s symbol is Au (from the Latin ''aurum'').', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science', 'The ''powerhouse of the cell'' is the:', 'Mitochondria', 'Nucleus', 'Ribosome', 'Golgi body', 'A', 'Mitochondria produce ATP and are called the powerhouse of the cell.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science', 'The most abundant gas in Earth''s atmosphere is:', 'Nitrogen', 'Oxygen', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Hydrogen', 'A', 'Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the atmosphere.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-general-science', 'The SI unit of force is the:', 'Newton', 'Joule', 'Watt', 'Pascal', 'A', 'Force is measured in newtons (N).', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics', 'The Reserve Bank of India was established in the year:', '1935', '1947', '1950', '1991', 'A', 'The RBI was established in 1935.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics', 'The Goods and Services Tax (GST) was introduced in India in:', '2017', '2010', '2020', '2005', 'A', 'GST came into effect on 1 July 2017.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics', 'The apex (central) bank of India is the:', 'Reserve Bank of India', 'State Bank of India', 'NABARD', 'SEBI', 'A', 'The RBI is India''s central bank.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-economy-basics', 'NITI Aayog replaced which earlier body in 2015?', 'Planning Commission', 'Finance Commission', 'Election Commission', 'UGC', 'A', 'NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs', 'World Environment Day is observed on:', '5 June', '22 April', '1 May', '16 September', 'A', 'World Environment Day is observed on 5 June.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs', 'International Yoga Day is observed on:', '21 June', '5 June', '8 March', '2 October', 'A', 'International Yoga Day is celebrated on 21 June.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs', 'India celebrates its Independence Day on:', '15 August', '26 January', '2 October', '14 November', 'A', 'India''s Independence Day is 15 August.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-days-current-affairs', 'World Health Day is observed on:', '7 April', '1 December', '5 June', '21 June', 'A', 'World Health Day is observed on 7 April, the WHO''s founding day.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards', 'The book ''Wings of Fire'' was written by:', 'A. P. J. Abdul Kalam', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'R. K. Narayan', 'Arundhati Roy', 'A', '''Wings of Fire'' is the autobiography of A. P. J. Abdul Kalam.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards', 'The highest civilian award of India is the:', 'Bharat Ratna', 'Padma Vibhushan', 'Param Vir Chakra', 'Padma Shri', 'A', 'The Bharat Ratna is India''s highest civilian award.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards', 'The Indian who won the Nobel Prize in Literature for ''Gitanjali'' was:', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 'Amartya Sen', 'C. V. Raman', 'Mother Teresa', 'A', 'Rabindranath Tagore won the 1913 Nobel Prize in Literature for Gitanjali.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-books-authors-awards', 'The book ''The Discovery of India'' was written by:', 'Jawaharlal Nehru', 'Mahatma Gandhi', 'B. R. Ambedkar', 'Sardar Patel', 'A', '''The Discovery of India'' was written by Jawaharlal Nehru.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q01', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'The rule of alligation is used to find the:', 'Ratio in which ingredients are mixed', 'Total cost only', 'Time taken', 'Simple interest', 'A', 'Alligation gives the ratio in which two ingredients at different prices are mixed for a mean price.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q02', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'In what ratio must rice at ₹20/kg be mixed with rice at ₹30/kg to get a mixture worth ₹24/kg?', '3:2', '2:3', '1:2', '4:1', 'A', 'Ratio = (30−24):(24−20) = 6:4 = 3:2.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q03', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'Sugar at ₹12/kg and ₹18/kg are mixed to give a mixture worth ₹16/kg. The ratio is:', '1:2', '2:1', '1:1', '3:2', 'A', 'Ratio = (18−16):(16−12) = 2:4 = 1:2.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q04', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'A 40-litre mixture has milk and water in the ratio 3:1. The quantity of water is:', '10 litres', '30 litres', '20 litres', '15 litres', 'A', 'Water = 40 × 1/4 = 10 litres.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q05', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'From 20 litres of pure milk, 4 litres are removed and replaced with water. The milk remaining is:', '16 litres', '18 litres', '15 litres', '12 litres', 'A', 'Milk left = 20 × (1 − 4/20) = 20 × 0.8 = 16 litres.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q06', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'The weighted average price of 2 kg at ₹10/kg and 3 kg at ₹20/kg is:', '₹16', '₹15', '₹18', '₹14', 'A', 'Mean = (2×10 + 3×20)/5 = 80/5 = ₹16.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q07', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'In what ratio must water be mixed with milk costing ₹40/litre to make the mixture cost ₹32/litre?', '1:4', '1:5', '1:3', '2:5', 'A', 'Treat water as ₹0: ratio = (40−32):(32−0) = 8:32 = 1:4.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q08', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'Two varieties of tea at ₹15/kg and ₹25/kg are mixed in equal quantities. The average price is:', '₹20', '₹18', '₹22', '₹19', 'A', 'Equal mix average = (15 + 25)/2 = ₹20.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', '60 litres of a milk-water mixture is in the ratio 2:1. To make the ratio 1:1, water to be added is:', '20 litres', '10 litres', '30 litres', '15 litres', 'A', 'Milk = 40, water = 20. For 1:1 water must equal 40, so add 20 litres.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'In a mixture, milk : water = 5:3. If the water is 24 litres, the milk is:', '40 litres', '36 litres', '30 litres', '48 litres', 'A', 'One part = 24/3 = 8; milk = 5 × 8 = 40 litres.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'The cost of the mean mixture always lies:', 'Between the two ingredient costs', 'Above both costs', 'Below both costs', 'At zero', 'A', 'A weighted average must fall between the smallest and largest ingredient prices.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-mixtures-alligation', 'A 50-litre mixture contains 20% water. The quantity of water is:', '10 litres', '20 litres', '5 litres', '15 litres', 'A', 'Water = 20% of 50 = 0.20 × 50 = 10 litres.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q01', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'When partners invest for the same period, profit is divided in the ratio of their:', 'Capitals', 'Ages', 'Salaries', 'Time only', 'A', 'For equal time, profit is shared in proportion to the capitals invested.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q02', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A and B invest ₹5000 and ₹10000 for the same time. The profit-sharing ratio is:', '1:2', '2:1', '1:1', '2:3', 'A', 'Equal time, so the ratio is of capitals: 5000:10000 = 1:2.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q03', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'When the investment periods differ, profit is shared in the ratio of:', 'Capital × time', 'Capital only', 'Time only', 'Capital + time', 'A', 'Profit ratio = (capital × time) for each partner.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q04', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A invests ₹6000 for 12 months and B invests ₹8000 for 6 months. The profit ratio is:', '3:2', '2:3', '1:1', '3:4', 'A', '6000×12 : 8000×6 = 72000:48000 = 3:2.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q05', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A partner who invests capital and also manages the business is a:', 'Working partner', 'Sleeping partner', 'Silent partner', 'Dormant partner', 'A', 'A working (active) partner both invests and runs the business.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q06', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A total profit of ₹9000 is shared in the ratio 2:1. The larger share is:', '₹6000', '₹3000', '₹4500', '₹5000', 'A', 'Larger share = 9000 × 2/3 = ₹6000.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q07', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'If two partners invest equal amounts for equal time, they share the profit:', 'Equally (1:1)', 'In the ratio 2:1', 'In the ratio 1:2', 'Unequally', 'A', 'Equal capital and equal time give an equal (1:1) profit share.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q08', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A, B and C invest in the ratio 2:3:5. Of a ₹10000 profit, C''s share is:', '₹5000', '₹3000', '₹2000', '₹4000', 'A', 'C''s share = 10000 × 5/10 = ₹5000.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A sleeping (dormant) partner is one who:', 'Invests capital but does not manage the business', 'Manages but does not invest', 'Neither invests nor manages', 'Only takes a salary', 'A', 'A sleeping partner contributes capital only and takes no part in management.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'A invests ₹4000 for 6 months and B ₹4000 for 12 months. Their profit ratio is:', '1:2', '2:1', '1:1', '1:3', 'A', '4000×6 : 4000×12 = 1:2.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'In a two-partner firm, A''s share of a ₹1200 profit is ₹800. B''s share is:', '₹400', '₹600', '₹300', '₹500', 'A', 'B = 1200 − 800 = ₹400.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-partnership-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-partnership', 'The profit ratio of A:B is 3:2. If A receives ₹300 more than B, the total profit is:', '₹1500', '₹1200', '₹900', '₹1800', 'A', 'Difference = 1 part = ₹300; total = 5 parts = ₹1500.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q01', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'A pipe that fills a tank is called an:', 'Inlet', 'Outlet', 'Leak', 'Drain', 'A', 'An inlet fills the tank (positive rate); an outlet or leak empties it.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q02', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'A pipe fills a tank in 6 hours. In one hour it fills:', '1/6 of the tank', '6 tanks', '1/3 of the tank', 'The whole tank', 'A', 'Rate = 1/time = 1/6 of the tank per hour.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q03', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Pipe A fills a tank in 4 hours and pipe B in 6 hours. Together they fill it in:', '2.4 hours', '2 hours', '3 hours', '5 hours', 'A', '1/4 + 1/6 = 5/12, so time = 12/5 = 2.4 hours.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q04', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'The work done by an outlet pipe is taken as:', 'Negative', 'Positive', 'Zero', 'Doubled', 'A', 'An outlet empties the tank, so its rate is subtracted (negative).', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q05', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Inlet A fills a tank in 3 hours; outlet B empties it in 6 hours. With both open, the tank fills in:', '6 hours', '3 hours', '9 hours', '2 hours', 'A', 'Net rate = 1/3 − 1/6 = 1/6, so time = 6 hours.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q06', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Two pipes fill a tank in 12 and 24 minutes. Together they fill it in:', '8 minutes', '6 minutes', '10 minutes', '12 minutes', 'A', '1/12 + 1/24 = 3/24 = 1/8, so 8 minutes.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q07', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'A pipe fills 1/5 of a tank in 3 minutes. The whole tank is filled in:', '15 minutes', '12 minutes', '10 minutes', '20 minutes', 'A', 'If 1/5 takes 3 min, the full tank takes 5 × 3 = 15 minutes.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q08', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'A tap fills a tank in 5 hours. In 2 hours it fills:', '2/5 of the tank', '1/2 of the tank', '2/3 of the tank', '1/5 of the tank', 'A', 'In 2 hours it fills 2 × (1/5) = 2/5 of the tank.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Pipe A fills in 8 hours; a leak empties the full tank in 12 hours. With both, the tank fills in:', '24 hours', '20 hours', '16 hours', '12 hours', 'A', 'Net rate = 1/8 − 1/12 = 1/24, so time = 24 hours.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Pipes-and-cisterns problems are mathematically analogous to:', 'Time-and-work problems', 'Profit-and-loss problems', 'Simple interest', 'Mensuration', 'A', 'Filling a tank is a work problem: rates add just like combined work rates.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'Two pipes fill a tank in 10 and 15 minutes. Together they fill it in:', '6 minutes', '5 minutes', '8 minutes', '12 minutes', 'A', '1/10 + 1/15 = 1/6, so 6 minutes.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-pipes-cisterns', 'If an inlet fills in ''a'' hours and an outlet empties in ''b'' hours (b > a), the fill time is:', 'ab / (b − a)', 'a + b', 'ab / (a + b)', 'b − a', 'A', 'Net rate = 1/a − 1/b = (b−a)/ab, so time = ab/(b−a).', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q01', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'Downstream speed equals the boat''s speed plus the:', 'Stream (current) speed', 'Wind speed', 'Distance', 'Time', 'A', 'Going downstream, the current helps, so speeds add: b + s.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q02', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'Upstream speed equals the boat''s speed minus the:', 'Stream speed', 'Distance', 'Time', 'Depth', 'A', 'Going upstream, the current opposes, so upstream speed = b − s.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q03', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A boat''s speed in still water is 10 km/h and the stream 2 km/h. Its downstream speed is:', '12 km/h', '8 km/h', '10 km/h', '5 km/h', 'A', 'Downstream = 10 + 2 = 12 km/h.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q04', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A boat''s speed in still water is 10 km/h and the stream 2 km/h. Its upstream speed is:', '8 km/h', '12 km/h', '10 km/h', '6 km/h', 'A', 'Upstream = 10 − 2 = 8 km/h.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q05', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'If downstream speed is 12 km/h and upstream 8 km/h, the boat''s speed in still water is:', '10 km/h', '4 km/h', '2 km/h', '20 km/h', 'A', 'Boat speed = (12 + 8)/2 = 10 km/h.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q06', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'If downstream speed is 12 km/h and upstream 8 km/h, the stream speed is:', '2 km/h', '4 km/h', '10 km/h', '1 km/h', 'A', 'Stream speed = (12 − 8)/2 = 2 km/h.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q07', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A boat covers 12 km downstream in 2 hours. Its downstream speed is:', '6 km/h', '8 km/h', '10 km/h', '4 km/h', 'A', 'Speed = distance/time = 12/2 = 6 km/h.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q08', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'If a boat''s still-water speed is 8 km/h and the stream is 3 km/h, its upstream speed is:', '5 km/h', '11 km/h', '3 km/h', '8 km/h', 'A', 'Upstream = 8 − 3 = 5 km/h.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', '''Speed in still water'' refers to the boat''s speed when:', 'There is no current', 'The current is strongest', 'It is anchored', 'It moves upstream', 'A', 'Still water means no current, so the effective speed is just the boat''s own speed b.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A man rows downstream at 15 km/h and upstream at 5 km/h. His speed in still water is:', '10 km/h', '5 km/h', '20 km/h', '7.5 km/h', 'A', 'Still-water speed = (15 + 5)/2 = 10 km/h.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A man rows downstream at 15 km/h and upstream at 5 km/h. The stream speed is:', '5 km/h', '10 km/h', '2.5 km/h', '20 km/h', 'A', 'Stream speed = (15 − 5)/2 = 5 km/h.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-boats-streams', 'A boat covers 16 km upstream in 4 hours. Its upstream speed is:', '4 km/h', '8 km/h', '12 km/h', '2 km/h', 'A', 'Upstream speed = 16/4 = 4 km/h.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q01', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'In BODMAS, the letter ''B'' stands for:', 'Brackets', 'Base', 'Bonus', 'Balance', 'A', 'BODMAS = Brackets, Orders, Division, Multiplication, Addition, Subtraction.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q02', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'Using BODMAS, 12 + 6 ÷ 2 equals:', '15', '9', '12', '18', 'A', 'Divide first: 6 ÷ 2 = 3; then 12 + 3 = 15.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q03', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of (8 + 2) × 3 is:', '30', '14', '24', '26', 'A', 'Brackets first: (10) × 3 = 30.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q04', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of 5 × 4 − 6 is:', '14', '10', '26', '20', 'A', 'Multiply first: 20 − 6 = 14.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q05', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of 20 ÷ 4 + 3 is:', '8', '5', '11', '23', 'A', 'Divide first: 5 + 3 = 8.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q06', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'Approximately, 49.8 × 10.2 is closest to:', '500', '400', '600', '250', 'A', 'Round to 50 × 10 = 500.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q07', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of 2³ + 1 is:', '9', '7', '6', '8', 'A', 'Orders first: 2³ = 8; then 8 + 1 = 9.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q08', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of √81 + √16 is:', '13', '12', '25', '10', 'A', '√81 = 9 and √16 = 4, so 9 + 4 = 13.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q09', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', '15% of 240 is:', '36', '30', '24', '40', 'A', '15% of 240 = 0.15 × 240 = 36.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q10', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of 7 × (3 + 2) is:', '35', '23', '17', '42', 'A', 'Brackets first: 7 × 5 = 35.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q11', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'The value of 100 − 20 ÷ 5 is:', '96', '16', '80', '95', 'A', 'Divide first: 20 ÷ 5 = 4; then 100 − 4 = 96.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-quant-simplification-q12', 'ssc-cgl-quant-simplification', 'In BODMAS, operations of the same rank (like ÷ and ×) are done:', 'Left to right', 'Right to left', 'In any order', 'Last', 'A', 'Division and multiplication share a rank and are evaluated left to right.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q01', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a row of 40 people, A is 10th from the left. A''s position from the right is:', '31st', '30th', '29th', '32nd', 'A', 'Position from right = 40 − 10 + 1 = 31st.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q02', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a class of 30, a student ranks 12th from the top. The rank from the bottom is:', '19th', '18th', '20th', '17th', 'A', 'Rank from bottom = 30 − 12 + 1 = 19th.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q03', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'If a person''s position from the left is L and from the right is R, the total number of people is:', 'L + R − 1', 'L + R', 'L + R + 1', 'L − R', 'A', 'Total = position from left + position from right − 1.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q04', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a row of 25, B is 7th from the right. B''s position from the left is:', '19th', '18th', '20th', '17th', 'A', 'Position from left = 25 − 7 + 1 = 19th.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q05', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a queue, a person is 8th from the front and 12th from the back. The total number of people is:', '19', '20', '18', '21', 'A', 'Total = 8 + 12 − 1 = 19.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q06', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a row of 50, a person 20th from the left is, from the right:', '31st', '30th', '29th', '32nd', 'A', 'From the right = 50 − 20 + 1 = 31st.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q07', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'X is 3rd from the top and 3rd from the bottom in a rank list. The total number of students is:', '5', '6', '4', '7', 'A', 'Total = 3 + 3 − 1 = 5.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q08', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'The rank from the bottom equals:', 'Total − rank from top + 1', 'Total − rank from top', 'Total + rank from top', 'Rank from top − 1', 'A', 'Rank from bottom = Total − rank from top + 1.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a row of 15, A is 5th from the left and B is 6th from the right. The number of people between them is:', '4', '5', '3', '6', 'A', 'B from left = 15 − 6 + 1 = 10th; between positions 5 and 10 there are 10 − 5 − 1 = 4 people.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'Ranking 1st in a list means being:', 'At the top', 'At the bottom', 'In the middle', 'Last', 'A', 'Rank 1 is the highest position — the top.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'A is 10th in a queue. B is 4 places ahead of A. B''s position is:', '6th', '14th', '5th', '7th', 'A', '''Ahead'' means nearer the front: 10 − 4 = 6th.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-order-ranking', 'In a row of 20, a person 12th from the left is, from the right:', '9th', '8th', '10th', '11th', 'A', 'From the right = 20 − 12 + 1 = 9th.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q01', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'A Venn diagram represents relationships between groups using:', 'Overlapping circles', 'Straight lines', 'Bar graphs', 'Tables only', 'A', 'Venn diagrams use overlapping circles to show how sets relate.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q02', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'The overlapping region of two circles represents elements that are:', 'Common to both groups', 'In neither group', 'Only in the first group', 'Only in the second group', 'A', 'The intersection (overlap) holds elements belonging to both sets.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q03', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'If all A are B, the correct diagram shows:', 'Circle A entirely inside circle B', 'Two separate circles', 'Two equal circles', 'Circle B inside circle A', 'A', '''All A are B'' means every A is contained in B, so A sits inside B.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q04', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'Which best represents Dog, Cat and Animal?', 'Dog and Cat as separate circles inside Animal', 'Three fully overlapping circles', 'Three separate circles', 'Animal inside Dog', 'A', 'Dogs and cats are distinct kinds of animals, so both lie separately within the Animal circle.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q05', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'If no A is B, the two circles are:', 'Separate (disjoint)', 'Overlapping', 'One inside the other', 'Identical', 'A', '''No A is B'' means the sets share nothing, so the circles do not touch.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q06', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'Which relationship suits Apple, Fruit and Food?', 'Apple inside Fruit inside Food (nested)', 'Three separate circles', 'Food inside Apple', 'Apple and Food overlapping only', 'A', 'Every apple is a fruit and every fruit is food, giving three nested circles.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q07', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', '''Some A are B'' is shown by:', 'Two partially overlapping circles', 'Two separate circles', 'A inside B', 'Two identical circles', 'A', '''Some'' means a partial overlap between the two circles.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q08', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'The universal set in a Venn diagram is usually drawn as a:', 'Rectangle enclosing the circles', 'Single line', 'Small dot', 'Triangle inside a circle', 'A', 'A rectangle around all the circles denotes the universal set.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'Which best represents Doctors, Women and Human Beings?', 'Doctors and Women overlapping, both inside Human Beings', 'Three separate circles', 'Human Beings inside Doctors', 'Doctors inside Women', 'A', 'Some doctors are women (overlap), and both are human beings (contained in that circle).', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'The central region common to three overlapping circles contains elements that are:', 'In all three groups', 'In only one group', 'In none of the groups', 'In exactly two groups', 'A', 'The centre where all three circles overlap holds elements belonging to every set.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'Pen, Pencil and Stationery are best shown as:', 'Pen and Pencil as separate circles inside Stationery', 'Three separate circles', 'Stationery inside Pen', 'Pen inside Pencil', 'A', 'Pens and pencils are distinct items of stationery, so both lie separately inside it.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-venn-diagrams', 'Two circles that do not touch at all represent groups with:', 'No common elements', 'All elements common', 'Some common elements', 'One inside the other', 'A', 'Non-touching (disjoint) circles indicate the groups share no elements.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q01', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A standard die has how many faces?', '6', '4', '8', '12', 'A', 'A die is a cube with 6 numbered faces.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q02', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'On a standard die, the numbers on opposite faces add up to:', '7', '6', '8', '5', 'A', 'Opposite faces of a standard die always sum to 7 (1-6, 2-5, 3-4).', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q03', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'If 1 is opposite 6 on a standard die, then 2 is opposite:', '5', '4', '3', '6', 'A', 'Opposite faces sum to 7, so 2 is opposite 5.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q04', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A cube has how many edges?', '12', '8', '6', '4', 'A', 'A cube has 12 edges, 6 faces and 8 vertices.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q05', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A cube has how many corners (vertices)?', '8', '6', '12', '4', 'A', 'A cube has 8 corners.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q06', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'How many faces of a cube meet at each corner?', '3', '2', '4', '6', 'A', 'Three faces meet at every corner of a cube.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q07', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A painted cube is cut into 27 identical small cubes (3×3×3). How many have no face painted?', '1', '8', '6', '12', 'A', 'Only the single hidden interior cube of a 3×3×3 has no painted face.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q08', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'In a painted 3×3×3 cube, how many small cubes have exactly three faces painted?', '8', '12', '6', '1', 'A', 'The 8 corner cubes each show three painted faces.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q09', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A cube cut into 3 equal parts along each dimension gives how many small cubes?', '27', '9', '18', '12', 'A', '3 × 3 × 3 = 27 small cubes.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q10', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'The sum of all the numbers on a standard die (1 to 6) is:', '21', '18', '24', '20', 'A', '1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 21.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q11', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'In a painted 3×3×3 cube, how many small cubes have exactly one face painted?', '6', '8', '12', '1', 'A', 'The centre cube of each of the 6 faces has exactly one painted face.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes-q12', 'ssc-cgl-reasoning-dice-cubes', 'A cube has how many faces?', '6', '8', '12', '4', 'A', 'A cube has 6 square faces.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q01', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'In a para-jumble question, the sentences must be arranged into a:', 'Coherent, logical paragraph', 'Reverse-alphabetical list', 'Random order', 'Set of questions', 'A', 'The goal is to reorder the sentences so the paragraph reads logically.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q02', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'The opening sentence of a paragraph is usually:', 'Independent and introduces the topic', 'Beginning with ''however''', 'Beginning with a pronoun', 'A conclusion', 'A', 'The first sentence stands alone and introduces the subject, without back-referring words.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q03', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'A sentence beginning with the pronoun ''it'' or ''they'' most likely comes:', 'After the sentence naming the noun it refers to', 'First in the paragraph', 'Independently anywhere', 'As the opening line', 'A', 'A pronoun needs an earlier antecedent, so its sentence follows the one that introduces the noun.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q04', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'Words like ''however'', ''therefore'' and ''moreover'' are called:', 'Transition (connecting) words', 'Nouns', 'Prepositions', 'Interjections', 'A', 'Transition words link ideas and signal how sentences relate.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q05', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'The concluding sentence of a paragraph typically:', 'Summarises or gives the result', 'Introduces a new topic', 'Starts with ''firstly''', 'Contains no verb', 'A', 'The final sentence usually wraps up or concludes the idea.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q06', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'The most reliable last step in solving a para jumble is to:', 'Read the arranged order end-to-end for flow', 'Count the words', 'Ignore the connectors', 'Reverse the order', 'A', 'Reading the final sequence checks that it flows logically and coherently.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q07', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'Arrange logically: (P) He switched off the lights. (Q) He felt sleepy. (R) He went to bed.', 'Q, P, R', 'R, P, Q', 'P, R, Q', 'R, Q, P', 'A', 'He felt sleepy, then switched off the lights, then went to bed — Q, P, R.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q08', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'The word ''finally'' in a sentence usually signals that it belongs:', 'Near the end of the paragraph', 'At the very beginning', 'In the middle only', 'Nowhere', 'A', '''Finally'' marks a concluding or last point, placing the sentence toward the end.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'Arrange logically: (P) It grew into a tree. (Q) He planted a seed. (R) The seed sprouted.', 'Q, R, P', 'P, Q, R', 'R, Q, P', 'Q, P, R', 'A', 'He planted a seed, it sprouted, then grew into a tree — Q, R, P.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'Chronological clues (first, then, next, later) help decide the sentences'':', 'Order', 'Spelling', 'Tense only', 'Length', 'A', 'Time-sequence words indicate the correct order of events.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'A sentence that gives background/definition of the main subject usually appears:', 'Early in the paragraph', 'As the conclusion', 'Never', 'Only last', 'A', 'Introductory background about the topic typically comes near the start.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-para-jumbles', 'Arrange logically: (P) So she took an umbrella. (Q) It was raining heavily. (R) She reached office dry.', 'Q, P, R', 'P, Q, R', 'R, Q, P', 'Q, R, P', 'A', 'It was raining, so she took an umbrella, and reached office dry — Q, P, R.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q01', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'Direct speech is marked by the use of:', 'Quotation marks', 'Brackets', 'Hyphens', 'No punctuation', 'A', 'Direct speech quotes the exact words within quotation marks.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q02', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'Indirect form of: He said, "I am happy."', 'He said that he was happy.', 'He said that he is happy.', 'He says he was happy.', 'He said I am happy.', 'A', 'Present tense shifts to past and ''I'' becomes ''he'': He said that he was happy.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q03', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'In indirect speech (past reporting verb), present tense usually changes to:', 'Past tense', 'Future tense', 'No change', 'Present perfect', 'A', 'With a past reporting verb, the reported present tense moves one step back to past.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q04', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'In indirect speech, ''now'' changes to:', 'then', 'here', 'today', 'soon', 'A', '''Now'' becomes ''then'' when converting to reported speech.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q05', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'In indirect speech, ''today'' changes to:', 'that day', 'this day', 'next day', 'yesterday', 'A', '''Today'' becomes ''that day'' in reported speech.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q06', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'Indirect form of: He said, "I will go."', 'He said that he would go.', 'He said that he will go.', 'He said he go.', 'He said I will go.', 'A', '''Will'' changes to ''would'': He said that he would go.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q07', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'In indirect speech, ''this'' generally changes to:', 'that', 'these', 'those', 'here', 'A', '''This'' becomes ''that'' in reported speech.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q08', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'A reported (indirect) question is usually introduced by ''if/whether'' or a:', 'Wh-word (what, where, why…)', 'Full stop', 'Comma only', 'Quotation mark', 'A', 'Yes-no questions use if/whether; others keep their wh-word, in statement order.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'In indirect speech, ''here'' changes to:', 'there', 'near', 'then', 'that', 'A', '''Here'' becomes ''there'' in reported speech.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q10', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'Commands and requests in indirect speech use verbs like:', 'told / ordered / requested … to', 'said that', 'asked if', 'exclaimed that', 'A', 'Imperatives are reported with told/ordered/requested + ''to'' + verb.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q11', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'If the reporting verb is in the present tense (e.g., ''He says''), the reported tense:', 'Does not change', 'Always becomes past', 'Becomes future', 'Is removed', 'A', 'With a present reporting verb, the tense of the reported words stays the same.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-narration-q12', 'ssc-cgl-english-narration', 'Indirect form of: She said, "I am reading a book."', 'She said that she was reading a book.', 'She said that she is reading a book.', 'She says she was reading a book.', 'She said I am reading a book.', 'A', 'Present continuous shifts to past continuous and ''I'' to ''she''.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q01', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Fill in: ''She is fond ___ music.''', 'of', 'for', 'with', 'to', 'A', 'The correct phrase is ''fond of''.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q02', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Fill in: ''He succeeded ___ his examination.''', 'in', 'at', 'on', 'for', 'A', 'One succeeds ''in'' something.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q03', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Choose the synonym of ''HAPPY'':', 'Joyful', 'Sad', 'Angry', 'Tired', 'A', '''Joyful'' means the same as ''happy''.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q04', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Choose the antonym of ''BIG'':', 'Small', 'Large', 'Huge', 'Wide', 'A', '''Small'' is the opposite of ''big''.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q05', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Fill in: ''The sun rises ___ the east.''', 'in', 'on', 'at', 'from', 'A', 'The idiom is ''rises in the east''.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q06', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'One word for ''a doctor who treats teeth'':', 'Dentist', 'Surgeon', 'Physician', 'Optician', 'A', 'A dentist specialises in teeth.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q07', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Fill in: ''He is angry ___ me.''', 'with', 'on', 'at', 'for', 'A', 'One is angry ''with'' a person.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q08', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Choose the synonym of ''QUICK'':', 'Fast', 'Slow', 'Late', 'Heavy', 'A', '''Fast'' is a synonym of ''quick''.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks-q09', 'ssc-cgl-english-fill-blanks', 'Fill in: ''I have been waiting ___ an hour.''', 'for', 'since', 'from', 'at', 'A', 'Use ''for'' with a period of time (an hour).', 8),
