  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-physics-gk-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-physics-gk', 'The lens used to correct short-sightedness (myopia) is:', 'Concave', 'Convex', 'Bifocal', 'Cylindrical', 'A', 'Myopia is corrected with a concave (diverging) lens.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-physics-gk-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-physics-gk', 'The force that pulls objects toward the centre of the Earth is:', 'Gravity', 'Friction', 'Magnetism', 'Tension', 'A', 'Gravity is the attractive force pulling objects toward the Earth.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q01', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The chemical symbol for gold is:', 'Au', 'Ag', 'Gd', 'Go', 'A', 'Gold''s symbol is Au, from the Latin ''aurum''.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q02', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The chemical symbol for sodium is:', 'Na', 'So', 'Sd', 'S', 'A', 'Sodium''s symbol is Na, from the Latin ''natrium''.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q03', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The most abundant gas in the Earth''s atmosphere is:', 'Nitrogen', 'Oxygen', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Hydrogen', 'A', 'Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the atmosphere.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q04', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The gas essential for human respiration is:', 'Oxygen', 'Nitrogen', 'Helium', 'Argon', 'A', 'Oxygen is required for respiration.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q05', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The pH of a neutral solution is:', '7', '0', '14', '1', 'A', 'A neutral solution (like pure water) has a pH of 7.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q06', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'Common salt is chemically known as:', 'Sodium chloride', 'Calcium carbonate', 'Sodium bicarbonate', 'Potassium chloride', 'A', 'Common table salt is sodium chloride (NaCl).', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q07', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The lightest element in the periodic table is:', 'Hydrogen', 'Helium', 'Lithium', 'Oxygen', 'A', 'Hydrogen is the lightest and simplest element.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q08', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The chemical formula of water is:', 'H₂O', 'CO₂', 'O₂', 'H₂O₂', 'A', 'Water is H₂O — two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'Rusting of iron requires oxygen and:', 'Water (moisture)', 'Nitrogen', 'Carbon', 'Salt only', 'A', 'Iron rusts in the presence of both oxygen and moisture.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The lighter-than-air gas commonly used to fill balloons is:', 'Helium', 'Oxygen', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Chlorine', 'A', 'Helium is lighter than air and non-flammable, so it is used in balloons.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'The hardest naturally occurring substance is:', 'Diamond', 'Iron', 'Gold', 'Quartz', 'A', 'Diamond, a form of carbon, is the hardest natural substance.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-chemistry-gk', 'Acids turn blue litmus paper:', 'Red', 'Blue', 'Green', 'Yellow', 'A', 'Acids turn blue litmus red; bases turn red litmus blue.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q01', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The ''powerhouse of the cell'' is the:', 'Mitochondria', 'Nucleus', 'Ribosome', 'Golgi body', 'A', 'Mitochondria produce ATP energy and are called the powerhouse of the cell.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q02', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The number of bones in the adult human body is:', '206', '201', '212', '198', 'A', 'An adult human skeleton has 206 bones.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q03', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The largest organ of the human body is the:', 'Skin', 'Liver', 'Heart', 'Brain', 'A', 'The skin is the body''s largest organ.', 2),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q04', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The red colour of blood is due to:', 'Haemoglobin', 'Plasma', 'Platelets', 'Melanin', 'A', 'Haemoglobin, the iron-containing pigment in red blood cells, gives blood its red colour.', 3),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q05', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The organ that pumps blood throughout the body is the:', 'Heart', 'Lung', 'Liver', 'Kidney', 'A', 'The heart pumps blood around the circulatory system.', 4),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q06', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'Insulin is produced by the:', 'Pancreas', 'Liver', 'Kidney', 'Thyroid', 'A', 'The pancreas secretes insulin, which regulates blood sugar.', 5),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q07', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The functional unit of the kidney is the:', 'Nephron', 'Neuron', 'Alveolus', 'Villus', 'A', 'The nephron is the kidney''s basic filtering unit.', 6),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q08', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'A human has how many pairs of chromosomes?', '23', '22', '46', '24', 'A', 'Humans have 23 pairs (46 total) of chromosomes.', 7),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q09', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'Deficiency of vitamin C causes:', 'Scurvy', 'Rickets', 'Night blindness', 'Goitre', 'A', 'A lack of vitamin C leads to scurvy.', 8),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q10', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The ''master gland'' of the human body is the:', 'Pituitary gland', 'Thyroid gland', 'Adrenal gland', 'Pancreas', 'A', 'The pituitary gland controls other endocrine glands, so it is called the master gland.', 9),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q11', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'The largest gland in the human body is the:', 'Liver', 'Pancreas', 'Thyroid', 'Salivary gland', 'A', 'The liver is the largest gland (and largest internal organ) in the body.', 10),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk-q12', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-biology-gk', 'During photosynthesis, green plants release:', 'Oxygen', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Nitrogen', 'Hydrogen', 'A', 'Plants take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen during photosynthesis.', 11),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes-q01', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes', 'The Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana is aimed at:', 'Financial inclusion (bank accounts for all)', 'Rural roads', 'Crop insurance', 'Space research', 'A', 'Jan Dhan Yojana provides banking access to unbanked citizens — financial inclusion.', 0),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes-q02', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission is related to:', 'Cleanliness and sanitation', 'Digital payments', 'Skill training', 'Defence', 'A', 'The Swachh Bharat Mission promotes sanitation and cleanliness.', 1),
  ('ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes-q03', 'ssc-cgl-general-awareness-current-affairs-schemes', '''Beti Bachao Beti Padhao'' focuses on:', 'Welfare and education of the girl child', 'Farmer loans', 'Urban housing', 'Tourism', 'A', 'The scheme aims to save and educate the girl child.', 2),
