  ('frm-quantitative-analysis-volatility-ewma-garch-q14', 'frm-quantitative-analysis-volatility-ewma-garch', 'In EWMA, a higher decay factor λ means volatility reacts:', 'More slowly to new shocks', 'Instantly', 'Randomly', 'Never', 'A', 'A larger λ puts more weight on the past, so volatility responds more slowly.', 13),
